{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest","id":501069,"title":"Second Edition Fairest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-02T18:19:46-07:00","id":501069,"title":"Second Edition Fairest","content":"Just dropped them in the blog. Here's the thread to discuss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:22:55-07:00","id":501088,"title":"","content":"Squeee! Can hardly wait for Ogres to come out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:23:54-07:00","id":501091,"title":"","content":"My plan is to put all of them public by the end of this coming week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:33:52-07:00","id":501111,"title":"","content":"So the Fairest are about accepting responsibility. They're basically the flip side of Darklings, then. I really wasn't expecting them to go this route but I think its an interesting direction for them to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:39:45-07:00","id":501122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501111#post501111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Fairest are about accepting responsibility. They're basically the flip side of Darklings, then. I really wasn't expecting them to go this route but I think its an interesting direction for them to go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So I guess <i>most</i> Disney princesses aren't Fairests after all, having their rewards handed to them on a silver, gleaming platter with little work on their part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:42:07-07:00","id":501125,"title":"","content":"So, immediate clarifying question: if the Fairest's &quot;call as the leader&quot; is &quot;go hurt that dude&quot;, is that a Clarity break? In other words, is the Curse supposed to apply only to accidents and other unforeseen collateral damage, or does it apply even when such consequences are intentional and deliberate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:52:39-07:00","id":501172,"title":"","content":"Very different than what I predicted, but still very cool! I'm not quite sure I totally grok it yet, but generally I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:55:54-07:00","id":501177,"title":"","content":"Thats a dramtic change of direction for the fairest.<br /> No longer just a pretty face right enough.<br /> Never been too keen on having a fifth of the characters loosely classed as &quot;Leaders&quot; though.<br /> Tends to result in players feeling that they Have to take charge and buy up social abilities or that most of the seasonal monarchs should be fairest in the setting.<br /> Perhaps something more along the lines of the fairest being shining paragons excelling at whatever they focus on?<br /> The fairest leader is the most convincing on public speakers who turns hearts with honeyed words.<br /> The fairest fighter is a elegent duelest who wields his blade with elegence and grace.<br /> The fairest thief is the cat burglar who steals the most heavily guarded item in the musuem and leaves a calling card too boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5851-ceycil","name":"Ceycil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:05:42-07:00","id":501200,"title":"","content":"I was expecting something darker, its a bit too bright and shiny for the horror genre. They seem to goody too shoes. Arrogance could be highlighted more. Both Darklings and Beasts have a element of the disturbing to them, of the tramatic, Fairests, while Fairest do seem to have a history of waste portential, they don't seem to have an edge to them. Perhaps the corruption angle could be expanded upon.<br /> <br /> Also is the anagonistic vibe between Fairest and Darklings intended? Its pretty obvious the two Seemings will likely butt heads alot. <br /> <br /> The obvious Fairest to me isn't what I expected, I was expecting someone pretty, instead its Chuck Bartawski from the chuck, series, it describes him almost perfectly.<br /> <br /> Its not bad, it could just use a Darker tone, Fairest are just to nice, too obviously the Good Guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:12:42-07:00","id":501208,"title":"","content":"Btw if anyone else finds it hard to find the blog post like I did, just use the Darkling link, and then replace the word Darkling with Fairest in the address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:13:19-07:00","id":501210,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;seriously hurt&quot; part of the Curse should specify that it covers anyone you lead, not everyone everywhere. For the reasons that Errol brought up.<br /> <br /> Also, I really feel like the Blessing has to be clarified; I had issues parsing what it was supposed to trigger off of (muddling your way through a leadership situation), but I dunno, maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> Also, much like Charlequin, this is different than I expected; I also share the &quot;iffy&quot; on them being classed as leaders, with their Blessing and Curse triggering off being a leader, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:13:50-07:00","id":501211,"title":"","content":"See, I don't see Darklings and Fairest as opposites. They are both very focused on getting things done, they just have different foci. A Fairest thinks that it is important for someone to be in charge and lead. They are all about stepping up. Even if they are unqualified or don't know what to do, that isn't important. They just need to seem to be qualified, seem to know what to do. The rest is details you work out as you go. Darklings, on the other hand, believe that shit gets done because of the people willing to do what other people aren't. It's all about the guy who can pull the trigger, who can make the tough call. Who is in charge isn't really important if they can't make the tough calls.<br /> <br /> I easily see both working together. The Fairest is the &quot;face&quot;, the one who rallies the troops and inspires them, regardless of what lies he has to tell to do so. The Darkling is the one in the shadows, doing the shit that needs doing. Walsingham to Elizabeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:15:18-07:00","id":501213,"title":"","content":"Hey, that came out of no where!<br /> <br /> Can't wait to look it over-though I was really hoping for the Elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:21:57-07:00","id":501218,"title":"","content":"Nyrufa, I think you need to recheck the Disney canon princess list. Snow White is directly referenced in the blog post. Cinderella and Aurora don't qualify, but Aurora and Phillip are barely characters; Sleeping Beauty is basically about the godmothers and Maleficent. And, yes, Cinderella's kind of a twit. Ariel pays a horrible price for just the chance to join the human world and seek the man of her dreams. She certainly works for her dream. Belle civilizes and tames the Beast, teaching him to love others; she qualifies as a Fairest candidate. Jasmine actively works to aid her man. Maybe she's not Fairest, but she sure works for what she gets. Pocahontas, have you even watched the film? It's a long way from historically accurate, but Pocahontas is very much a take-charge sort. She averts a war, for pity's sake! Mulan, again, go watch the film and tell me she just gets things handed to her. And she's definitely a leader type. She took control of her squad to take down the lead villain and save the Emperor. Tiana's absolutely the leader between herself and Prince Naveen. Rapunzel isn't a leader type, that's certain, but she certainly goes through her share of tribulations on the way to regaining her birthright. Merida? She nearly causes a full-blown war, then gets her mother changed into a bear, then has to clean up the mess she's made, and by the end of everything, she's still only a princess, albeit one with a better family situation. Though the way she takes charge near the end of film would suit a Fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:22:46-07:00","id":501220,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is pretty different than what I was expecting. It's still awesome, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:26:25-07:00","id":501223,"title":"","content":"Good point. Chuck's (Fairest) to Sarah Walker's (Darkling) (abit a very pretty Darkling). I still think Fairest could be Darker, this is the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:28:36-07:00","id":501225,"title":"","content":"Well, this paradigm is not what I was expecting for the Fairest, but it's definitely an interesting one.<br /> <br /> They... actually kind of remind me of Captain America's character, in the nature of their choice. Except with the burden of leadership added on. Hilariously I came back from Avengers 2 tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-02-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:29:15-07:00","id":501226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501200#post501200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting something darker, its a bit too bright and shiny for the horror genre. They seem to goody too shoes. Arrogance could be highlighted more. Both Darklings and Beasts have a element of the disturbing to them, of the tramatic, Fairests, while Fairest do seem to have a history of waste portential, they don't seem to have an edge to them. Perhaps the corruption angle could be expanded upon.<br /> <br /> Also is the anagonistic vibe between Fairest and Darklings intended? Its pretty obvious the two Seemings will likely butt heads alot.<br /> <br /> The obvious Fairest to me isn't what I expected, I was expecting someone pretty, instead its Chuck Bartawski from the chuck, series, it describes him almost perfectly.<br /> <br /> Its not bad, it could just use a Darker tone, Fairest are just to nice, too obviously the Good Guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Like the others, Fairest function as a reaction to trauma. In this case they've got a martyr-complex and absolutely have to shoulder the burdens of everyone. Think of older siblings in dysfunctional households who take on the responsibilities of a parent at extremely young ages. It's about taking on <i>everything</i> because you are (or maybe you just <i>think</i> you are) the only one who can.<br /> <br /> Basically, every Fairest is going to go gray in like five years and it owns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501211#post501211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't see Darklings and Fairest as opposites.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're totally opposites. Darklings forsake others and are responsible for only themselves. Fairest forsake themselves and are responsible for <i>everyone</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","user":"Illuminated Minutia","date":". 05-02-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:30:34-07:00","id":501227,"title":"","content":"Cinderella, at least in the Disney animated version, certainly filled this role for the mice. More impressive when you think of the house as being <i>really</i> divorced from the rest of normal civilization.<br /> <br /> Still reading, so I might be missing some notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:35:15-07:00","id":501231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501211#post501211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't see Darklings and Fairest as opposites. They are both very focused on getting things done, they just have different foci. A Fairest thinks that it is important for someone to be in charge and lead. They are all about stepping up. Even if they are unqualified or don't know what to do, that isn't important. They just need to seem to be qualified, seem to know what to do. The rest is details you work out as you go. Darklings, on the other hand, believe that shit gets done because of the people willing to do what other people aren't. It's all about the guy who can pull the trigger, who can make the tough call. Who is in charge isn't really important if they can't make the tough calls.<br /> <br /> I easily see both working together. The Fairest is the &amp;quot;face&amp;quot;, the one who rallies the troops and inspires them, regardless of what lies he has to tell to do so. The Darkling is the one in the shadows, doing the shit that needs doing. Walsingham to Elizabeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone else read this and think of Rick vs. Shane in the first couple seasons of Walking Dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:35:19-07:00","id":501232,"title":"","content":"True, I hadn't thought of that aspect. It's been a long time since I last saw the film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:39:06-07:00","id":501235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501227#post501227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cinderella, at least in the Disney animated version, certainly filled this role for the mice. More impressive when you think of the house as being <i>really</i> divorced from the rest of normal civilization.<br /> <br /> Still reading, so I might be missing some notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>New version is probably a little better, if she doesn't qualify as someone else (her big break came when she proved unbreakable and unwilling to compromise, since compromise would mean still allowing her agency to be decided by someone else).<br /> <br /> Also, makes sense that the Fairest is, in fact, the prince, and the prince is defined by being a leader...and leadership can be really, really dark at times. My only criticism is that the martyr complex of Fairest should be a bit more blatant, as should be self-doubt (self-loathing is, by the looks of it, a Fairest's trauma button). Make it clear they aren't more stable than all their contemporaries, even if it's manifested as a desperate charisma.<br /> <br /> <i>That being said, </i>I now want to play a Fairest, who up until now were my personal whipping boys. Very, <i>very </i>good job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:40:48-07:00","id":501238,"title":"","content":"Darklings don't trust others, they haven't forsaken others and may in fact be drawn to those who have been forsaken. And in fact the Darkling's blessing only functions on behalf of someone else, on behalf of another character.<br /> <br /> I just realized the Character most likely to come into conflict with a Fairest is another Fairest. A Motley of only Fairest is potentially a disaster in the making, too many Chiefs, not enough Indians as the saying goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:44:11-07:00","id":501244,"title":"","content":"Oh exalted hero, oh great princess,<br /> how pure is the virtue that brightens your face;<br /> how noble is the spirit that lifts your peers?<br /> You walk lightly on the glass,<br /> and sing the songs for the weak.<br /> They'll need you always, their fairest of all.<br /> <br /> Oh miserable knight, oh wretched maiden,<br /> how vile is the poison that darkens your heart;<br /> how bitter is the curse that haunts your mirrors?<br /> You bleed heavily from the glass,<br /> and choke the song for yourself.<br /> They'll need you always, their fairest of all.<br /> <br /> It's not how I would have done it, but I can dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2015, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:13:28-07:00","id":501263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501244#post501244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh exalted hero, oh great princess,<br /> how pure is the virtue that brightens your face;<br /> how noble is the spirit that lifts your peers?<br /> You walk lightly on the glass,<br /> and sing the songs for the weak.<br /> They'll need you always, their fairest of all.<br /> <br /> Oh miserable knight, oh wretched maiden,<br /> how vile is the poison that darkens your heart;<br /> how bitter is the curse that haunts your mirrors?<br /> You bleed heavily from the glass,<br /> and choke the song for yourself.<br /> They'll need you always, their fairest of all.<br /> <br /> It's not how I would have done it, but I can dig it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That from somewhere?<br /> <br /> Also, I will not be surprised if the Darkling stereotype of the Fairest, or vice versa, is some variation of &quot;...I understand.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:16:31-07:00","id":501265,"title":"","content":"In the sense that my mind is a dark ocean, yes.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Fairest have got it rough. I don't have the Shadow/Jesus dialogue with me right now, but that entire exchange in sitting pretty in my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:21:09-07:00","id":501268,"title":"","content":"Actually, something Lubaf on RPGnet brought up:<br /> <br /> Blessing is a bit vague, we need to know what &quot;feeling your way&quot; through is in plain English, and we need to know if Fairest are okay with handing off leadership, if only temporarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:23:55-07:00","id":501270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501125#post501125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, immediate clarifying question: if the Fairest's &quot;call as the leader&quot; is &quot;go hurt that dude&quot;, is that a Clarity break? In other words, is the Curse supposed to apply only to accidents and other unforeseen collateral damage, or does it apply even when such consequences are intentional and deliberate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm going to say unintentional is what causes a breaking point. You're the leader, everybody looks to you to guide them to victory. So when your orders fuck up and things go south, it's not a very good feeling as a Fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> This means that as a Fairest, players are going to have to be very strategic and plan out their actions, lest the Story Teller pull a whammy on them. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:32:12-07:00","id":501291,"title":"","content":"I'm really noticed that the seemings all seem to correspond with different responses to abuse. Beasts become rebellious of anything resembling authority, Darklings have trust issues, and now Fairest have a martyr complex feeling and that they have to save everyone.<br /> <br /> I can only wonder what the rest will end up looking like (I'm betting that Elementals become withdrawn though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:33:55-07:00","id":501292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501270#post501270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to say unintentional is what causes a breaking point. You're the leader, everybody looks to you to guide them to victory. So when your orders fuck up and things go south, it's not a very good feeling as a Fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> This means that as a Fairest, players are going to have to be very strategic and plan out their actions, lest the Story Teller pull a whammy on them. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Which creates some great tension with the fact that their Blessing rewards them with Clarity for taking the lead when they don't actually have a plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:38:34-07:00","id":501304,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all your comments. I'm getting some thoughts here. I will remind you this is a very first draft draft, and clearly, I need to tighten up some of the language. So here's some thoughts and comments and questions answered. Ready? Here we go! <br /> <br /> 1)Someone asked if the Clarity check is for when you make hard choices and people get hurt or also when you're 'job' makes you punch a dude, and they get hurt. I can clarify that. It is in fact when the damage is splash-over or accidentally. It's meant to be about collateral damage, not about 'I need to punch a guy because that guy needs to be punched.' It's meant to be, &quot;I punched a guy because he needed to be punched, and then he died, and now his widow can't support her family any more.&quot; This plays into the idea that ever if you're a good leader (which not all Fairest are) the choices you make, even perfectly legit choices, are going to have consequence. And for the tragic Fairest, that eats at you. See, the Fairest didn't ask to be a leader, didn't ask for people to look up to them, but they kinda have to do it. And even though they generally don't 'sign up for it' so to speak, it still eats at them and slowly kills them that they fuck up even when they don't fuck up. That's the tragedy of the Fairest. And the horror. No matter what you do, even as you do your best, you can never be as perfect as everyone thinks you are, and that could just break you into a million pieces one day. If you know the play, ask yourself, what did Lear look like before he was old and established? King Lear is a place where Fairest can end up, easily, and plenty of them KNOW that, and maybe, can't do shit to stop it.<br /> <br /> 2)I see some comments about 'horror' and 'this isn't dark enough.' Well. Horror comes in many shades and genre. Changeling the Lost is, at it's core, psychological horror. Horror in your head and your gut, not horror that jumps out of the corner and screams at you. So. Sometimes the scary is more cerebral. See above. And below probably.<br /> <br /> 3)I see some discussion about Disney Princesses. First, full disclosure,I have STRONG opinions about Princesses. They are highly problimatic and yet incredibly important, and that they can do as much good as they do harm, culturally speaking. And actually, that's kind of the Fairest too, isn't it? They CAN do a lot good, but will they? I also saw someone saying basically 'Disney Princesses can't be Fairest because they had everything just handed to them.&quot; Actually, that's exactly why they would be Fairest. Each Fairest made a choice to step up, to stand up, to help someone, and that let them escape. But they didn't sign up for the long-haul, you understand. It's thrust on them. Imagine if you saved a guy from being hit by a car one day. Nice feelings, yay! You made a really good self sacrificing choice! Cool! Now the dude is living on your front doorstep, waiting for you to come out, asking you what to do with his life, begging you to take care of him, advise him, and worse, his friends are joining in. If you're not careful, there's going to a cult around you in no time. And just imagine how that cult is going to react when they find out that you only saved the guy because you were trying to steal his wallet. Whoopse. Higher the pedestal, the harder the fall. (You see this in the treatment of famous people ALL THE TIME!) To bring it back to the Princesses, because I can't resist them... Imagine Cinderella. She's spent most of her life now, abused by her stepmother, all of her skills involve house cleaning and management. She can mend clothes. That was good enough. Now (because she saved some mice, basically) she's a queen of an entire kingdom and married to a man she doesn't really know. A pure heart, or at least, a moment of purity put her in this position. What if she can't hack it? What if she turns around and abuses her staff the way she was abused, because she has no idea how to communicate with employees except the abuse she learned? What if the rush passes and she realizes her Prince Charming is a jerk for XYZ reason, and or she simply can't connect with him? What will the people of her fair kingdom do when she's caught in an affair with a stable hand because, frankly, she can emotionally connect with him better? What if she's asked to make an important domestic choice for the kingdom, and the result hurts everyone? Mice-workers right SOUNDED good, but it's crushed the local economy because she doesn't have the know-how to transition the kingdom from a domestic-slavery culture to something more fair? <br /> <br /> 4)On a smaller, more intimate level, the big brother who takes the abuse so that drunk dad can't murder mom and little sister? Who ever tagged this idea? Yeah. Hard, but, yeah, that's actually the deeper undertone I was going for. If you want to take it to this level, which is smaller and harder, you look at the Fairest like this. You take the beatings so dad doesn't murder mom. Every day you ask yourself, though, would mom have left if you weren't taking the heat? Would mom and everyone leave if little sister got popped the way you do, even once? (How unfair would that be, huh?) Little sister is kind of turning into a monster, she's hurting small animals, is that your fault too? Why doesn't anyone ever fucking THANK you for the beatings you take? Would everyone be better off if you just murdered dad? Who would you be if you killed him? Maybe you should just leave, let them sort their own shit out! But. You won't do that. You can't do any of that, because they need you, they don't thank you, but they need you, and know it. <br /> <br /> 5)Darklings and Fairest are opposite, but not enemies. In fact, they should work in a fucked up sort of harmony most of the time. In the example in number 4? Yeah. The Darkling there might be little sister. Big brother can't do the deed, the deed that needs to be done, and so, one day, Darkling little sister will creep into dad's room when he's out cold, and put something in his drink. She knows big brother may have to hate her for it, but she does it anyway. Big brother will do the right thing, probably, though, and take credit for the killing, going to prison, but the end result is actually the right one. Mom is free of dad, and little sister slips off through the cracks, and big brother gets to be the big hero. The fairytale ending, right?<br /> <br /> 6} Someone wanted Elementals next. I can nudge that to happen next. No problem. For a taste? Have you seen the movie Party Monster? Or know the story of Michael Alig? Look it up if not. That's a place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/184-filamena","name":"Filamena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar184_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:38:54-07:00","id":501305,"title":"","content":"Clarity is starting to confuse me, a little.<br /> <br /> Is it supposed to suggest healthy behaviors, or behaviors that declare that one's independence from Faerie? Because if, say, Darklings are mechanically incapable of putting their trust in others without setting up countermeasures, that's definitely <i>in line with the strategy of betrayal of principle and constant vigilance</i>, but also definitely not a healthy behavior.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Fairest seem like their strategy is the martyr complex - they gain Clarity when they force their way into the protagonist role for the good of others, when they take the heat, especially when their methods are dubious in doing so, and I don't think that's <i>healthy </i>but it is definitely princely.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm getting a &quot;all Fairest are leaders&quot; vibe. Is &quot;the farmhand of noble ancestry who quests, alone, to earn the hand of the princess&quot; no longer a viable concept? I mean, the story only follows the farmhand while he's on the quest - it's not about what he does with the half-kingdom he inherits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 05-02-2015, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:44:52-07:00","id":501307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501218#post501218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nyrufa, I think you need to recheck the Disney canon princess list. Snow White is directly referenced in the blog post. Cinderella and Aurora don't qualify, but Aurora and Phillip are barely characters; Sleeping Beauty is basically about the godmothers and Maleficent. And, yes, Cinderella's kind of a twit. Ariel pays a horrible price for just the chance to join the human world and seek the man of her dreams. She certainly works for her dream. Belle civilizes and tames the Beast, teaching him to love others; she qualifies as a Fairest candidate. Jasmine actively works to aid her man. Maybe she's not Fairest, but she sure works for what she gets. Pocahontas, have you even watched the film? It's a long way from historically accurate, but Pocahontas is very much a take-charge sort. She averts a war, for pity's sake! Mulan, again, go watch the film and tell me she just gets things handed to her. And she's definitely a leader type. She took control of her squad to take down the lead villain and save the Emperor. Tiana's absolutely the leader between herself and Prince Naveen. Rapunzel isn't a leader type, that's certain, but she certainly goes through her share of tribulations on the way to regaining her birthright. Merida? She nearly causes a full-blown war, then gets her mother changed into a bear, then has to clean up the mess she's made, and by the end of everything, she's still only a princess, albeit one with a better family situation. Though the way she takes charge near the end of film would suit a Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I put 'most' in italics for a reason, I'm quite aware that there are some princesses who put up a hell of a fight to get what they wanted. However...<br /> <br /> <br /> Aeriel defies her father, goes to visit a Sea Witch, gambles her soul away on a contract she didn't even read (seriously, she has her eyes closed and head turned), and trades her voice for a pair of legs, all so she can be with a man she has never even spoken to before in her life. Now of course the original story has this plan fuck up royal, but in the Disney universe, the hero always wins. So, she tries to back out of her contract, ends up having her father sacrifice his own soul and his kingdom to save her, then has her would be lover kill the seawitch and steal back the trident. Yes, it is stealing because these were binding contracts that she willingly signed. And despite all rational logic, the man who she only met 3 days ago SOMEHOW decides he truly loves her.<br /> <br /> Aeriel is a complete and utter brat, and her disney story pretty much says disobey your parents, run off with some guy you barely know, back out of legal wavers, and everything will be A-O-K.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sleeping Beauty didn't do crap. She fell into a coma for several years and a random knight did all the work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Snow White, I'm on the fence about. She taught the Dwarves how to properly take care of themselves, but other than that, she didn't really do much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cinderella isn't a twit, she was constantly abused her whole life. In the end, she seduces the prince with her courtship skills and humiliates her step sisters / mother in public when the prince comes to their house and the slipper fits on her foot. Hell of a way to rise to your potential, which seems to be a theme for Fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, Pocahontas was a 12 year old, and John (that's his name, right?) was a curly haired ginger with a beard, instead of some blond haired Greek God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:47:07-07:00","id":501309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501305#post501305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity is starting to confuse me, a little.<br /> <br /> Is it supposed to suggest healthy behaviors, or behaviors that declare that one's independence from Faerie? Because if, say, Darklings are mechanically incapable of putting their trust in others without setting up countermeasures, that's definitely <i>in line with the strategy of betrayal of principle and constant vigilance</i>, but also definitely not a healthy behavior.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Fairest seem like their strategy is the martyr complex - they gain Clarity when they force their way into the protagonist role for the good of others, when they take the heat, especially when their methods are dubious in doing so, and I don't think that's <i>healthy </i>but it is definitely princely.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm getting a &quot;all Fairest are leaders&quot; vibe. Is &quot;the farmhand of noble ancestry who quests, alone, to earn the hand of the princess&quot; no longer a viable concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blessings, in this case, are like hacks, where the Seeming lets a Changeling benefit from their role even if it isn't 'healthy.' They're tweaked, of course they all are, and here's how being tweaked lets them cope. These aren't great behaviours, exactly, but they're a coping mechanism that just somehow 'works' for the specific Changeling. (And also, it's a way of rewarding a player for playing their Changeling in a thematically appropriate way. It's a carrot-stick kinda thing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/184-filamena","name":"Filamena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar184_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:49:46-07:00","id":501313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501305#post501305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity is starting to confuse me, a little.<br /> <br /> Is it supposed to suggest healthy behaviors, or behaviors that declare that one's independence from Faerie? Because if, say, Darklings are mechanically incapable of putting their trust in others without setting up countermeasures, that's definitely <i>in line with the strategy of betrayal of principle and constant vigilance</i>, but also definitely not a healthy behavior.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Fairest seem like their strategy is the martyr complex - they gain Clarity when they force their way into the protagonist role for the good of others, when they take the heat, especially when their methods are dubious in doing so, and I don't think that's <i>healthy </i>but it is definitely princely.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Seeming Blessings, Clarity is about reasserting one's sense of self-particularly one's sense of self of <i>taking control back</i>. It reasserts that they have the power to make decisions and control their fate via their milestone choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:52:31-07:00","id":501316,"title":"","content":"<i>Guys, I think I've figured it out!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>What if Elementals...</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Are </i><i>apathetic</i><i>?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Think about it, what's one thing that we know about nature? It has a tendency to endure whatever comes its way. A reed can bend without breaking, water can mold to new shapes, but its still water. Rocks can endure centuries of punishment.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>What if becoming an Elemental is deciding that you won't let your Keeper's abuse destroy you? Your Keeper can bend you, but they can not break you! You are like the rock against the wind and rain, and you will weather this terrible storm.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-03-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:58:46-07:00","id":501319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501316#post501316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I think I've figured it out!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What if Elementals...<br /> <br /> <br /> Are <i>apathetic</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> Think about it, what's one thing that we know about nature? It has a tendency to endure whatever comes its way. A reed can bend without breaking, water can mold to new shapes, but its still water. Rocks can endure centuries of punishment.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if becoming an Elemental is deciding that you won't let your Keeper's abuse destroy you? Your Keeper can bend you, but they can not break you! You are like the rock against the wind and rain, and you will weather this terrible storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your brilliant idea has the twin downsides of treading old speculative ground and not actually being a means of reclaiming agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:59:20-07:00","id":501320,"title":"","content":"Apathy is a <i>terrible</i> protagonist trait.<br /> <br /> So no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:01:53-07:00","id":501321,"title":"","content":"My initial guess for Elementals was a kind of Zen denial of the Self, but this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501304#post501304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6} Someone wanted Elementals next. I can nudge that to happen next. No problem. For a taste? Have you seen the movie Party Monster? Or know the story of Michael Alig? Look it up if not. That's a place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is interesting. I'm not entirely sure how you'll tie in the Melendez murder, if that's what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:06:09-07:00","id":501327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501319#post501319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your brilliant idea has the twin downsides of treading old speculative ground and not actually being a means of reclaiming agency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That second part's not quite true. I think it would be a very effective means of reclaiming your agency. It's like staring your keeper straight in the face and saying &quot;Thank you sir, may I have another?&quot; Your Keeper tries to whip you into submission, and you keep standing back up and going on about your business, such as escaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:18:07-07:00","id":501337,"title":"","content":"Without saying too much, no, I'm not really into apathy. Apathy doesn't make for great characters. Nihilism, maybe? But not apathy. (I don't personally do Nihilism either, though, not my bag.)<br /> <br /> I'm starting to think Illuminated is reading my drafts before they get posted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Zen denial of self is actually kind of part of it? Yeah. Party Monster + Zen. It works, I think, when you put it together. I hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/184-filamena","name":"Filamena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar184_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:28:58-07:00","id":501342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501327#post501327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be a very effective means of reclaiming your agency. It's like staring your keeper straight in the face and saying &quot;Thank you sir, may I have another?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what &quot;reclaim&quot; means. That is the shit you pull to show that your agency has not been lost yet. Defiance of the convention of &quot;when you're beaten down, stay down&quot; is more in line with the escape narrative of the Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:40:57-07:00","id":501349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501307#post501307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleeping Beauty didn't do crap. She fell into a coma for several years and a random knight did all the work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen <i>Maleficent</i>? Compared to previous renderings of the fairy tale, it's much better, and Aurora works much better as a Fairest there. Not perfect; she's not the protagonist or anything, but it certainly vaults over the low bar presented by the 1959 movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:42:33-07:00","id":501350,"title":"","content":"Conceptually, I feel like the Fairest write-up as-is is a little narrow - in that there aren't many provisions for a Fairest concept that doesn't involve being in a position of authority of some kind.<br /> <br /> Would &quot;being tested&quot; be compelling to anyone as the thematic idea for Fairest? In fairy tales, the prince is crowned and the princess succeeds because, when they are presented with tests of their morals - for example, &quot;did you drop this golden axe or this silver one or was it this normal one&quot; - or their wits or their humility, they give the right answer, invariably, even where the Gentry would answer wrong. The Fairest treat their Durances, sooner or later, as a test. They prove that they're just as good as their Keepers, if not better, and thus escape by asserting that they are not beneath the Gentry, who come and go as they please, and thus should be afforded the exact same right. They inherit the crown and win the princess's hand, and thus become nobles. In the trauma-and-asserting-agency analogy, they're the ones who say &quot;You think I'm useless? I'll show you. I won't just meet the insane expectations you set, and I won't just exceed them - I'll be <i>better</i> than you are, and I'll do it without borrowing a single page from your playbook.&quot; And it feels so good to be proven, but from then on, every time there's a test, you need to prove you're better than your Keeper all over again...<br /> <br /> (Might give Clarity for pulling out all the stops to win, for the sake of proving something or accomplishing something on behalf of others or out of principle, and cause Clarity issues when you're being tested and you think of yourself, or other people think of you, as having failed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:02:58-07:00","id":501362,"title":"","content":"Fairest are not in in positions of power automatically, they are handed authority. It's kind of a fine point, but it's an important one. People look up to them and expect them to be perfect. That's the soul of it as I'm writing it. <br /> <br /> If you'd like something more specific catered exactly to your tastes, that's cool too. Play it however you like at your table. If you'd like me to write for your specifications, my rate is five cents a word with half upfront and half on delivery of the second draft. Happy to help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/184-filamena","name":"Filamena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar184_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:19:27-07:00","id":501370,"title":"","content":"I don't want to necessarily drag in the Wyrd where plain old psychology works fine, but another recently occured thought to me is that a Seeming isn't just a choice to define yourself, it's a <i>promise</i> made to the Wyrd, a promise to change, to become, to self-transcend into that choice, one that binds very closely so as to rewrite who you are. Akin to Curse's Decrees, sort of.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, it can be read that way-I certainly wouldn't declare that an absolute fact of the setting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If it weren't more fun to write my own takes on the matter, I would almost take you up on that Filamena.<br /> <br /> CLARITY: Which isn't to say I don't love these write-ups. I do, but now you've got the idea of alternative interpretation going on in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-03-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:49:27-07:00","id":501386,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the Fairest are that I really like them! I think they are much more developed than the 'better than thou' haughty elves of 1e, I can see now why a Fairest would be who they are and how they earn the Seeming. I also liked that some could be not so regal and more relateable, laid-back, a person of the people (the quote from Diana, RIP, really sold me into them). I see the Fairest now as even moreso a Seeming that other changelings wish they held. I see conflicts in a motley too of a Fairest being the hero for a would-be Darkling, the Fairest pulling others out of Arcadia with them but for some unfortunate circumstance, the changeling with that unrequited crush on their hero gets left and develops down the path in feeling betrayed to become a Darkling. That in itself makes me actually want to play that Darkling and also see things from the Fairest's POV.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:54:08-07:00","id":501392,"title":"","content":"I would totally play the tag-team of Fairest and Darkling, each one doing what the other can't and teetering on gladness and envy because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:26:17-07:00","id":501432,"title":"","content":"Well, from what I can see this is going to be a controversial opinion. Oh well, here goes nothing! I can't get behind this draft. Almost not at all! That worries me because CtL is my favorite line out of all the White Wolf products. So what's bugging me about this? <br /> <br /> The first issue that jumps out at me is that the writing feels sterile. It feels like I'm reading bullets on a power point slide trying to bash out as much exposition as it can without letting it breath. Plus, there doesn't seem to be anything to draw the reader in. The text just jumps right into talking about the Fairest without giving the reader a chance to get a clear picture in their heads. The first edition gave a short fairy tale attempting to illustrate the overarching concept of the Seemings, and to me those helped not only with understanding the Seemings, but also the tales and the folklore that they sprung from. However, that could be first draft stuff! That kind of flavor could be skipped over in favor of just getting the Seeming concept on paper. Perfectly understandable. <br /> <br /> My second issue is more fundamental. I don't like how the Fairest's core concept has been changed. They went from being the epitome of Faerie's beauty to the Leader Seeming? Why exactly? I've seen it posited that it's to parallel common reactions to abuse, but that rubs me the wrong way. I would rather have my character's reaction to the trauma suffered in Arcadia determined by their personality than by their Seeming. That kind of parallelism is much better suited to the Courts (since I've seen it argued that they are based off the 5 stages of grief(minus one)) because which Court you end up in is your character's choice. This change seems to want to dictate how my character acts and the demons that haunt them, and as a player I want those details to be left up to my imagination. I also agree with the people who expressed their dislike for having a designated Leader Seeming. Not every player who wants to lead will want to play a Fairest, and not every player who wants to play a Fairest will want to lead.<br /> <br /> This is all just my opinion, and it could very well be a bad reaction to change. I'm certainly not going to rain on anyone's parade if they like this conception of the Fairest over another. I just don't see myself enjoying the direction this draft has started out on. Okay falling asleep on my keyboard now. Hopefully there was some useful feedback in that rambling mess!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3343-radiodragon","name":"Radiodragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:34:23-07:00","id":501435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Radiodragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501432#post501432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather have my character's reaction to the trauma suffered in Arcadia determined by their personality than by their Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Your Seeming in the 2e paradigm<i> is their agency-reclaiming response to their experience in Arcadia.</i> This has been common knowledge since <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/\" target=\"_blank\">the Beasts blog entry dropped</a> and was already being talked about well before then.<br /> <br /> Your Seeming is predicated on that reaction. Horse goes before cart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:38:42-07:00","id":501437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Radiodragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501432#post501432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather have my character's reaction to the trauma suffered in Arcadia determined by their personality than by their Seeming. That kind of parallelism is much better suited to the Courts (since I've seen it argued that they are based off the 5 stages of grief(minus one)) because which Court you end up in is your character's choice. This change seems to want to dictate how my character acts and the demons that haunt them, and as a player I want those details to be left up to my imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the core concept of the way Seeming is going to work in 2e: your Seeming <i>is</i> a choice, it'sthe method you <i>chose</i> to escape Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Kith is what was done to you. Seeming is how you escaped. Court is how you continue to cope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:40:38-07:00","id":501438,"title":"","content":"Courts are how others <i>think</i> you should cope. Courtless are alive and well, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:44:49-07:00","id":501440,"title":"","content":"Also, the Seasonal Courts never were, and visibly continue to not be, the entire spectrum of wayward changelings' societal structure, even if the Courts-as-stages-of-grief fanon weren't a shallow read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:45:03-07:00","id":501441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501438#post501438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Courts are how others <i>think</i> you should cope. Courtless are alive and well, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purpose of brevity I folded Courtless into the general concept of Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:00:51-07:00","id":501450,"title":"","content":"I... like it, but on the flip side, am starting to understand a bit more issues people had with the Darklings. <br /> <br /> With that said, I do like the idea, and understand their place. I'm just not as head over heels in love with it as I was with Darklings or Beasts. As for why, they're essentially the Leader archetype. And that just feels more restrictive for some reason than Darklings who, while arguably having a more unified background, wouldn't have a unified skill set, if you will. <br /> <br /> Regardless, eagerly awaiting all of these, and honestly, even if the Fairest was say, the, &quot;worst,&quot; in my viewpoint, it would still be an incredibly awesome list of Seemings.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:10:22-07:00","id":501453,"title":"","content":"So, Fairests 2.0 are Ventrues? Didn't see that coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:18:47-07:00","id":501455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501362#post501362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairest are not in in positions of power automatically, they are handed authority. It's kind of a fine point, but it's an important one. People look up to them and expect them to be perfect. That's the soul of it as I'm writing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. This makes me think of Fairest in subordinate positions, who are still given perhaps unreasonably high standards to meet within their areas, and crushed just as much when their counsel receives deference and results in problems.<br /> <br /> I really like that side (unless I'm off-base &gt;.&gt; ), and agree authority vs. leadership is a really important distinction. I don't think I would have gotten that idea from the current draft (though it has been a long day), and think it might benefit from being given more emphasis, perhaps even explicitly.<br /> <br /> Even without that, I really dig this writeup. ^_^ It's not what I expected, but I love it. Definitely my favorite of the first three by a long shot, and the one I'm likely to play the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:37:34-07:00","id":501462,"title":"","content":"I generally like the change on the Fairest as &quot;those that want to lead&quot;.The only problem I have now is they are a bit too bright. In second draft there should be pointing how &quot;leadership&quot; is taught and your choices made for others can lead to bad things, sometimes. Like <b>Filamena</b> breaks down Disney Princess and consequances of thier fiary tale - the story of the character does not end when she has a crown on their head, it's only begining of their problems. Maybe adding a bit more &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; vibe in the text? You finally are Leader, only it comes with ugly questions and even more ugly answers to them - this would be suitable to the &quot;paragon ideal&quot; in the World of Darkness. Your geneuanly want do good things, but world is not created to sustain this kind idealism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501122#post501122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess <i>most</i> Disney princesses aren't Fairests after all, having their rewards handed to them on a silver, gleaming platter with little work on their part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Original Disney Princess were talked about, but I must say now half of characters in <b>Once Upon a Time</b> TV Show should be now 2ED Fairest. Series is basiclly tale of how &quot;too good wanters&quot; must make tough choices now, after their &quot;fairy tale&quot; has ended. Or does it? Maybe they now challanges and test are the Fairy Tale itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:41:33-07:00","id":501464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501455#post501455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh. This makes me think of Fairest in subordinate positions, who are still given perhaps unreasonably high standards to meet within their areas, and crushed just as much when their counsel receives deference and results in problems.<br /> <br /> I really like that side (unless I'm off-base &gt;.&gt; ), and agree authority vs. leadership is a really important distinction. I don't think I would have gotten that idea from the current draft (though it has been a long day), and think it might benefit from being given more emphasis, perhaps even explicitly.<br /> <br /> Even without that, I really dig this writeup. ^_^ It's not what I expected, but I love it. Definitely my favorite of the first three by a long shot, and the one I'm likely to play the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this does make me view it better, the whole expectations part, so... hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:43:26-07:00","id":501466,"title":"","content":"So the darklings and fairest are flip sides of the same coin. Darklings don't trust anyone for fear of being betrayed, fairest don't trust anyone else not to fuck things up. So the homeless fairest won't just protect the other disenfranchised, they'll (perhaps unkmowingly) keep them away from things that would make them more independent, because people are, in their mind, incapable of running their own lives; otherwise they wouldn't be there, needing the fairest's protection. <br /> <br /> For steven universe fans, Pearl is a good example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:45:17-07:00","id":501467,"title":"","content":"Four pages already? Wow, so here's my thoughts.<br /> <br /> 1) The core concept is absolutely sweet! I love it to bits!<br /> <br /> 2) It has the same issue as Darklings in that the background and durance focus too heavily on one possibility. The &quot;flower who never blossomed&quot;. What about, for example, the charachter who was a genuinely good leader before the Durance. It strikes me that a lot of them could end up as Fariest. For example a military general who was abducted to serve as a domestic servants, but trained the other servants until they could fight their way to freedom? I wouldn't say a general &quot;never blossomed&quot; before his Durance.<br /> <br /> I don't want to get too much into this here because we're having that Discussion over at the Darkling thread and having it in two places would be awkward; but I wanted to note it.<br /> <br /> 3) I concur with what others have been saying. The Curse needs to be clarified. I'd say the clarification must cover you ordering your followers to hurt someone or ordering your followers to get hurt (e.g. get your ten guys with guns to fight their ten guys with guns).<br /> <br /> 4) Filamena, your post on page 3. The bit about Cinderella post wedding and number 4 really should go into the book in some form if it's possible. Heck, I would go so far as to say cut out the Background section entirely and replace it with a section on coping post Durance and fill that section with your Cinderella like ideas because it's far more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:01:39-07:00","id":501486,"title":"","content":"This is an area where I feel like unfulfilled potential is... rather broad. <br /> <br /> I bring this up because I don't quite get your issues here as you had with Darklings which, while I disagree with still somewhat, I understand more where you're coming from. I mean, someone could already be a good leader... and still have wasted potential. <br /> <br /> That, and them being given expectations later fits that. <br /> <br /> The Fairest have warmed up to me, but, I had to get used to the idea of them being tied to a relatively specific archetype(the leader if you're wondering.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:26:42-07:00","id":501489,"title":"","content":"Well sure someone could be a good leader but still have wasted potential. But let's say, for the sake of example, that this general doesn't have any wasted potential. He's 100% the best he could be.<br /> <br /> He trains the servants into an army, and leads them in the fight to freedom. Does that not make him a Fairest?<br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> But you know. as MachineIV said - saying that the charachter does not have this cool and interesting trait to prove a point doesn't make him interesting. So rather than saying this general doesn't have &quot;unfulfilled potential&quot; I'm going to give him a different trait: Jingoism.<br /> <br /> General Warfield became a soldier because he believed in America. America was the land of the free, the home of the brave, and if America did it then it couldn't be wrong. He believed it even when he was ordering a carpet bombing of some Afghanistan village.<br /> <br /> Then when he was abducted for the first time he experienced what it was like to be powerless. How different was living in fear of the faerie sultan from living in fear of the American bombers? Being a slave made Warfield resolve to fight for the weak against the strong, not the strong against the week. He trained his fellow slaves into an army and fought his way to freedom, and after returning he trains any Freehold who asks to defend themselves from the Gentry and their Servants. (Legionnaire of the Iron Wall basically)<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that's an interesting charachter. It's definately a Fairest, he's a leader through and through, and he escaped his Durance by being a leader. But does he have wasted potential? Maybe a little, but this story clearly isn't <u>about</u> his wasted potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:42:13-07:00","id":501509,"title":"","content":"So it struck me that Granny Weatherwax is a strangely perfect example of a Fairest, if you take this part form <i>Witches Abroad </i>(spoilers for the end of the book)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Granny Weatherwax: \u201cI\u2019m goin\u2019 to give you the hidin\u2019 our Mam never gave you, Lily Weatherwax. Not with magic, not with headology, not with a stick like our Dad had, aye, and he used a fair bit as I recall- but with skin. And not because you was the bad one. Not because you meddled with stories. Everyone has a path they got to tread. But because, and I wants you to understand this prop\u2019ly, <b>after you went <u>I had</u> to be the good one. You had all the fun. An\u2019 there\u2019s no way I can make you pay for that, Lily, but I\u2019m surely goin\u2019 to give it a try</b>.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lily: \u201cBut\u2026I\u2026I\u2026 I\u2019m the good one. I\u2019m the good one. I can\u2019t lose. I\u2019m the godmother. You\u2019re the wicked witch\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Granny: \u201cGood? Good? Feeding people to stories? Twisting people\u2019s lives? That\u2019s good, is it. <b>You mean you didn\u2019t even have fun? If I\u2019d been as bad as you, I\u2019d have been a whole lot worse.</b> Better at it than you\u2019ve ever dreamed of.\u201d</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She's a Fairest Witchtooth who wishes she was a Darkling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:46:42-07:00","id":501510,"title":"","content":"My god. You're right! That's brilliant!<br /> <br /> (And wasted potential was never part of Granny's charachter - in fact she became a witch by tracking down a teacher and forcing her to take Granny as her student)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:48:25-07:00","id":501511,"title":"","content":"I have to say that this draft of the Fairest didn't really manage to grab me. Which is a shame as the Fairest has been one of my favorite Seemings of 1st edition being basically closest to the Gentry themselves in many ways.<br /> <br /> I agree with an above poster about the background though, it seems forced unless 2nd ed will change from all Lost having been willingly taken or having wondered to the arms of the Gentry by themselves instead of being abducted or taken. And even if it has changed it still feels like it is saying that if you want to play a Fairest you have to have been a wallflower with potential instead of already having been a leader or something else entirely. Limiting choices like this is not a good way to go in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As for the Blessing/Curse aspect. The Blessing works once a <i>Story</i> while the Curse in this case seems something that will happen once a session at the least. There is always collateral damage of some sort involved in leadership one important part of that is accepting it and trying to minimize it or guide it towards things that do not matter that much. Of course this might be just an issue of clarity as well since it seems that for example the Darklings can benefit from their Blessing as often as it comes up, but the ST is encouraged to make sure it has a chance to come up at least once per story while the Fairest Blessing clearly limits it to once per story. Also the Darklings Curse is a matter of choice, basically if you choose to not trust anyone and, even if you secretly trust someone, decide to not follow them blindly questioning them at all times the Curse barely ever comes up while the Fairest Curse seems ever present. You sent someone to procure a map from a store nearby as part of you organizing your next project and he get's assaulted on the journey, it would have been avoided if you had not given the order or had sent more people etc., and you get struck by the Curse. You as a leader have to make a difficult choice and whatever you choose will end up hurting someone, not at all uncommon position for a leader to be in, what ever you choose you will be hit by the Curse etc. For Darklings it's a choice that can be averted, similarly for a Beast though as it is about being bound so it can also be force on them but still it is not entirely unavoidable unlike it seems to be for the Fairest.<br /> <br /> Of course I may be understanding it wrong but to me it still reads like something you will be struck with several times a session potentially while the other Seeming's Curses may come up once or twice a story if at all in the hands of a clever player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T02:32:55-07:00","id":501579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501349#post501349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen <i>Maleficent</i>? Compared to previous renderings of the fairy tale, it's much better, and Aurora works much better as a Fairest there. Not perfect; she's not the protagonist or anything, but it certainly vaults over the low bar presented by the 1959 movie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, I haven't. I heard they gave her a backstory in order to make Maleficent tragic or sympathetic. That is not the Maleficent I know and love. My version has green skin, crashes royal birthday parties, and turns into a dragon because she gives zero fucks about what you have to say on the matter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-03-2015, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T03:49:37-07:00","id":501590,"title":"","content":"Your Maleficent is an old green hag living in a half-crumbled castle, surronded by idiotic toadies and who decided to waste years in a bitter petty revenge against an inocente for a lesser slight, because deep down she doesn't know what else do with her life?<br /> <br /> Sounds like my uncle's wife with magical powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-04-2015, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T04:57:42-07:00","id":501602,"title":"","content":"Just noting this, but as a long time Changeling fan I'm tickled pink that the 'leader' faction in this draft is not a lording over backwards fool or too arrogant for their own good.<br /> <br /> So, yay, finally a fresh new take on the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:11:18-07:00","id":501606,"title":"","content":"I think this has the same specific focus as Darklings, which is not ideal in my opinion. It is evocative and well written though.<br /> <br /> For me, the theme of abuse is only part of what makes Changeling a great game. The other parts are beautiful madness, the sanity aspect, the wonder and the sheer fairy-tale weirdness of it all. You can play Fairy tale: PTSD or you can play Fables or Sandman or just weirdly powered politics. Most games have a balance of all of these.<br /> <br /> I think my main issue with the seemings as written is that the abuse angle is focused on strongly, but the current write-ups are lacking the other parts, the weirdness, the wonder, the madness, the beauty. The beast write up had elements of this, the character concepts were vague enough you could think of a few different animialistic characters, (except the shark broker, I'd have preferred a write up that gives the impression of a predator thats all tooth rather than be so explict).<br /> <br /> Perhaps this comes from the drafts being shown out of context and the new focus on Seeming as your escape-choice naturally draws out the abuse themes. The writing is not a problem for me, its good. Its just the choice on what is being written doesn't fully capture the full tone of the game. Presumably seemings will be one of the first things in the book someone will read? If so then I think a little bit more time on the other aspects of the game is important.<br /> <br /> If it was my choice, I would limit background sections to a sentance or two and use the extra space to add more fairy tale weirdness. If background is defintely staying in, then please re-write the character concepts to be more fairy-tale esqe.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion. It is an attempt at constructive criticism. I won't be offended if the drafts stay as is, I will ignore them, or run Changeling 1e with 2e mechanics (which I have no doubt will be excellent!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:16:10-07:00","id":501609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501304#post501304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6} Someone wanted Elementals next. I can nudge that to happen next. No problem. For a taste? Have you seen the movie Party Monster? Or know the story of Michael Alig? Look it up if not. That's a place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, uh, I read his story on wikipedia and this quote really hit me: &quot;What do you have to do to get attention around here - kill somebody?&quot;.<br /> What if Elementals had to kill someone, or a part of themselves to escape? Or, more accurately, to remember being human in the first place?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:26:37-07:00","id":501613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501304#post501304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for all your comments. I'm getting some thoughts here. I will remind you this is a very first draft draft, and clearly, I need to tighten up some of the language. So here's some thoughts and comments and questions answered. Ready? Here we go! <br /> <br /> 1)Someone asked if the Clarity check is for when you make hard choices and people get hurt or also when you're 'job' makes you punch a dude, and they get hurt. I can clarify that. It is in fact when the damage is splash-over or accidentally. It's meant to be about collateral damage, not about 'I need to punch a guy because that guy needs to be punched.' It's meant to be, &amp;quot;I punched a guy because he needed to be punched, and then he died, and now his widow can't support her family any more.&amp;quot; This plays into the idea that ever if you're a good leader (which not all Fairest are) the choices you make, even perfectly legit choices, are going to have consequence. And for the tragic Fairest, that eats at you. See, the Fairest didn't ask to be a leader, didn't ask for people to look up to them, but they kinda have to do it. And even though they generally don't 'sign up for it' so to speak, it still eats at them and slowly kills them that they fuck up even when they don't fuck up. That's the tragedy of the Fairest. And the horror. No matter what you do, even as you do your best, you can never be as perfect as everyone thinks you are, and that could just break you into a million pieces one day. If you know the play, ask yourself, what did Lear look like before he was old and established? King Lear is a place where Fairest can end up, easily, and plenty of them KNOW that, and maybe, can't do shit to stop it.<br /> <br /> 2)I see some comments about 'horror' and 'this isn't dark enough.' Well. Horror comes in many shades and genre. Changeling the Lost is, at it's core, psychological horror. Horror in your head and your gut, not horror that jumps out of the corner and screams at you. So. Sometimes the scary is more cerebral. See above. And below probably.<br /> <br /> 3)I see some discussion about Disney Princesses. First, full disclosure,I have STRONG opinions about Princesses. They are highly problimatic and yet incredibly important, and that they can do as much good as they do harm, culturally speaking. And actually, that's kind of the Fairest too, isn't it? They CAN do a lot good, but will they? I also saw someone saying basically 'Disney Princesses can't be Fairest because they had everything just handed to them.&amp;quot; Actually, that's exactly why they would be Fairest. Each Fairest made a choice to step up, to stand up, to help someone, and that let them escape. But they didn't sign up for the long-haul, you understand. It's thrust on them. Imagine if you saved a guy from being hit by a car one day. Nice feelings, yay! You made a really good self sacrificing choice! Cool! Now the dude is living on your front doorstep, waiting for you to come out, asking you what to do with his life, begging you to take care of him, advise him, and worse, his friends are joining in. If you're not careful, there's going to a cult around you in no time. And just imagine how that cult is going to react when they find out that you only saved the guy because you were trying to steal his wallet. Whoopse. Higher the pedestal, the harder the fall. (You see this in the treatment of famous people ALL THE TIME!) To bring it back to the Princesses, because I can't resist them... Imagine Cinderella. She's spent most of her life now, abused by her stepmother, all of her skills involve house cleaning and management. She can mend clothes. That was good enough. Now (because she saved some mice, basically) she's a queen of an entire kingdom and married to a man she doesn't really know. A pure heart, or at least, a moment of purity put her in this position. What if she can't hack it? What if she turns around and abuses her staff the way she was abused, because she has no idea how to communicate with employees except the abuse she learned? What if the rush passes and she realizes her Prince Charming is a jerk for XYZ reason, and or she simply can't connect with him? What will the people of her fair kingdom do when she's caught in an affair with a stable hand because, frankly, she can emotionally connect with him better? What if she's asked to make an important domestic choice for the kingdom, and the result hurts everyone? Mice-workers right SOUNDED good, but it's crushed the local economy because she doesn't have the know-how to transition the kingdom from a domestic-slavery culture to something more fair? <br /> <br /> 4)On a smaller, more intimate level, the big brother who takes the abuse so that drunk dad can't murder mom and little sister? Who ever tagged this idea? Yeah. Hard, but, yeah, that's actually the deeper undertone I was going for. If you want to take it to this level, which is smaller and harder, you look at the Fairest like this. You take the beatings so dad doesn't murder mom. Every day you ask yourself, though, would mom have left if you weren't taking the heat? Would mom and everyone leave if little sister got popped the way you do, even once? (How unfair would that be, huh?) Little sister is kind of turning into a monster, she's hurting small animals, is that your fault too? Why doesn't anyone ever fucking THANK you for the beatings you take? Would everyone be better off if you just murdered dad? Who would you be if you killed him? Maybe you should just leave, let them sort their own shit out! But. You won't do that. You can't do any of that, because they need you, they don't thank you, but they need you, and know it. <br /> <br /> 5)Darklings and Fairest are opposite, but not enemies. In fact, they should work in a fucked up sort of harmony most of the time. In the example in number 4? Yeah. The Darkling there might be little sister. Big brother can't do the deed, the deed that needs to be done, and so, one day, Darkling little sister will creep into dad's room when he's out cold, and put something in his drink. She knows big brother may have to hate her for it, but she does it anyway. Big brother will do the right thing, probably, though, and take credit for the killing, going to prison, but the end result is actually the right one. Mom is free of dad, and little sister slips off through the cracks, and big brother gets to be the big hero. The fairytale ending, right?<br /> <br /> 6} Someone wanted Elementals next. I can nudge that to happen next. No problem. For a taste? Have you seen the movie Party Monster? Or know the story of Michael Alig? Look it up if not. That's a place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div> You won me over with this. It makes me think of Justin Trudeau honestly (not going to make this political, but its pretty obvious).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:31:15-07:00","id":501616,"title":"","content":"I think its more rolemodel then they're all born to be King. Even when not in charge, people look to the Fairest for advice or with high expectations, ones they might not be capable of, and this dynamic can get people killed.<br /> <br /> I can see Fairest who go and become hermits to avoid this, especially ones who realize they'll never met expectations.<br /> <br /> Now that I get Fairest better I really like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:51:29-07:00","id":501619,"title":"","content":"I think I found a better way to summarize my problem with the Fairest Blessing/Curse. With the two previous Seemings when you play into to Seeming archetype you get the blessing and kinda automatically avoid the Curse, for the most part, where as if you play the Fairest to their archetype you get the Blessing but are stuck in constant struggle with the Curse as well.<br /> <br /> That is the curse punishes a Darkling for having trust which is uncharacteristic of the Darklings who have trust issues and the Blessing enforces this same matter by rewarding them for making and going thru with the hard choices where as the Fairest are punished for being leaders while their Blessing tries to guide them to be leaders. Is this difference intentional?<br /> <br /> If I am misunderstanding something please enlighten me but to me this is just odd design here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also as is the Fairest are kinda forced into being leaders, aka this is their only concept where as a Darkling despite not himself trusting of anyone and ready to make the hard choices could still be played out as a leader, if somewhat ruthless one, similarly Beast could be played as a sort of Pack Alpha etc. Their Blessings and Curses do not limit the concepts one can play with them unlike with the Fairest who are kinda forced into being leaders by their Blessing and Curse. Again this differentiates them from the two previously shown Seemings. Is this intentional as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:51:51-07:00","id":501620,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit ambiguous about this Seeming. As presented, their Escape focuses on making people go along with them, while it could focus on how they chose to help others escape too. I've seen the whole designated leader thing lead to lot of troubles with the Sidhe in the Dreaming and the Silver Fangs in Apocalypse, so I'm kind of wary about this aspect, especially since it looks like it's all the Fairest do now. In my experience, it can often lead to a player trying to take charge, using the splat's write up as an excuse to coerce the others into going along with him. I'd be more comfortable if they were about something broader, that could include leadership, like being protectors or caregivers. <br /> <br /> I'm also for better defining their curse. As of now, it kind of condemn them into trying to emulate some kind of pacifist benevolent ruler, since it doesn't even indicate if the people getting hurt have to be the Fairest's people for the currse to take effect. I think it makes them a bit too much super hero-like for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I like their backgrounds as people who once didn't live up to their potential but finally stepped up when it mattered most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T06:23:10-07:00","id":501631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501111#post501111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Fairest are about accepting responsibility. They're basically the flip side of Darklings, then. I really wasn't expecting them to go this route but I think its an interesting direction for them to go.</div> </div> </div> </div> In a way, the Darklings actually talk about the Fairest. The document describes the Fairest as the shining heroes, and the Darkling writeup talks about them falling into darkness as the hero marches off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, after reading the Fairest writeup, I feel like its describing the police almost to a T. Well, the good, non-a-hole peoples anyways. A lot of people end up joining those professions because they feel that they have to give stuff up for protecting and leading people. Certainly, they don't join because of the money. When they're on patrol, so much is left up to making snap judgement and &quot;reasonable suspicion,&quot; try to shove a plan together at the snap second; so much can go so wrong so fast, and it often crushes their souls so quickly. Righteousness gets tainted really quickly when you're constantly faced with the worst troublemakers and disappointments before it crushes your idealism.<br /> <br /> In a real way, the Fairest are the embodiment of fairy tale heroes. I can't tell if a lot of Fairest would be drawn to that job after they return, thinking they could do things right in the mortal world with their hero complex with jobs that attract highly moral people. That's the intent I feel, anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On that same vein, however. I feel like the Fairest.... aren't anymore. Mirror mirror, on the wall, who's the fairest of them all? That was a huge thing before, but now... I don't feel it. Snow White and Prince Charming could both be Fairest. In 1e, so was the Evil Queen. Now? She's not. Instead, we could have even ugly heroes as Fairest. <br /> <br /> The name feels 100% like a misnomer. There is nothing about the Fairest that are fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T06:31:45-07:00","id":501634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501606#post501606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this has the same specific focus as Darklings, which is not ideal in my opinion. It is evocative and well written though.<br /> <br /> For me, the theme of abuse is only part of what makes Changeling a great game. The other parts are beautiful madness, the sanity aspect, the wonder and the sheer fairy-tale weirdness of it all. You can play Fairy tale: PTSD or you can play Fables or Sandman or just weirdly powered politics. Most games have a balance of all of these.<br /> <br /> I think my main issue with the seemings as written is that the abuse angle is focused on strongly, but the current write-ups are lacking the other parts, the weirdness, the wonder, the madness, the beauty. The beast write up had elements of this, the character concepts well vague enough you could think of a few different animialistic characters, (except the shark broker, I'd have preferred a write up that gives the impression of a predator thats all tooth rather than be so explict).<br /> <br /> Perhaps this comes from the drafts being shown out of context and the new focus on Seeming as your escape-choice naturally draws out the abuse themes. The writing is not a problem for me, its good. Its just the choice on what is being written doesn't fully capture the full tone of the game. Presumably seemings will be one of the first things in the book someone will read? If so then I think a little bit more time on the other aspects of the game is important.<br /> <br /> If it was my choice, I would limit background sections to a sentance or two and use the extra space to add more fairy tale weirdness. If background is defintely staying in, then please re-write the character concepts to be more fairy-tale esqe.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion. It is an attempt at constructive criticism. I won't be offended if the drafts stay as is, I ]will ignore them, or run Changeling 1e with 2e mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a counterpoint: I feel like there's probably plenty of space in the book to present and explore &quot;fairy tale weirdness&quot;. Even if it's not heavily prevalent in the individual Seeming write-ups, the taking charge of agency is evidently connected to the narrative of Arcadia and wrestling <i>yours</i> specifically back from your Keeper, and this aspect will likely be explored in the introduction chapter. I'm sure the beautiful madness, the wonder, and the oddity of it all will be emphasized through the book.<br /> <br /> Additionally, let's remember how David said that Seeming is the one section of the book that <i>can't</i> be much about trauma (also as a nod to those commenting the Fairest seem &quot;too bright&quot;), and in very much the same way (though this is just my interpretation), Seeming is probably one section of the book that <i>can't</i> be too much about the strangeness of Faerie. Because it is also about how you grounded yourself in your escape and away from the madness of your captivity and Arcadia. In fact, that's exactly what the Blessing is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-03-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T07:43:50-07:00","id":501701,"title":"","content":"I'm going to offer what I can on the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501304#post501304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Someone asked if the Clarity check is for when you make hard choices and people get hurt or also when you're 'job' makes you punch a dude, and they get hurt. I can clarify that. It is in fact when the damage is splash-over or accidentally. It's meant to be about collateral damage, not about 'I need to punch a guy because that guy needs to be punched.' It's meant to be, &quot;I punched a guy because he needed to be punched, and then he died, and now his widow can't support her family any more.&quot; This plays into the idea that ever if you're a good leader (which not all Fairest are) the choices you make, even perfectly legit choices, are going to have consequence. And for the tragic Fairest, that eats at you. See, the Fairest didn't ask to be a leader, didn't ask for people to look up to them, but they kinda have to do it. And even though they generally don't 'sign up for it' so to speak, it still eats at them and slowly kills them that they fuck up even when they don't fuck up. That's the tragedy of the Fairest. And the horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and see in here a lot of what the Fairest in this write up are really about. I do think the writing needs tightened up, as that might help the feeling that Fairest are getting pigeon-holed, that they can't be anything other than the Court Monarch or Motley Leader. For instance, as you pointed out Filamena, the Fairest aren't about necessarily being in the official leadership position (I actually think maybe trying the write-up without using the word &quot;leader&quot; <i>at all</i> would an interesting way to try this) they're all about taking up responsibility. This doesn't necessarily mean becoming King of the Summer Court (though certainly a Fairest could!) but what it does mean (in my interpretation of the Fairest) is this;<br /> <br /> Benjamin is probably one of the most iconic Summer King's the Court has ever had, no one doubts the Ifrit Beast's rage at the Gentry, and he proved it when that Huntsmen's fire station went up in smoke. What everyone realized quick, though, was that when you needed anything other than a whole lot of fire you didn't visit the king, you walked straight into the hall and took a right, to a small office with a flowering fairest sitting behind it and a name plaque reading &quot;Tulip&quot; (the name being part of the campaign scheme). Tulip doesn't mind though, and listens to all your troubles with a smile. Having trouble with a loan? She'll tell you how to deal the creditors, can't bring yourself to mess with with those creepy Autumn Court types? Tulip will handle it for you.<br /> <br /> What nobody ever bothers to wonder is how Karen (her real name, not that anyone bothers to ask) got the job in the first place. That Benjamin thought he needed someone sociable to handle the reception work. That the only experience she had was as a Computer Science major, and giving advice on how to keep Mizer from smashing your knees for his money without calling a significant chunk of the Winter Court down on you was something she had no idea how to do. She has to though, she knows that, the Court can't look to Benjamin for this, so she'll have to do. <br /> <br /> She just prays what she's doing won't make it worse. But she's gotten this far, and no matter what happens she won't let what happened with Charlotte's motley happen again, she can't.<br /> <br /> (ugh, apologize if that's terrible, I just hope it gets my point across)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501304#post501304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6} Someone wanted Elementals next. I can nudge that to happen next. No problem. For a taste? Have you seen the movie Party Monster? Or know the story of Michael Alig? Look it up if not. That's a place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, please Elementals next, as much as I like all the Seeming's I want to see how the one for my first Changeling character will be in 2.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T07:44:32-07:00","id":501702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501631#post501631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that same vein, however. I feel like the Fairest.... aren't anymore. Mirror mirror, on the wall, who's the fairest of them all? That was a huge thing before, but now... I don't feel it. Snow White and Prince Charming could both be Fairest. In 1e, so was the Evil Queen. Now? She's not. Instead, we could have even ugly heroes as Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which makes sense, since the Evil Queen's entire point is that she wasn't the fairest of them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said if you look at some of the other portrayals of the evil Queen archetype - I'm currently thinking of Cora from Once Upon a Time and the Evil Queen for the 10th Kingdom. I can see how they would work.<br /> <br /> They have such a aura of power and competence that you &quot;know&quot; they're going to win. You know they're the bad guy, but you also believe they're like a steamroller, you're either behind them or you're in front of them; so you get behind them and do their evil bidding and hope there's still a place for you when they've won.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T07:52:47-07:00","id":501706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501702#post501702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which makes sense, since the Evil Queen's entire point is that she wasn't the fairest of them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said if you look at some of the other portrayals of the evil Queen archetype - I'm currently thinking of Cora from Once Upon a Time and the Evil Queen for the 10th Kingdom. I can see how they would work.<br /> <br /> They have such a aura of power and competence that you &quot;know&quot; they're going to win. You know they're the bad guy, but you also believe they're like a steamroller, you're either behind them or you're in front of them; so you get behind them and do their evil bidding and hope there's still a place for you when they've won.</div> </div> </div> </div>After snow white, you're right. Before? She absolutely was the fairest. The fact she couldn't stand being second best after being first is the point of the story.<br /> <br /> The point is that Fairest have nothing to do with their name anymore. It has to do with being a Big D@#$ Hero now, even if they are fallible, make bad choices. I feel a disconnect between the name and what we're actually presented with, because being a hero has nothing to do with being fair.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that we're presented with a selfish-evil type of Fairest anymore. The write up suggests they're driven by duty and responsibility - not exactly ingredients for evil. Misguided, perhaps. But making a choice to risk lives? I'm not seeing the evil queen archetypes at all, no matter how fair they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-03-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T07:59:34-07:00","id":501709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501706#post501706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After snow white, you're right. Before? She absolutely was the fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div> But we never see her before snow white, who knows what she was like back then. Maybe she was a great leader.<br /> <br /> Maybe the entire point is that she wasn't a terrible leader. She did one act of leadership that impressed the king, then <i>completely</i> failed to follow through and finally snapped when the mirror said she wasn't good enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501706#post501706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that Fairest have nothing to do with their name anymore. It has to do with being a Big D@#$ Hero now, even if they are fallible, make bad choices. I feel a disconnect between the name and what we're actually presented with, because being a hero has nothing to do with being fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't argue with that; and I won't object to them changing the name.<br /> <br /> However it's not a big deal to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T08:21:47-07:00","id":501729,"title":"","content":"After my first read through, it's not something I like. Now, I'm not going to go Edition wars, because each edition will be valid in its own way, but there was something about the Beautiful Madness that floated around Fairest in First edition that I really liked, and made Fairest stand out. Now, it seems more like that has been excised, and the leader archetype has been thrust on them, and while that is a nice concept, it's removed one of the signatures of Fairest. Fairest aren't supposed to be 'nicer' than other people, or more like a leader (though, the leader thing might be the case with this new write-up), they've just previously been creatures that may be a little more like the Gentry and that causes its own problems which other characters can admire... and fear.<br /> <br /> Do we want it in the system that Fairest are most likely to be Monarchs? Maybe, we can see, but I don't want 1/6th of Seemings to be based around it. It tilts the game a lot more than the Beast and Darkling seeming write ups have appeared to.<br /> <br /> I'm going to come back in a bit after I've dwelled on it to see if I feel the same way later, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":287,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","user":"Wildfire","date":". 05-03-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T08:37:29-07:00","id":501735,"title":"","content":"While I loved the other Seeming write-ups I didn't like this one as much. I have no problem with the Fairest being the ones that seek to inspire or lead, but I do agree with Wildfire, the defining feature of them that I felt essential to their character was that they were the closest of the Seemings to the mindset of the True Fae, they Fae-like arrogance is what made them stand out from other Seemings to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T08:49:16-07:00","id":501739,"title":"","content":"After some thought, I think I have to eccho Felipe. I'm fine with the new leadership angle, but I definitely don't want the Fairest to lose their identity as the most similar to the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:03:25-07:00","id":501745,"title":"","content":"I agree with both Wildfire and Felipe above. The Fairest have lost that Beautiful Madness inherent in them, and what made them into my favourite Seeming in the 1st ed, and with it they lost any concept that is about an unfair or selfish person since their Curse kinda forces them to be nice and considerate. Where as for example Darklings are rewarded for making the hard choices they are not forced to make them, it's an option, meanwhile their Curse again inflicts almost no restrictions on their personalities, they are as able to be the noble hero as anyone else except they cannot trust others only trusting themselves, while the Fairest Curse actively forces players to play the good guy as they are punished for neglecting others getting a Clarity break if they inflict emotional or physical harm to people circling them.<br /> <br /> That is to say one cannot play an aloof and beautiful tyrant as Fairest at all unless of course 2nd edition Clarity works considerably differently from before and loosing it isn't that big of a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:06:04-07:00","id":501749,"title":"","content":"You're worried that the <i>leader-type</i> splat will lose their connection to the <i>Lords and Ladies </i>of Faerie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:09:52-07:00","id":501750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501749#post501749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're worried that the <i>leader-type</i> splat will lose their connection to the <i>Lords and Ladies </i>of Faerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Lords and Ladies of Faerie seem concerned for their subjects? Are they forced into being non-tyrant types? Can they be any sort of leader they desire?<br /> Answer to all of the above is yes for the Gentry and resounding no for the Fairest.<br /> <br /> Hence the worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:10:24-07:00","id":501751,"title":"","content":"The Fairest can still be mad and fey, no one said that the causes they take up have to be sane. They can still be arrogant bastards who abuse their authority because damnit people just keep putting everything on them and they need to live a little. Maybe if they're an asshole then others will grow up. Maybe that dude you sent out who got jumped, that was the -plan- you knew it was a risk that could happen, you accepted it, move on. <br /> <br /> Being a Fairest you have responsibility piled on you, by others or by yourself or both. What you consider a correct way to execute those responsibilities, and which of them you accept or reject are up to you. You receive Clarity for being right, for succeeding, but it doesn't matter what you were right about. You suffer a breaking point because you failed to meet your own expectations, but there's nothing to force you into only having morally acceptable expectations.<br /> <br /> Everyone keeps mentioning that the Fairest is now pigeon-holed to the Leader archetype, but the example of the homeless dude puts paid to that concept. None of the people he's helping have any clue he's doing it. He's just arbitrarily grabbed this cause to represent, and it just so happens to help out others.<br /> <br /> If you have problems with the trope thn subvert or deconstruct it, you never have to play it straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:34:33-07:00","id":501801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501453#post501453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Fairests 2.0 are Ventrues? Didn't see that coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, especially since in 1.0 they were Daevas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:54:24-07:00","id":501813,"title":"","content":"Hard to subvert it when the Curse literally goes like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any time a Fairest makes a call as a leader, and someone gets seriously hurt physically or otherwise, is a Clarity Break. </div> </div> </div>Any of your call's whether intentional or not that lead to someone getting hurt will cause you a Clarity break. You cannot be a bastard towards others since it would cause you to plummet in Clarity, you cannot be a Tyrant because it causes you to plummet in Clarity. All you can really be is either someone who completely avoids any and all leadership positions and actively refuses to give directions orders and suggestions or you can be a nice and considerate leader hoping that you always are able to make such calls that do not cause any misfortune to fall upon someone.<br /> <br /> Makes it a bit hard to subvert or deconstruct it.<br /> <br /> Also like I have pointed out their Curse deviates sharply from those given for the Darklings and the Beasts whom both have Curses that come rarely into play if playing the archetype, coming more into focus if trying to break or deviate from the archetype, where as the Fairest playing straight into his archetype of leader will be constantly suffering from his Curse.<br /> <br /> Even the Fairest Blessing seems to talk about how all they need to do is lead those under them and it matters not whether it is right or wrong thing to do, it's about it appearing to be the right thing. But this is in direct opposition to what the Curse says in that they must actually make only decisions that cause no one to be hurt in any manner or form. Better Curse would likely be that they suffer a Clarity break should someone reveal that their leadership is not actually needed. That is to say since it is natural for people to follow the Fairest and it is natural, and Blessing worthy, for the Fairest to take up that leadership the Curse should be that they suffer a Clarity break should it be proven that someone else would do a better job, in essence the mirror answering that they are not the fairest of them all anymore, or that the people following them wouldn't even need to be lead. But even in this case it should be noted that to be a good leader in the large scale does not necessarily mean that he should need to be a nice leader or a considerate one, in fact a tyrant could in some cases be the best option.<br /> <br /> So perhaps something on that line should replace the no harm done Curse? How does it sound?<br /> <br /> Should I just open up my wallet and pay filamena the 5 cents a word price to rewrite the Curse? In the end it would only cost around 3$ or so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *In case it isn't obvious the last part was a jest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:32:23-07:00","id":501882,"title":"","content":"I can a Darkling who ends up as the Darkling, because of a Fairest. Maybe the Fairest convinces a Romantic Kith Changeling to seduce someone who has a way out and refuses to share it.<br /> <br /> The Fairest points out that this other changeling was going to abaddon the rest of them and that they need the key that Changeling has to get free. <br /> <br /> So the Romantic feeling betrayed by the Changeling with the key seduces and then steals the key, and runs off with the other changelings, leaving the key's owner behind. The Fairest baits the Guard Dogs while the Darkling is seducing, yet manages to get free in time to flee with the others. The Fairest becomes a Fairest from risking her life distracting the guard dogs so others can escape, while the Darkling becames a Darkling because she betrayed the Changeling with the key, which she did reluctantly because the Fairest convinced her too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:35:39-07:00","id":501897,"title":"","content":"Maybe its no accident that the Fairest's Blessing sets them up often for they're curse, drifting into madness was always a key part of the Fairest, not impossible to avoid, but a natural drift nevertheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:41:10-07:00","id":501901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501897#post501897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe its no accident that the Fairest's Blessing sets them up often for they're curse, drifting into madness was always a key part of the Fairest, not impossible to avoid, but a natural drift nevertheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it is intentional. I actually really like the interplay between the Blessing and the Curse. Although, I liked that with Beasts and Darklings, the Curse was something that reminded them of their Durance and the Blessing was something that recalled their escape. I had hoped that would be a consistent pattern for all of the Seemings, but I don't really see it in the Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:56:57-07:00","id":501907,"title":"","content":"For those who say you can't make an evil Fairest... Filamena pointed out the curse is about collateral damage, unexpected complications. The Evil Queen can avoid her curse by being aloof and cruel. If she leaves others to handle decisions (despite the fact they come to her), she evades her curse and blessing both. If she orders her knight to die for the cause, and makes it obvious that will be the case, I dont think itd trigger her Curse. Now, if she orders the knight (who was supposed to die) and he comes back victorious, but with his squire dead and the enemy (who the queen wanted to live) dead.. thats when she loses Clarity. selfish and fae are still a part of the Fairest, even if its in subtext and not obvious. also.. I don't see the Fairest as the leader splat. Hell, if anything, Id see most trying to avoid actual positions of leadership to avoid their Curse. many won't want to handle all those expectations because they realistically know theyre not perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:01:38-07:00","id":501909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501901#post501901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it is intentional. I actually really like the interplay between the Blessing and the Curse. Although, I liked that with Beasts and Darklings, the Curse was something that reminded them of their Durance and the Blessing was something that recalled their escape. I had hoped that would be a consistent pattern for all of the Seemings, but I don't really see it in the Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failed potential again and again and again, I think is the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:42:32-07:00","id":501952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501907#post501907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who say you can't make an evil Fairest... Filamena pointed out the curse is about collateral damage, unexpected complications. The Evil Queen can avoid her curse by being aloof and cruel. If she leaves others to handle decisions (despite the fact they come to her), she evades her curse and blessing both. If she orders her knight to die for the cause, and makes it obvious that will be the case, I dont think itd trigger her Curse. Now, if she orders the knight (who was supposed to die) and he comes back victorious, but with his squire dead and the enemy (who the queen wanted to live) dead.. thats when she loses Clarity. selfish and fae are still a part of the Fairest, even if its in subtext and not obvious. also.. I don't see the Fairest as the leader splat. Hell, if anything, Id see most trying to avoid actual positions of leadership to avoid their Curse. many won't want to handle all those expectations because they realistically know theyre not perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... except that Fairest, according to the write up, are natural leaders and heroes; their Blessing and likely Contracts are all wrapped up in that as well, I bet. &quot;I'm avoiding my curse by being aloof!&quot; isn't so much of avoiding the curse as &quot;avoiding having anything to do with the Seeming by being aloof.&quot; Seems kind of counter intuitive to me. I can play a Darkling that's all trusting social butterfly. I can play a conservative Beast that is all about following traditions and social norms. But .... why? Isn't there a bit of a buy in when you're picking these Seemings? <br /> <br /> You don't have to play the cliche stereotype, but isn't there something tied in? Why is the Seeming picked at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:35:59-07:00","id":502036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501813#post501813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Fairest Blessing seems to talk about how all they need to do is lead those under them and it matters not whether it is right or wrong thing to do, it's about it appearing to be the right thing. But this is in direct opposition to what the Curse says in that they must actually make only decisions that cause no one to be hurt in any manner or form. Better Curse would likely be that they suffer a Clarity break should someone reveal that their leadership is not actually needed. That is to say since it is natural for people to follow the Fairest and it is natural, and Blessing worthy, for the Fairest to take up that leadership the Curse should be that they suffer a Clarity break should it be proven that someone else would do a better job, in essence the mirror answering that they are not the fairest of them all anymore, or that the people following them wouldn't even need to be lead. But even in this case it should be noted that to be a good leader in the large scale does not necessarily mean that he should need to be a nice leader or a considerate one, in fact a tyrant could in some cases be the best option.<br /> <br /> So perhaps something on that line should replace the no harm done Curse? How does it sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put this other way, also. Fairest of 1ed are <b>both</b> Snow White and Evil Queen. Cinderella and here Evil Stepmother. 1ed was about rather grandour of person, not if she was &quot;good&quot;. In 2ed it should also be consider.<br /> <br /> In <b>Once Upon a Time</b> at least half of characters are 1ed Fairest, and most seems like they work even better as now version of 2ed Fairest. But the problem is with villians - almost all of them in series, very fairy tale like, could work as 1ed Fairest - they all bold, beautiful, and wicked to the core. Until they do not, but it's characters choice, not some &quot;uphill struggle with mechanics&quot; of world.<br /> <br /> I very miss this &quot;shades of grey&quot; part of Fairest write-up, and with now 2ed Curse construction, I feel you cannot make logically Fairest villian - the are all &quot;justice and honor&quot; or raveging maniacs ( low Clarity ). There cannot be Operating Tyrants of Freehold, or even just &quot;devil with good intentions&quot;, that were large part of 1ed Fairest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:06:27-07:00","id":502068,"title":"","content":"The villains of OUAP still qualify.<br /> <br /> Very, very little of what, say, Rumpelstilskin or Regina does is without forethought and noting who is going to be hurt very specifically. That kind of thing, by developer notes, nixes Clarity loss. A Fairest pure villain is a patient, calculating one, sort of like how an Evil Monarch is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I also suspect that if you're looking for pure villains, you don't look at truly free changelings. Or changelings in general; it's hard to hate an escaped slave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:15:15-07:00","id":502072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502068#post502068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or changelings in general; it's hard to hate an escaped slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhh.... since when aren't cycles of abuse not a compelling plot point. Most of the worst villains are only the way they are because they have trauma and brokenness in their past.<br /> <br /> This obviously doesn't hold true for born psychopaths, but they are rarely terribly compelling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:19:29-07:00","id":502079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502072#post502072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhhh.... since when aren't cycles of abuse not a compelling plot point. Most of the worst villains are only the way they are because they have trauma and brokenness in their past.<br /> <br /> This obviously doesn't hold true for born psychopaths, but they are rarely terribly compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he did say pure villains. <br /> <br /> That, and you could easily have villains in the style of Fairest, just base them off say, Byronic Heroes, or for that matter, someone so full of their own worldview that they do think they're say, taking on other responsibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:21:37-07:00","id":502081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Fairest pure villain is a patient, calculating one, sort of like how an Evil Monarch is supposed to be. </div> </div> </div>Which works well for a villain of a TV-series or a movie or even an RPG NPC but for a player character it's pretty damn demanding. I have yet to meet, and I have been playing since D&amp;D, a player who could pull such plots off in game, especially since ST fiat often comes to fore if nothing else, without collateral damage. Believe me no matter how well PC's plot things out and how meticulous their planning there will be collateral damage, and that collateral damage is exactly what set's of the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> So like said for me it's a no go but I envy people who's gaming group, and ST's who allow it, can plot and plan things in such detail that no collateral damage comes of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:22:30-07:00","id":502085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502072#post502072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhhh.... since when aren't cycles of abuse not a compelling plot point. Most of the worst villains are only the way they are because they have trauma and brokenness in their past.<br /> <br /> This obviously doesn't hold true for born psychopaths, but they are rarely terribly compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't view those people as pure villains. <br /> <br /> It's like Ultron from the most recent Avengers flick; he's evil, but it's quite clear he's also legitimately insane and honestly doesn't understand how &quot;destroy world&quot; is not the same as &quot;ensure peace.&quot; He's not evil because he's greedy or selfish, he has a bizzare way of looking at the world that makes sense to him.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think cycles of abuse are a bit overplayed, the abused usually becomes a different person than the abuser. Probably better in at least some ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:49:47-07:00","id":502132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502068#post502068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The villains of OUAP still qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wicked Witch? Snow Queen? Maleficent? Cruella? Ursula? They all be 1ed Fairest, but would be bonkers insane in 2ed, becuase of mishaps that Heroes put on them - the way they are <b>not </b>in OUAP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502068#post502068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very, very little of what, say, Rumpelstilskin or Regina does is without forethought and noting who is going to be hurt very specifically. That kind of thing, by developer notes, nixes Clarity loss. A Fairest pure villain is a patient, calculating one, sort of like how an Evil Monarch is supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will support Possesed point - now 2ed Curse makes you must play &quot;valor&quot; leader than &quot;wicked&quot; one - other way. you will, in time of play, loss Clarity very quickly as Fairest. Much more than Beasts by being civilized, or Darklings for trusting others. In other way - it's much easier in roleplaying game that something goes wrong with your plan ( most my games are all about it! ) than like you will be tricked by the trust you put on others. It's just unbalnced Curse, compared to others.<br /> <br /> I much more like to see a Curse as Fairest loosing they Clarity by the people do not beliving your leadership. &quot;You do not think I'm real Queen! Of with his head!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502068#post502068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also suspect that if you're looking for pure villains, you don't look at truly free changelings. Or changelings in general; it's hard to hate an escaped slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes I do. Escape slaves could develop their captives rituals. It's even a point on both 1ed Fairest and Ogres - you become somehow like the abusers that keep you in. In 1ed Fairest could be a megalomanic Flowering that think the Crown of Spring should be her's. It could be also the elvish consort that used ther beuty to trick people in the her way of thinking. I ask then - how can I recreate this kind of partial amorality with 2ed Fairest now, based on their Curse in write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T15:53:34-07:00","id":502251,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure I like this. The fairest from 1e were sympathetic not because of leadership, but because the price of whatever beauty was forced upon them by their keeper, was greater susceptibility to madness. They took all the flaws of the flesh and put them inside the brain. The Curse works up to a point here, but suggests that only the Fairest should be leaders. Or at least forces them into a role that not all such characters should take up.<br /> Maybe it\u2019s just the wording, I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T16:29:45-07:00","id":502287,"title":"","content":"The Fairest being painted as leaders, that makes sense. The Lords and Ladies, the rulers. Even having their blessing and curse tied into it. That makes sense. The problem comes from the fact that the leadership is being portrayed as <i>heroic</i>. Every last Fairest is Prince or Princess Charming, basically. And, while we're not saying other changelings can't be heroic, the implication is that this is the Seeming for it. <br /> <br /> Associating hero with beauty is... problematic to say the least. Not only by saying that evil isn't Fair, but that heroes generally are Fair; anyone can, and should, be considered heroic, not just the people we call Fairest. Good = beautiful is a bad trope to fall into, and I think that's part of the problem I have here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T16:44:28-07:00","id":502295,"title":"","content":"There is some shallow reading going on.<br /> <br /> Per usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T17:58:31-07:00","id":502338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502251#post502251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure I like this. The fairest from 1e were sympathetic not because of leadership, but because the price of whatever beauty was forced upon them by their keeper, was greater susceptibility to madness. They took all the flaws of the flesh and put them inside the brain. The Curse works up to a point here, but suggests that only the Fairest should be leaders. Or at least forces them into a role that not all such characters should take up.<br /> Maybe it\u2019s just the wording, I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe you're doing with them what the nameless people in the writeup do with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:01:19-07:00","id":502342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501813#post501813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes it a bit hard to subvert or deconstruct it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it. I see that as glaringly easy to deconstruct and subvert. During the initial discussions, I told her it was maybe too easy to subvert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:34:27-07:00","id":502366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501122#post501122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess <i>most</i> Disney princesses aren't Fairests after all, having their rewards handed to them on a silver, gleaming platter with little work on their part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Disney princesses lack agency, and so aren't suitable Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:39:37-07:00","id":502369,"title":"","content":"Are they fair, though? They seem to emphasize leadership more than anything else. Would Lords be a better title?<br /> <br /> There seems to be a disparity between, 'Fairest are, natural leaders, and of course rapidly and easily pick up the skills to go with that. Unless he avoids it, many Fairest show a knack for politics and law.'<br /> <br /> And the descriptions of the fairest given in the kiths sample.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:58:32-07:00","id":502376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502338#post502338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think maybe you're doing with them what the nameless people in the writeup do with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T19:07:03-07:00","id":502377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502376#post502376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Over-idealization is the Fairest bane; people assume they're the protagonists, and that's it. They may be deep protagonists, but they're still assumed to be the leaders of any given party and at least tolerate the duty, as well as at least having the ideals and morals of an ideal hero.<br /> <br /> It was mentioned on RPGnet that Filomena guessed this would happen. Maybe a little sidebar where it's pointed out that yes, this is really a problem and they really <i>don't </i>have those, inherently, and pointing out you, the reader, may be doing it right now, is in order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-03-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T19:08:01-07:00","id":502378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502369#post502369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they fair, though? They seem to emphasize leadership more than anything else. Would Lords be a better title?<br /> <br /> There seems to be a disparity between, 'Fairest are, natural leaders, and of course rapidly and easily pick up the skills to go with that. Unless he avoids it, many Fairest show a knack for politics and law.'<br /> <br /> And the descriptions of the fairest given in the kiths sample.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, but being a Fairest is about taking responsibility, and they don't do that. Even when it's heavily implied that their parents are dead or whatever, they hesitate to take the title of queen and are never seen conducting political or governmental business. In fact, they always seem disinterested or bored with such duties and rebel against social expectations of their status. Also, if they're princesses, then they should have a military or something under their command to help deal with the villain of the story, and instead they sit around waiting for a dashing knight to come to their rescue. One decree from a real Fairest and the villain could be dragged to the courtroom by the end of the day.<br /> <br /> Just look at Frolo, he was a priest / city official (depends on the version) and instead of hunting for Esmerelda himself, he rallied the people of Notre Dame into a full scale manhunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-03-2015, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T19:08:41-07:00","id":502379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502377#post502377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was mentioned on RPGnet that Filomena guessed this would happen. Maybe a little sidebar where it's pointed out that yes, this is really a problem, and pointing out you, the reader, may be doing it right now, is in order?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an easy assumption to make when it outright says they're natural leaders. Nothing seems to say they aren't leaders, just that they're not necessarily good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:34:40-07:00","id":502444,"title":"","content":"if Fairest are natural leaders and everyone tries to put them in positions of leadership, what reason could i have so that they arent always the leaders of the court?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:52:40-07:00","id":502455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502287#post502287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Associating hero with beauty is... problematic to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the mechanics make them attractive. That used to come from their glamour fueled Blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:59:26-07:00","id":502457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502444#post502444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tries</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502444#post502444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what reason could i have so that they arent always the leaders of the court?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attempting is not, for all intents and purposes, succeeding. Or, for that matter, motivating them to accept the gig. After all, if they accept the gig, they're liable to lose Clarity. They're aware of this burden. It says something about the kind of Fairest that take the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:02:05-07:00","id":502541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502287#post502287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Associating hero with beauty is... problematic to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take it up with the Wyrd. Faerie tales predate modern sensibilities. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502455#post502455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the mechanics make them attractive. That used to come from their glamour fueled Blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The kith write up does make the Fairest seem attractive.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:05:31-07:00","id":502546,"title":"","content":"As I said, they sounds like Ventrues: believing themselves as the only ones fit with the capacity to handle the power and responsability of leadership... Whatever It's true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:29:45-07:00","id":502554,"title":"","content":"I don't see the Fairest as natural leaders... They're the changelings flung into positions where the others are expecting them to lead, either as ones who escaped with the Fairest from Arcadia on that one fateful day or just due to the Seeming itself and how it is gained. Their Blessing activates essentially when they blag or fast-talk a decision... Their Curse reinforces this where it comes in when people get hurt from these spur of the moment decisions. These are people woefully unprepared for a role that's been thrust upon them by taking agency in one specific moment of time and they're being remembered for it and a repeat performance is expected. Maybe it just comes down to that they're the prettiest one about, people put their trust in them down to their looks and now they have to follow through because the house of cards is going to tumble if they don't do something.<br /> They're not natural leaders, if anything they're battlefield promotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:36:31-07:00","id":502555,"title":"","content":"So you are saying, like I mentioned as a possibility few posts ago, that unlike with other so far revealed Seemings Fairest chose a method of leadership as their escape and acts of leadership actually enforce and root them, like with the other Seemings ie the Darklings chose to escape by doing a hard choice and are empowered by doing the same in the future, but unlike the otehr Seemings these same acts of leadership drive them to low Clarity, that is unlike with others with whom enforcing and living again their choice of escape (that is their Seemings archetype) also acts as a foil to their Curse but with the Fairest it actually drives forward their Curse. <br /> <br /> What I mean is that when a Darkling makes a hard choice and gains Clarity he will not be subject to his Curse. When a Beast breaks Taboo at a personal cost to gain Clarity he is again not automatically within the purview of his Curse, actually such acts of freedom are the exact opposite of their Curse, even if breaking such a Taboo may cause them to get undue official scrutiny that could perhaps lead to incarceration thus triggering the Curse. But when a Fairest takes up the task of leadership and regains Clarity he is almost certainly, really in an RPG when does a PC's plan ever go so perfectly as to not cause any collateral damage, visited with his Curse for the exact same action causing him to suffer a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> See the difference? All that I am asking is consistency. Either change the Darklings and the Beast Curses so that they too trigger at the same acts, ie the hard choice only counts if you do it in blind trust of someone else, and the Taboo breaking only counts if the great cost to yourself is being captured or tied with Oaths or, in my mind a better option, just change the Fairest Curse to go along with the rest so that it doesn't trigger from the same act that triggers the Blessing. Like said I would much more prefer something like what I suggested, poorly thought out as it was, and refine it so that it touches more of the question <i>who's the fairest of them all </i>if the answer is you your golden if not then the Curse hits. And personally to me even the Blessing enforced leadership role is just a throwback to the Sidhe, whom I admit to loving, so perhaps both should be revisited.<br /> <br /> And since Filamena has told us the prize, if that option is still on the table, I can easily pay the 3-10$ that it would cost to rewrite one or both of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally I think the Fairest should be about beauty and madness instead of leadership.<br /> <br /> Perhaps their method of escape should be that they had to accept the madness of the Faerie, to think like a Gentry so to speak, to succeed and so their have as a Blessing the <i>Clarity of a Broken Mirror</i>. The Fairest find surprising Clarity from seeming madness when the character gives in and seeks to think like the Gentry to resolve an issue he feels revived by his incursion into insanity so familiar to his former Keeper. Their Curse could then be something like the <i>Land of the Blind</i>. The Fairest are the one eyed man seeing the world as it is, a mad place governed by rules and Oaths most are completely unaware of, and it acts as a hard reminder of how different they are of from the blind that cling to them for company, leadership and attention. Fairest naturally gather people around them yet are acutely aware of how different, how separated, they are from them. Their are subject to Clarity Break when they forget this difference and seek to abandon the madness of the Faerie to be like them. Thus the Fairest must stay aloof of others so as not to close their eyes and join their blind ranks, when they allow others to truly see them as they are and they open themselves to another they suffer from the effects of this Curse such openness was the surest way to allow the Gentry to dig their claws in after all.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps their Blessing should simply be <i>Thou art fairer than all who are here</i>. The Fairest gain a free dot of Clarity when they use their awe inspiring looks to steal away the scene from someone else, for example by stealing the leadership role despite having no claim to it simply through the fact that you are clearly the Fairest of them all or usurping the spotlight from and stealing the credit for the work of your sage etc. Where as the Curse should then be <i>But more beautiful still is...</i> The Fairest suffer from their Curse when they find themselves usurped of their status and spotlight or when they are proven to be nothing more than a pretty face, should another Fairest usurp them as befits their Blessing or should they make themselves seen as a laughing stock and loose credibility they suffer a Clarity Break for it.<br /> <br /> I'll freely admit that I only put a few minutes of thought into these and that they could be much deeper and more refined but as examples I think they do an adequate job of presenting alternative ways to see the Fairest that differ from the leadership role given here even though both, especially the latter, also encompasses the leadership concept but neither is limited by it.<br /> <br /> Just throwing ideas as that is I think the idea of open development. I just feel that since the responses here suggest that most of those who liked the Fairest in 1st ed seem discouraged by their 2nd ed incarnation then perhaps it should be re-thought a bit even if that re-thinking only result in you deciding to keep the change from beauty and madness into leadership in place. So please do not get defensive about it, I know how easy that is when concerning your own material, but try to look at it from a more aloof place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:52:11-07:00","id":502562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502555#post502555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing ideas as that is I think the idea of open development. I just feel that since the responses here suggest that most of those who liked the Fairest in 1st ed seem discouraged by their 2nd ed incarnation then perhaps it should be re-thought a bit even if that re-thinking only result in you deciding to keep the change from beauty and madness into leadership in place. So please do not get defensive about it, I know how easy that is when concerning your own material, but try to look at it from a more aloof place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assure you, I'm doing a LOT of thinking about this material. Otherwise, I wouldn't post it online and wade through pages of comments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:54:38-07:00","id":502564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or perhaps their Blessing should simply be <i>Thou art fairer than all who are here</i>. The Fairest gain a free dot of Clarity when they use their awe inspiring looks to steal away the scene from someone else, for example by stealing the leadership role despite having no claim to it simply through the fact that you are clearly the Fairest of them all or usurping the spotlight from and stealing the credit for the work of your sage etc. Where as the Curse should then be <i>But more beautiful still is...</i> The Fairest suffer from their Curse when they find themselves usurped of their status and spotlight or when they are proven to be nothing more than a pretty face, should another Fairest usurp them as befits their Blessing or should they make themselves seen as a laughing stock and loose credibility they suffer a Clarity Break for it. </div> </div> </div>I would hope this wouldn't happen... It would be a field-day for all the powerplayers out there who like to take control of the troupe and be the 'Big I Ams'. Scene-stealing is bad... and that curse is just an invite for some spiteful revenge tactics by other players to get their own back.<br /> <br /> For the record, I've played Fairest in 1e and I happen to like the new take on them for 2e in the draft shown. That they're now classed as fairest for something than they did and must continue to masquerade as rather than just because they're the pretty ones and favoured ones is a good move in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T00:23:19-07:00","id":502603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> be the 'Big I Ams' </div> </div> </div>Though this is what the Fairest in Faery Tails actually are either the big villains, aka the Evil Queen, or the heroes, aka Prince Charming or Snow-White. They are the Big I Am's.<br /> <br /> But that aside that was like the third suggestion I had in this thread and I admit all of them may have plenty of kinks to smooth over but consider that they have been cobbled together in the time it took me to type out my thoughts so no deep thoughts there. I just personally find the current 2nd edition version so far from the one we had, and hate the fact that one cannot play the Evil Queen as fairest anymore without bleeding Clarity like nothing else. Just throwing alternate ideas in the hopes that one of them inspires the writers and they, or I if they asked me, could refine the very rough draft I give here.<br /> <br /> The thing is in my opinion the Fairest should be able to play both the Hero and the Villain they should be able to portray both the Evil Queen, who let's face it was the Fairest of them all, and Snow-White, whom became the Fairest of them all. Currently I can only play one of them without bleeding out my Clarity. I don't want people to feel boxed in by the Seemings, like I didn't feel with the Beast or the Darklings whose Blessings and Curses work fine for a multitude of Characters, including both Dark Kings and Heroes alike. I can play a Darkling Hero, though with trust issues, as easily as I could play Darkling King or a Darkling Assassin. Similar is true of Beast. But with the Fairest I am kinda forced to be the Hero and absolutely forced to be such if taking up a leadership position. It seems too restrictive of a Seeming to me currently and like I said it's Blessing and Curse are, in my opinion, inconsistent with those of other Seemings.<br /> <br /> Finally I would like to add that stealing spotlight can be done in a non-offensive manner without disrupting a game if such disruptions are common no amount of game mechanics are going to prevent it and it's a problem player and the solution is usually to speak about it with them outside the game. For example in our current, long running, Aberrant game my character is the groups leader, or rather it's face, and so I pretty much take all the credit when we succeed but on the flip side I also take all the blame when we mess up and we only play the blame game within the group never in public. I wouldn't do this if it wasn't okay for the whole group tho, that is the players as their characters of course sometimes have other opinions about my actions. In other games I have been more than happy to let other players take the credit while I have stayed in the background, it all depends on the character one is playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T00:30:22-07:00","id":502607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502287#post502287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Associating hero with beauty is... problematic to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>That's</i> problematic, but it's perfectly OK to associate a bestial appearance with taboo-breaking? If I think someone looks creepy, I should assume they're treasonous and incapable of trusting others? Arcadia works off fairy tale logic and stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T01:01:40-07:00","id":502612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502603#post502603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and hate the fact that one cannot play the Evil Queen as fairest anymore without bleeding Clarity like nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. If you get people (your people or theirs) hurt on purpose then it's fine. If you screw up and do it by accident you have a breaking point.<br /> <br /> So Evil Queens are good to go. Hopefully the rewording makes that completely clear.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T01:13:00-07:00","id":502613,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, balancing one dot of Clarity 'once per story' versus potentially limitless Clarity loss checks suggests you should avoid a long term position of leadership altogether.<br /> <br /> As an aside, of the people who've played changeling, did your motleys have leaders? Or was it more of a democratic/collaborative group thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T01:41:48-07:00","id":502621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502612#post502612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can. If you get people (your people or theirs) hurt on purpose then it's fine. If you screw up and do it by accident you have a breaking point.<br /> <br /> So Evil Queens are good to go. Hopefully the rewording makes that completely clear.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot, point maid clearer by the nofather above, without bleeding Clarity. Also you can be a successful leader and your plans work to your and your peoples benefit even when there are unfortunate collateral damage, as that is often result of something unpredictable happening. Unless of course you can avoid said Clarity breaking points by adding a clause of &quot;do so no matter the cost or collateral damage&quot; to all orders is enough for them to become purposeful hurtings.<br /> <br /> There are millions of things no-one, except a movie villain who has the script, can account for that can cause collateral damage and get people hurt. You give a simple order that slightly changes things and someone get's hurt and you are struck by the Curse. Let's say you order the capture of a criminal and unbeknowst to anyone that criminal has given a certain percentage of his ill begotten gains to an orphanage he grew in and that small contribution has helped keep the place afloat. Now by your order the criminal is capture and punished as he should but the orphanage goes under causing much grief for a lot of people, and emotional hurt is part of the Curse, and you are struck by the Curse. There was literally no way to know this would happen especially if even the orphanage didn't know who their mystery benefactor was. Still it was your leadership that lead there and therefore you are in for a Clarity Break and this is even true despite the fact that you are an Evil Queen who could have ordered the damn orphans to be burned alive without batting an eyelid. The point here being that even hurting people you care absolutely nothing about, since you know evil tyrant and all, triggers the Curse. It makes any Fairest taking up a leadership position bleed Clarity at an unprecedented rate, especially PC Fairest who have no plot protection, like the scripted villains on TV, or ST shenanigans, like NPC villains. You know how every ST guide always tells ST's to cheat when the players seem to crack their master minds plots, cheat in a way that the ST behind the scenes and unseen by players changes how the NPC has prepared for the encounter taking into account the idea players came up with, with ease to protect the plot. Well such behaviour now automatically tends to result in Fairest being hit with their Curse if they are in a leadership position even if it would be the best for the game as a whole. Tell me how often have you seen a PC plan to work exactly as planned? With no collateral damage whatsoever? In over two decades I have never seen that to be the case, not once<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> For a little additional food for thought how often do you think real life leadership roles tend to work without accidentally hurting anyone? Even in a benevolent environment of a workplace, no supernatural problems and no wartime leadership is needed for this to be true, every time the boss has to put his foot down someone is likely to get hurt somewhere and I'd like to think these things weren't calculated evils perpetrated by said bosses but rather unintentional collateral damage. For example at my work place two people wanted to trade shifts to accommodate their out of work schedules the boss agreed to this and gave her permission but also added that due to the shift the other worker had to do a very specific job on her new shift, the boss didn't think much about it as it was just common sense decision to her but the worker was devastated she stressed over it loosing sleep and messing up her off-weekend. She got hurt by that act of leadership even though it bore no ill-intent and the boss had no idea she would become so stressed over that. See? Most Common sense acts of leadership may cause someone to get hurt emotionally if not physically and the Curse encompasses both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 05-04-2015, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T05:33:55-07:00","id":502794,"title":"","content":"I'd just shift the theme from Leadership to Idealization. Some Fairest might have people flock to them if they act leadery because people idealize them, for other Fairest who don't act in that way, maybe people treat them more like a rockstar or fashion model, and still others assume the Fairest.knows what.she's.talking about as long as she acts with confedence, even if she has no clue and no credentials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T06:42:28-07:00","id":502863,"title":"","content":"&quot;Leadership&quot; is definitely the problem key word here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:23:05-07:00","id":502881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502541#post502541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take it up with the Wyrd. Faerie tales predate modern sensibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm taking it up with the writers, who are deciding what the Wyrd is doing. &quot;Its fantasy!&quot; is no more an excuse for ignoring modern sensibilities than any other story out there, which uses &quot;its medieval fantasy&quot; as an excuse for sexism or racism. They can write whatever they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502607#post502607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That's</i> problematic, but it's perfectly OK to associate a bestial appearance with taboo-breaking? If I think someone looks creepy, I should assume they're treasonous and incapable of trusting others? Arcadia works off fairy tale logic and stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wrong on two counts with Beasts.<br /> <br /> All changelings can have a beastial appearance. That's up to the Keeper and Kith. So, trying to make an association is going to end up problematic because there's so many beastial fae that aren't Beasts. We have Wizened described with clockwork body parts - that doesn't make them Elementals either.<br /> <br /> Beasts are all about the mindset that doesn't quite fit into human culture; they have different drives than humans. This isn't fairy tale logic, its basic human logic. Non-human animals don't think or act like humans, but humans can think like many other animals. Beasts are, in part, shifting away from being a human animal.<br /> <br /> As for Darklings? They're defined by shadows and hiding, not being creepy. There's a difference. Darklings benefit from doing the necessary evil - maybe they decided to be an assassin when no one else would step up and kill the guy. That's not betrayal. They have problems trusting others - okay, that's why we have pledges, and betrayal is a common theme in Changeling. That's pragmetism.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Fairest? The write up flat out calls them (fallible) heroes. Their very name and the description in the kith area suggest beauty. There's no way around the association. &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fairest is a brilliant, shining, idealization.&quot; First words after the quote. Fairests are bright ideals. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502863#post502863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Leadership&quot; is definitely the problem key word here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I don't think leader isn't that much of a problem thematically. Contracts of Vainglory had, as its first level, the ability to act as if you were someone of high Status - a leader of some kind. A lot of the Vainglory powers did something similar. Most Fairest did benefit from acting like they were in charge in 1e due to how Vainglory worked.<br /> <br /> That said, in game, that's not necessarily going to put you in charge of others. A lot of leadership comes down to roleplaying style, not your choice of a splat. So...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-04-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:36:40-07:00","id":502939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502794#post502794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just shift the theme from Leadership to Idealization. Some Fairest might have people flock to them if they act leadery because people idealize them, for other Fairest who don't act in that way, maybe people treat them more like a rockstar or fashion model, and still others assume the Fairest.knows what.she's.talking about as long as she acts with confedence, even if she has no clue and no credentials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Idealization idea - your Blessing and Curse should be tide to you becoming epitome of the Archetype the Kith is putting you. This way Heroes are <i>Most Heroic of Them All</i> and Villians are <i>Most Wicked of Them All</i>. And still, people would flock too them, as they are paragons, soothing changlings souls. WITHOUT MARKING THEM ALL THE TIME LEADERS - just examplar to that people naturally tend too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-04-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:27:49-07:00","id":503000,"title":"","content":"Take for example (bear with me a sec) if Legolas from Lord of the Rings was a changeling. He's the epitome of a Fairest, but he's not the main figurehead of the books. He's pretty, he's witty, he's got maddog skills with a bow, but he's never in a position of leadership. He's a prince, sure, but he never commands anyone in the Motley (Fellowship), because he's not that kind of character.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though to be fair, durances often augment changelings to match their torment, which can sometimes be seen as poetically apropos, like a guy who lived like a pig his whole life comes back from Arcadia looking like one.<br /> <br /> P.S: Just wanted to say sorry if I came out antagonistic. Please don't hate me. :&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 05-04-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:08:05-07:00","id":503039,"title":"","content":"And I think Idealization can still be Agency - you were abused under you Lords and Ladies. You had unused potential, smathered by your abusers. And in the second of clariness, you understand &quot;I CAN DO IT!&quot; or &quot;WE CAN DO IT!&quot;. You understud you must be stronger, witter, smarter - more perfect - to win with Gentry. And so you become. But in the way, you become partially more like them. This is how I would see 2ED Fairest - and that would work with little chagnes with presantation of them in preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:11:40-07:00","id":503123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502881#post502881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong on two counts with Beasts.<br /> <br /> All changelings can have a beastial appearance. That's up to the Keeper and Kith. So, trying to make an association is going to end up problematic because there's so many beastial fae that aren't Beasts. We have Wizened described with clockwork body parts - that doesn't make them Elementals either.<br /> <br /> Beasts are all about the mindset that doesn't quite fit into human culture; they have different drives than humans. This isn't fairy tale logic, its basic human logic. Non-human animals don't think or act like humans, but humans can think like many other animals. Beasts are, in part, shifting away from being a human animal.<br /> <br /> As for Darklings? They're defined by shadows and hiding, not being creepy. There's a difference. Darklings benefit from doing the necessary evil - maybe they decided to be an assassin when no one else would step up and kill the guy. That's not betrayal. They have problems trusting others - okay, that's why we have pledges, and betrayal is a common theme in Changeling. That's pragmetism.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Fairest? The write up flat out calls them (fallible) heroes. Their very name and the description in the kith area suggest beauty. There's no way around the association. &quot;The Fairest is a brilliant, shining, idealization.&quot; First words after the quote. Fairests are bright ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in the Fairest description does it say they are beautiful physically. It's only in the kith example descriptions. Guess what? The Darkling example kiths are almost all creepy as heck. The Artist looks like a &quot;menacing, insect-like creature&quot;. The Coldscale specifically notes it is &quot;disturbing to look upon&quot;. Etc. As for the fact that some kiths have bestial characteristics, that's no more significant than the fact that the Nightsinger and Witchtooth always look scary and Iles are always beautiful by starlight. Or the fact that you can straight up say &quot;also my character is beautiful&quot; no matter your kith or seeming.<br /> <br /> The change in appearance you get from your Seeming works off fairy tale stereotypes. The one with themes of broken trust and betrayal makes you look dark and creepy. The one with themes of being outside social constraints makes you look like an animal. The one with themes of leadership and inspiration makes you look pleasant. Because in fairy tales, the hero(ine) is good looking, and someone who looks dark and creepy is probably untrustworthy. Note that I didn't say Darklings are untrustworthy. (Anymore than I've said you should trust Fairest.) But their defining thing was a &quot;hard choice&quot;, and they took that into their nature, and their appearance reflects it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 05-04-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:23:33-07:00","id":503174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503123#post503123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere in the Fairest description does it say they are beautiful physically. It's only in the kith example descriptions. Guess what? The Darkling example kiths are almost all creepy as heck. The Artist looks like a &amp;quot;menacing, insect-like creature&amp;quot;. The Coldscale specifically notes it is &amp;quot;disturbing to look upon&amp;quot;. Etc. As for the fact that some kiths have bestial characteristics, that's no more significant than the fact that the Nightsinger and Witchtooth always look scary and Iles are always beautiful by starlight. Or the fact that you can straight up say &amp;quot;also my character is beautiful&amp;quot; no matter your kith or seeming.<br /> <br /> The change in appearance you get from your Seeming works off fairy tale stereotypes. The one with themes of broken trust and betrayal makes you look dark and creepy. The one with themes of being outside social constraints makes you look like an animal. The one with themes of leadership and inspiration makes you look pleasant. Because in fairy tales, the hero(ine) is good looking, and someone who looks dark and creepy is probably untrustworthy. Note that I didn't say Darklings are untrustworthy. (Anymore than I've said you should trust Fairest.) But their defining thing was a &amp;quot;hard choice&amp;quot;, and they took that into their nature, and their appearance reflects it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh... You're not wrong, but when you say it like that it sounds awfully problematic... I guess that's part of the point of Changeling though, deconstructing the problematic aspects of the Fairy Tales it draws inspiration though. But that does make it all the more important for Fairest to be capable of being villanous and Darklings to be capable of being heroic, without going against their Seeming archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:48:10-07:00","id":503275,"title":"","content":"Far Darklings, it's not hard: the heroic ones are \u201cI'm getting my hands dirty so that nobody else has to.\u201d The question is, how to do a Fairest antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:08:15-07:00","id":503290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503275#post503275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far Darklings, it's not hard: the heroic ones are \u201cI'm getting my hands dirty so that nobody else has to.\u201d The question is, how to do a Fairest antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not hard either. It's not like all villains don't care about their underlings, or don't plan on them dying all the time. The leader cast of the Fairest does not solely lead them to nobility-the Fairest are just as inclined to lead with poisoned hearts and cursed whispers as anything else-but it does lead to a particular kind of villain/antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:17:25-07:00","id":503310,"title":"","content":"I will only point to Idealization post I made about how to make Fairest villians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502939#post502939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Idealization idea - your Blessing and Curse should be tide to you becoming epitome of the Archetype the Kith is putting you. This way Heroes are <i>Most Heroic of Them All</i> and Villians are <i>Most Wicked of Them All</i>. And still, people would flock too them, as they are paragons, soothing changlings souls. WITHOUT MARKING THEM ALL THE TIME LEADERS - just examplar to that people naturally tend too.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:22:18-07:00","id":503353,"title":"","content":"My only real comment on all of this stuff right now is &quot;Roll with it and see how it works.&quot; It's part of that buy in thing Black Hat Matt and Justin Achilli talk about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:24:04-07:00","id":503356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502939#post502939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with Idealization idea - your Blessing and Curse should be tide to you becoming epitome of the Archetype the Kith is putting you. This way Heroes are <i>Most Heroic of Them All</i> and Villians are <i>Most Wicked of Them All</i>. And still, people would flock too them, as they are paragons, soothing changlings souls. WITHOUT MARKING THEM ALL THE TIME LEADERS - just examplar to that people naturally tend too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Everybody loves a good villain. The way they seem to outmaneuver the heroes until the very end, the way they disguise themselves in a weaker form because they don't need their full power to deal with supporting cast, and they always get the best musical numbers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:31:16-07:00","id":503391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502939#post502939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with Idealization idea - your Blessing and Curse should be tide to you becoming epitome of the Archetype the Kith is putting you. This way Heroes are <i>Most Heroic of Them All</i> and Villians are <i>Most Wicked of Them All</i>. And still, people would flock too them, as they are paragons, soothing changlings souls. WITHOUT MARKING THEM ALL THE TIME LEADERS - just examplar to that people naturally tend too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Your Kith is something your Keeper forced upon you. Your seeming is how you broke free. Your Seeming shouldn't reinforce your Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:33:32-07:00","id":503393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503391#post503391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Your Kith is something your Keeper forced upon you. Your seeming is how you broke free. Your Seeming shouldn't reinforce your Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, yes, this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:09:48-07:00","id":503473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503391#post503391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Your Kith is something your Keeper forced upon you. Your seeming is how you broke free. Your Seeming shouldn't reinforce your Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha ha, it's what would They want you to belive... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or, you have 5/6 other Seemings to truly defy your Keeper's Kith. Fairest should be about playing in the game of Gentry and trying to win with them be being more... fairy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And outsmart your Fae master in it's play.<br /> <br /> I still think Idealisation could make logical and cool &quot;not so white only&quot; Agency that also sustain a bit of spirit of 1ed Fairest in 2ed. It also comes with now Leadership idea nicely, with not making all the Fairest &quot;good doers&quot;. Win-win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-04-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:32:10-07:00","id":503495,"title":"","content":"So in in an effort to improve upon one of my example Blessing/Curse pairings I tried to encompass the current leadership role, absorbing some of the idolization mentioned and tried to keep it all within the theme of Beauty and Madness. Still not the best of write ups and I am unhappy about the language but here goes nothing,<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: <i>Thou art fairer than all who are here</i>. Fairest escaped their Keepers thru guile, seduction and charm by proving themselves to be the fairest of them all. The truth is that confidence, beauty, and charm are all traits that make people heap expectations upon you. Any time the Fairest takes those expectations and runs with them using her charm, guile, and beauty to manipulate someone else into doing her task for her she reaffirms her sense of self. Once per story, a Fairest may manage a task through her fairness alone and she gains a point of Clarity for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse</b>: <i>But more beautiful still is...</i>Fairest sense of self is strongly anchored to how others see her. She needs to feel admired and looked upon for her counsel, even when she clearly isn't the best choice to give one. When the illusion of her fairness shatters, by her own hand or through others, so shatters her sense of self. If the fairest is shown to be a charlatan, fraud, or just plain incompetent to handle her tasks and is confronted about it she suffers a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> So the basic idea here is that the Fairest are inspiring, beautiful and/or charismatic enough to draw attention and the basics of the current write up stay, that is people tend to expect the Fairest to lead, counsel and be perfect at everything but should their plans fail and their efforts be foiled then they suffer for it, ever seen how villains take bad news when their minions fail to deliver that is the point of Clarity break here and for the heroic it plans failing usually, but not always, means someone got hurt which again is a Clarity breaking moment. It's not about the collateral damage but about their self-confidence, when the latter is rattled they risk loosing their Clarity. The main difference to the original Fairest write up is that the Curse does not care about people being hurt unintentionally or otherwise unless said consequence somehow makes the Fairest seem incompetent. So it wouldn't be a Clarity break, from the Curse, if a few innocents suffered if the plan as a whole worked and the larger benefits outweigh the minor suffering caused.<br /> <br /> Then again I am doing this in the middle of the night so I might not be at my best coherency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:47:44-07:00","id":503507,"title":"","content":"I'd say something like this would work better, capturing both the leadership and the beauty angle in a broader package of <i>image</i>:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: <i>Standing High Upon a Pedestal</i>. Fairest escaped their Keepers through seduction, persuasion, leadership, but ultimately by proving themselves to be the Fairest of them all. Once proven to be the Fairest, they are always the Fairest. People can see the Fariest's greatness, and expect her to live up to it. One who charmed her Keeper with pleasant conversation will hear the neighbours gossiping about how good company she is, even if she has never spoken more than a few words to anyone. A fairest who led his fellow slaves in revolution will find all eyes turning to him in a crisis. Once per story a fairest who lives up to her image and uses it to make others do as she wishes gains a point of Clarity for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse</b>: <i>Falling from a Height. </i>Moving on from Arcadia is hard for anyone, but the Fairest have an advantage. She may have forgotten how to trust or how to talk to other humans but her image shines before her. The script is easy to learn and the part is fun to wear, isn't Prince Charming better than Harold Smith anyway? The Fairest builds her new life upon the part she claimed in Arcadia, but what is easy for an hour is impossible to do for a life time. No one can be the perfect lady every hour of every day, eventually the changeling slips up and it feels as though the rug has been pulled from under her identity. Any time the Fairest cannot live up to her role she suffers a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can get something very similar to the original 2E Blessing or Curse by taking the image of leader; but you can get something very similar to 1E by taking the image of Dancer, or... most of the 1E Fairest Kiths really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-04-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:53:10-07:00","id":503515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503507#post503507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say something like this would work better, capturing both the leadership and the beauty angle in a broader package of <i>image</i>:<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: <i>Standing High Upon a Pedestal</i>. Fairest escaped their Keepers through seduction, persuasion, or leadership, but ultimately by proving themselves to be the fairest of them all. Once proven to be the fairest, they are always the Fairest of them all. People can see the Fariest's greatness, and expect her to live up to it. One who charmed her Keeper with pleasant conversation will hear the neighbours gossiping about how good company she is, even if she has never spoken more than a few words to anyone. A fairest who led his fellow slaves in revolution will find all eyes turning to him in a crisis. Once per story a fairest who lives up to her image and uses it to make others do as she wishes gains a point of Clarity for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse</b>: <i>Falling from a Height. </i>Moving on from Arcadia is hard for anyone, but the Fairest have an advantage. She may have forgotten how to trust or how to talk to other humans but her image shines before her. The script is easy to learn and the part is fun to wear, isn't Prince Charming better than Harold Smith anyway? The Fairest builds her new life upon the part she claimed in Arcadia, but what is easy for an hour is impossible to do for a life time. No one can be the perfect lady every hour of every day, eventually the changeling slips up and it feels as though the rug has been pulled from under her identity. Any time the Fairest cannot live up to her role she suffers a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can get something very similar to the original 2E Blessing or Curse by taking the image of leader; but you can get something very similar to 1E by taking the image of Dancer, or... most of the 1E Fairest Kiths really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, these are great. I would love something more along these lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:08:12-07:00","id":503532,"title":"","content":"Ack, now you've quoted it, it's pinned down and I can already see a flaw. (I'm implying seduction, persuasion, or leadership are the only three choices in the first sentence).<br /> <br /> More seriously: Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:19:51-07:00","id":503543,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think the martyr complex/control freak angle still works better than Raven's suggestion with the themes 2E is using. Issues with living up to expectations feels more like a direct result of abuse than a PTSD symptom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:59:14-07:00","id":503577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503543#post503543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think the martyr complex/control freak angle still works better than Raven's suggestion with the themes 2E is using. Issues with living up to expectations feels more like a direct result of abuse than a PTSD symptom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sold on Martyr Complex/Control Freak as the Fairest's expression of PTSD, though. I could probably come around to it, but I also don't see how the current Boon fits into that model - regaining Clarity when you encourage people to follow you in half-cocked kind of seems like the opposite of control freak to me. I like Raven's suggestion mostly because I can clearly see why their Boon would reinforce their sense of agency and why their Bane would be triggering. I don't see that in the versions in the draft yet, though the Bane is close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:39:11-07:00","id":503608,"title":"","content":"People seem hung up on the Fairest because of being unable to play the villian... Shouldn't the ST be handling them? Also, that type of Evil Queen role may fit better with one of the other Seemings not revealed yet. The Elemental perhaps, given what we can gather from them given the hints we've had so far.<br /> <br /> Fairest to me atm from the draft seem to have a kind of more Guilt Complex in how they see things... The Curse should really be reworded to clarify someone on their side of a decision made gets seriously injured, which has them keep Clarity more than what other people seem to be seeing here. It'd be really, really stupid if a Fairest leader in a war makes a decision and due to the other side getting injuries, they'd lose Clarity now, wouldn't it? I really don't think the draft was meaning that in it's wording.<br /> <br /> They seem to be the ones with anxiety... The ones who lead because it's expected of them and they feel guilt over each decision if something bad comes out of it for them or their people. Compare to the Darkling who puts no trust in their people and makes the hard decisions. Or the Beast who goes where they want and says and does what they want. Each could be a leader and all have their issues in being that person too. And every one could be The Evil Queen as much as the Kind Princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:43:56-07:00","id":503615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503608#post503608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem hung up on the Fairest because of being unable to play the villian... Shouldn't the ST be handling them? Also, that type of Evil Queen role may fit better with one of the other Seemings not revealed yet. The Elemental perhaps, given what we can gather from them given the hints we've had so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I saw them as iconic villains first when I read it. I was worried they were too cynical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:02:01-07:00","id":503630,"title":"","content":"Is that the Fairest or the Elementals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:59:34-07:00","id":503667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=502881#post502881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, I don't think leader isn't that much of a problem thematically. Contracts of Vainglory had, as its first level, the ability to act as if you were someone of high Status - a leader of some kind. A lot of the Vainglory powers did something similar. Most Fairest did benefit from acting like they were in charge in 1e due to how Vainglory worked.<br /> <br /> That said, in game, that's not necessarily going to put you in charge of others. A lot of leadership comes down to roleplaying style, not your choice of a splat. So...</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept itself is okay - it's the fact that 'leader' as a quality or word has too much OOC associated baggage. You say leader in text and people will subconsciously assume that they must be in charge of the motley/freehold/whatever.<br /> <br /> 1E Fairest feels a bit different - there's that obvious connect that using a contract to appear to be in charge is a short lived or flimsy facade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T18:23:05-07:00","id":503704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503667#post503667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept itself is okay - it's the fact that 'leader' as a quality or word has too much OOC associated baggage. You say leader in text and people will subconsciously assume that they must be in charge of the motley/freehold/whatever.<br /> <br /> 1E Fairest feels a bit different - there's that obvious connect that using a contract to appear to be in charge is a short lived or flimsy facade.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They brought back their seeming from the Fae realm, and with it, they brought back cruelty, and this cruelty is sometimes amplified by the arrogance that comes from knowing that they were pure enough of heart and strong enough of will to escape.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some manage, by sheer force of personality and charm alone, to rise to the top, but there are more Fairest in positions of authority than there are Fairest who know what they\u2019re doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wherever the Fairest find themselves, they\u2019re prominent. They push themselves into everything they do. Sometimes their undoubted charisma is enough to carry an enterprise on its own. Sometimes it isn\u2019t. But then, of all the changelings, the Fairest are the least suited to being alone. Although sometimes haughty, and sometimes cruel, they are social beings, and when they rise above their shortcomings, they work surpassingly well as part of a team.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;One stereotype among the Lost claims that every Fairest wishes to become an autocratic and lionized leader. However, while some do, there are a great many Fairest who have no interest in public power. Some Fairest would greatly prefer to become the power behind the throne of a freehold, rather than having to deal with the many difficulties of being the public face of power and authority. Also, despite what they might want, a great many Fairest never attain positions of leadership in a freehold, in part because many other changelings worry that Fairest are the ones most likely to abuse their power and neglect or ignore the needs and desires of other changelings.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1E Fairest were stereotyped as the Faces and People Persons of a given group. 2E Fairest appear to be carrying this over in a fashion that meshes with the decoupling and reversal of Seeming and Kith. It's not exactly a huge thematic change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T19:50:49-07:00","id":503739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503615#post503615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, I saw them as iconic villains first when I read it. I was worried they were too cynical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand, how can the Fairest be villains, or at least relatively stable-long-term villains, if anytime their actions as a leader results in someone being hurt, they risk Clarity? Is it meant to only refer to UNINTENTIONALLY (on the Fairest's part) hurt? Or only refer to the people specifically following their orders?<br /> <br /> Because if so that needs to be written into the fraility, because it's not what it currently says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T20:33:59-07:00","id":503758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503739#post503739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't understand, how can the Fairest be villains, or at least relatively stable-long-term villains, if anytime their actions as a leader results in someone being hurt, they risk Clarity? Is it meant to only refer to UNINTENTIONALLY (on the Fairest's part) hurt? Or only refer to the people specifically following their orders?<br /> <br /> Because if so that needs to be written into the fraility, because it's not what it currently says.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three words.<br /> <br /> Gentleman John Marcone.<br /> <br /> Two more?<br /> <br /> Totally Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T21:17:31-07:00","id":503773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503758#post503758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three words.<br /> <br /> Gentleman John Marcone.<br /> <br /> Two more?<br /> <br /> Totally Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>His organization hurts others on a regular basis. With the fraility written as it currently is, he'd quickly lose all his Clarity. If it only applies to people following your orders being hurt by them, the Fraility needs to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T21:22:45-07:00","id":503775,"title":"","content":"Of course even if we assume the frailty only applies to those following your orders being hurt as a result, it does mean no Fairest can ever command in a war. Ever! Without hemoragging all of their Clarity..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T21:23:55-07:00","id":503781,"title":"","content":"I place money on this fitting the idea, so if that's grounds for text clarity, then so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T21:45:46-07:00","id":503809,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about the character.<br /> <br /> And a lot of people seem to be working off of more information than exists in the peeks we've gotten, so some of us are working with a few pieces of a puzzle that don't seem to fit together. An issue should probably be expanded upon. Is Clarity guilt, now? It doesn't seem to be, so what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-05-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:21:41-07:00","id":503827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503809#post503809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind spoilers, you can learn more from his <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dresden_Files_characters#.22Gentleman.22_Johnny_Marcone\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia subsection</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a lot of people seem to be working off of more information than exists in the peeks we've gotten, so some of us are working with a few pieces of a puzzle that don't seem to fit together. An issue should probably be expanded upon. Is Clarity guilt, now? It doesn't seem to be, so what is it? </div> </div> </div>It's not yet clear what changes are in store for Clarity, but I suspect it's similar to 1e, measuring one's sense of stability and groundedness.<br /> <br /> The impression I get is that the Seeming Blessing gives a Clarity because the Changeling does what she did when she gained that Seeming and took back control of her life: it reaffirms to herself that she <i>is </i>in control, and thereby grants her a greater sense of stability. The Seeming Curse instead reminds her of when she wasn't in control,* and thus deals her stability a blow.<br /> <br /> * A Beast getting forcibly denied the freedom she took back, a Darkling placing complete trust in someone in the manner that got her betrayed, a Fairest not measuring up to high standards she set, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T23:55:16-07:00","id":503886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503739#post503739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand, how can the Fairest be villains, or at least relatively stable-long-term villains, if anytime their actions as a leader results in someone being hurt, they risk Clarity? Is it meant to only refer to UNINTENTIONALLY (on the Fairest's part) hurt? Or only refer to the people specifically following their orders?<br /> <br /> Because if so that needs to be written into the fraility, because it's not what it currently says.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was address in post #31.<br /> <br /> Yes, it needs to be addressed in revisions; but we're seeing the first draft. The author has stated the intent is that the Clarity risk is only if the harm is accidental/unintentional/collateral in nature.<br /> <br /> If the Fairest's plans are to go out and kill someone, and they accomplish that, they don't risk Clarity (at least no more than any other changeling would for doing that). If one of the members of the assault force kills an innocent bystander for seeing them, and that wasn't part of the Fairest's plans/orders, then Clarity could get risked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T00:05:59-07:00","id":503896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503886#post503886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Fairest's plans are to go out and kill someone, and they accomplish that, they don't risk Clarity (at least no more than any other changeling would for doing that). If one of the members of the assault force kills an innocent bystander for seeing them, and that wasn't part of the Fairest's plans/orders, then Clarity could get risked.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this was mention on 1st page of topic - those scenarios almost ALWAYS result in the Clarity loss, as we are playing RPG game here. Every time something goes wrong, or some bystander dies. Even just because ST need a twist in the plot when the game session is in still. That's why it's bad Curse - it will in play penalty player for not being ST himself. He is not TV scripted villains that can precognitive everything. I much more would be okay with Curse that make you Breaking Point for playing like the Others - but still it would be blow to Fairest as villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T00:12:33-07:00","id":503898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503608#post503608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem hung up on the Fairest because of being unable to play the villian... Shouldn't the ST be handling them? Also, that type of Evil Queen role may fit better with one of the other Seemings not revealed yet. The Elemental perhaps, given what we can gather from them given the hints we've had so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Seeming should be possible to be played as heroes or villians. The Gentry are not the worse enemies of Lost - sometimes, it's other changelings. Tyrannical Freehold leaders, devious Courts Royalty, evil contacts, even Lost that forge you this ID that sell you to your Court rivals - they all should be possible concepts in the framework of Seemings. Maybe I'm mistaken in game design, but Changeling game should be have villains even if no True Fae or Hedge being shown in game session. And that means the Fairest should also be possible to run as villains, no only heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T00:51:42-07:00","id":503909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503739#post503739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if so that needs to be written into the fraility, because it's not what it currently says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's going to be written into the frailty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T01:53:00-07:00","id":503970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503781#post503781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I place money on this fitting the idea, so if that's grounds for text clarity, then so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I think maybe it was written assumptively. I know when I read it, it didn't even occur to me that it could apply to those aside from &quot;your side&quot;. I'll make sure it's clarified; it should only be those under your charge. Not your targets. Bystanders would count, though. So, I guess maybe the wording will have something to do with unintentional vs intentional harm. If the plan is literally to harm someone, that person is not going to force Clarity breaking points (inherently, of course it might be under other circumstances). <br /> <br /> And re: war, I'll note that suffering breaking points is not identical to losing Clarity. A Fairest warlord is liable to have a low Clarity, but it doesn't inherently mean she'll lose it all, any more than mortal mass murderers lose all their Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T02:17:25-07:00","id":504001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503896#post503896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this was mention on 1st page of topic - those scenarios almost ALWAYS result in the Clarity loss, as we are playing RPG game here.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this remains a poor assumption. The 2e breaking points systems so far have made if likely that PCs will pass breaking point checks more often than not. We don't know the specifics of Clarity yet, but if it works like Integrity, have 5-6 dice means that most of the time you don't fail the roll, so you don't lose Clarity.<br /> <br /> The idea that these scenarios will almost always put Clarity at risk is a very different point that these scenarios will always result in Clarity loss.<br /> <br /> This distinction is especially important with the Seemings also providing ways to guaranteed Clarity gains. If you are getting your automatic gain as frequently as the dice are failing on you and resulting in loses, you're netting even; not a net loss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every time something goes wrong, or some bystander dies. </div> </div> </div>There is a fairly massive gap between &quot;something goes wrong,&quot; and &quot;someone is unintentionally caused significant harm;&quot; the second being the actual Curse and such. Plans simply not going 100% as intended isn't an issue. Plans not going as intended and bystanders needing to be dealt with isn't inherently an issue either. If you have a way to incapacitate an unexpected bystander without causing them serious harm, then no risk of Clarity loss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even just because ST need a twist in the plot when the game session is in still. </div> </div> </div>Poor STing doesn't mean the rule in question is bad. If things like drug trips can still risk Clarity, and the ST constantly smacks the changelings with drugs via plot until they're all Clarity 0, that's not an issue with Clarity. That's just bad STing. It's no different from sending wave after wave of combat enemies until the PCs are all dead. Sure you can do it in the rules, but that's not the problem. If the ST is constantly pulling &quot;Gotcha! You didn't plan for X so roll for a Clarity break!&quot; then the problem is the ST. Because they can do this without Seeming specific ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T02:59:06-07:00","id":504011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503970#post503970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess maybe the wording will have something to do with unintentional vs intentional harm. If the plan is literally to harm someone, that person is not going to force Clarity breaking points (inherently, of course it might be under other circumstances).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one issue but there's a second one to worry about.<br /> <br /> If you say to 10 people, grab some guns and fight those 10 people. Then obviously you're not intending to harm your people but you know they're going to get hurt. So if your guys win the fight, but 3 of them die, that went according to plan and shouldn't cost Clarity.<br /> <br /> So rather than unintentional vs intentional - maybe success vs failure. &quot;If the Fairest's plan fails and someone gets hurt as a result&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T06:18:07-07:00","id":504094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=503898#post503898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Seeming should be possible to be played as heroes or villians. The Gentry are not the worse enemies of Lost - sometimes, it's other changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Gentry aren't the worst enemies of the Lost in 2e, it seems anyways. Its the Huntsmen. Plus, I imagine that Loyalists are still around, if they're not part of the Huntsmen, and I don't know if Loyalists will need Seemings. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T08:47:04-07:00","id":504194,"title":"","content":"Odds are I won't be getting into a mass combat game of changeling but I can see the problems for those who might.<br /> <br /> As a player in a motley, what constitutes leadership? We don't have a 'group leader,' but if one member asks, 'What should we do?' does the Fairest make themselves eligible by offering their opinion the way every other player might? And if the fairest's idea is followed, would players be more reluctant to take a Dramatic Failure, knowing it might cripple a member of the motley? Or would players simply not ask the fairest's opinion, an option I could see taken in more gamist groups?<br /> <br /> Our changeling group wasn't really much in the way of backstabby, but I could see the current curse really urging the fairest player to simply not participate in decision making. And it wouldn't even be against character, since the seeming is supposed to be reluctant leaders. Opting out is a sure way to show reluctance and as we've already established 1 Clarity per story versus Potentially Infinite Clarity Breaks is not a good gamble.<br /> <br /> As for Gentleman John, he doesn't seem shaken by anything. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonny_Corinthos\" target=\"_blank\">Sonny Corinthos</a> might be a better example, as extreme aspects of his bipolar disorder are often triggered during tense times when his leadership and hard choices are constantly required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:01:54-07:00","id":504208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504094#post504094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Gentry aren't the worst enemies of the Lost in 2e, it seems anyways. Its the Huntsmen. Plus, I imagine that Loyalists are still around, if they're not part of the Huntsmen, and I don't know if Loyalists will need Seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strangers <i>are</i> the worst enemies of the Lost, but they're taking more of a backseat. Their presence is felt everywhere, but there's less need for them to be on screen. When they do arrive, it's &quot;OH FUCK&quot; time.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen are bigger deals because they're on the ground and the <s>biggest</s> craftiest things you are likely to run into. At least, this seems to be the design at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-05-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:19:58-07:00","id":504361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504194#post504194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odds are I won't be getting into a mass combat game of changeling but I can see the problems for those who might.<br /> <br /> As a player in a motley, what constitutes leadership? We don't have a 'group leader,' but if one member asks, 'What should we do?' does the Fairest make themselves eligible by offering their opinion the way every other player might? And if the fairest's idea is followed, would players be more reluctant to take a Dramatic Failure, knowing it might cripple a member of the motley? Or would players simply not ask the fairest's opinion, an option I could see taken in more gamist groups?<br /> <br /> Our changeling group wasn't really much in the way of backstabby, but I could see the current curse really urging the fairest player to simply not participate in decision making. And it wouldn't even be against character, since the seeming is supposed to be reluctant leaders. Opting out is a sure way to show reluctance and as we've already established 1 Clarity per story versus Potentially Infinite Clarity Breaks is not a good gamble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really the best approach, if the group wants to be gamist about it, would be to let the Fairest take the lead (with no real plan in mind) once per story. That's a guaranteed +1 Clarity, and if things do go pair shaped, it's only a Breaking Point. You've got a pretty good chance of succeeding the roll, and even if you fail, it's a wash at worst. Then don't let the fairest lead again until next story.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, if that's how some groups want to play it, that's fine. I'd rather decisions be made based on what suits the game's themes than on trying to prevent other groups from having badwrongfun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:33:38-07:00","id":504433,"title":"","content":"I feel like a group who does that is playing into Changeling's themes and that it makes perfect thematic sense, even. No matter how much the terrible leader Fairest tries, she is just terrible at being a leader. Her Motley gives her chance after chance, but she blows it. Then some time later, because she instinctively <i>must</i> be the leader because of her seeming, they cave and let her try again. Who is she going to hurt this time? How does she deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:04:31-07:00","id":504479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504361#post504361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really the best approach, if the group wants to be gamist about it, would be to let the Fairest take the lead (with no real plan in mind) once per story. That's a guaranteed +1 Clarity, and if things do go pair shaped, it's only a Breaking Point. You've got a pretty good chance of succeeding the roll, and even if you fail, it's a wash at worst. Then don't let the fairest lead again until next story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great, providing high Clarity is a good thing. While it granted some bonuses in first edition, it also had you essentially having a breakdown and possibly receiving a derangement when confronted with 'Minor unexpected life changes' or such drastic acts as 'Entering the Hedge.' Which could leave you a gibbering wreck trying to deny your nature as a changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:09:37-07:00","id":504482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504479#post504479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's great, providing high Clarity is a good thing. While it granted some bonuses in first edition, it also had you essentially having a breakdown and possibly receiving a derangement when confronted with 'Minor unexpected life changes' or such drastic acts as 'Entering the Hedge.' Which could leave you a gibbering wreck trying to deny your nature as a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I assume it's going to be <i>mostly</i> a good thing, given that the ability to regain it is a Blessing. But I wouldn't be surprised if it came with drawbacks like it did in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:49:34-07:00","id":504520,"title":"","content":"Derangements were only when you dropped to 6 and under. At clarity 10 you're fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:04:49-07:00","id":504530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504520#post504520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Derangements were only when you dropped to 6 and under. At clarity 10 you're fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Close, it was 7. And you're not exactly fine, even without gaining derangements you're suffering breaking points over minor things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:12:18-07:00","id":504534,"title":"","content":"Breaking points which don't really do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:30:36-07:00","id":504542,"title":"","content":"A call for a breaking point is an indicator that something happened that's shaken up the character something fierce. It's still a big deal for the character, even absent a mechanical impact. If it wasn't, it wouldn't have been a breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T14:00:40-07:00","id":504614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504530#post504530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Close, it was 7. And you're not exactly fine, even without gaining derangements you're suffering breaking points over minor things.</div> </div> </div> </div>With fairly good odds of winning on those minor things.<br /> <br /> So, more or less fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T14:44:10-07:00","id":504660,"title":"","content":"Also, the idea that high Clarity changelings are gibbering messes from how easily their Clarity is challenged isn't really supported in how Clarity was described in 1e.<br /> <br /> While the challenges to their Clarity should have role-playing weight, all those relatively easy to pass high Clarity breaking points would be reaffirmations and strengthening of their Clarity as working; not a nightmare of frustration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:44:30-07:00","id":504688,"title":"","content":"Well that was a great sidetrack.<br /> <br /> So what is Clarity in second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:04:13-07:00","id":504784,"title":"","content":"Clarity is the Integrity equivalent stat for changelings in the Second Edition of Changeling the Lost. It reflects your grasp on what is real and what is everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:25:24-07:00","id":504834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504011#post504011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one issue but there's a second one to worry about.<br /> <br /> If you say to 10 people, grab some guns and fight those 10 people. Then obviously you're not intending to harm your people but you know they're going to get hurt. So if your guys win the fight, but 3 of them die, that went according to plan and shouldn't cost Clarity.<br /> <br /> So rather than unintentional vs intentional - maybe success vs failure. &quot;If the Fairest's plan fails and someone gets hurt as a result&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I want them to risk Clarity if someone on their team gets Whedoned, despite overall success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:29:42-07:00","id":504857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504834#post504834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I want them to risk Clarity if someone on their team gets Whedoned, despite overall success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that normally falls under basic Clarity loss. Sounds about right, too. People seeing their comrades burning, or worse, is a surefire way of getting PTSD. Don't think you have to be restricted to the fairest seeming to appreciate that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T18:20:59-07:00","id":504909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504857#post504857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that normally falls under basic Clarity loss. Sounds about right, too. People seeing their comrades burning, or worse, is a surefire way of getting PTSD. Don't think you have to be restricted to the fairest seeming to appreciate that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Where did PTSD come in to this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T18:29:28-07:00","id":504914,"title":"","content":"Post traumatic stress? Mental faculties deteriorate from experiencing abrupt moments of horror and pain, permanently scarring the fragile psyche of a changeling already tormented by their time in Arcadia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T18:42:43-07:00","id":504921,"title":"","content":"From previous posts, it doesn't sound like the Seeming based Clarity breaking points are meant to be exclusive to those Seemings. But we don't know the rules for them yet. If it works like Integrity, where it is more player defined, the Seeming Curses become inescapable ones. If Clarity is more like Humanity, there are ways to ensure they're distinctly worse for the Seemings even if any changeling would roll in a given circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:47:00-07:00","id":504950,"title":"","content":"Wild out-of-the-blue thought; but maybe Blessings and Curses should be thought of (and written) a bit like Virtues and Vices? Blessings already are: if you do this thing that reaffirms the core feature of your Seeming, you get a significant reward (your Clarity goes up by one). <br /> <br /> But the Curses? They're all built around telling the player that he's going to be punished further if he lets his character get into a particular adverse situation. Contrast with Vices (and, in a different way, Conditions) which <i>reward the player</i> for letting his character get into thematically appropriate trouble. Could the Seeming Curses maybe be reworked in a similar way? For instance: instead of (or in addition to) saying that the Fairest suffer a Clarity Breaking Point when someone under their care gets hurt because of the Fairest's actions, say that if the Fairest gains a Condition from a Clarity Break as a result of someone they're responsible for getting hurt, then resolving that Condition earns the Fairest a point of Glamour as well as (or instead of) a Beat of experience. It's still a Curse in that it's fundamentally tied to Bad Things Happening; but it uses a carrot approach to encourage players to get their characters into appropriate messes (or at least to compensate them for going along with the Storyteller when it hurts their character) rather than using a stick approach that causes them to shy away from such problems at all costs. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, that would require rewriting all six Curses; but I think it would be a 20% rewrite: the essence of the existing Curses could remain unchanged; only the game system effects backing them up would change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-05-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:58:00-07:00","id":504954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504011#post504011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rather than unintentional vs intentional - maybe success vs failure. &quot;If the Fairest's plan fails and someone gets hurt as a result&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes you wonder if that simply hones on the difference between Fae and Reality.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I don't understand.. This was supposed to work. IT'S SUPPOSE TO WORK!?&quot;<br /> <br /> Thorns of iron digging into a mind of flesh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T20:58:41-07:00","id":504988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504834#post504834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. I want them to risk Clarity if someone on their team gets Whedoned, despite overall success.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is exactly the problem, they really cannot act as villains if they have to care for their minions so much, similarly like said any player of a Fairest will likely choose that Seeming because they like the looks and such that it imparts and if taking a Seeming that's Blessing is about taking charge it's likely they would like to take charge then but the Curse implies the complete opposite here as it encourages one to never lead and never offer counsel on any matter. Really this Curse as it is makes the player paranoid about saying anything at all since if he says something that ends up as the plan, and like said even in the best RPGs under the best ST's the players plan has never to my experience worked exactly as planned (you know plot twists etc. similarly to how movies would be quite boring if they always went exactly to the protagonists plan) , or a part of a plan since it practically automatically involves a Clarity Break for them.<br /> <br /> What the Curse then becomes is incentive for the player to avoid taking part in the game and this is bad that is not what a Curse should do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:13:17-07:00","id":504998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504988#post504988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is exactly the problem, they really cannot act as villains if they have to care for their minions so much, similarly like said any player of a Fairest will likely choose that Seeming because they like the looks and such that it imparts and if taking a Seeming that's Blessing is about taking charge it's likely they would like to take charge then but the Curse implies the complete opposite here as it encourages one to never lead and never offer counsel on any matter. Really this Curse as it is makes the player paranoid about saying anything at all since if he says something that ends up as the plan, and like said even in the best RPGs under the best ST's the players plan has never to my experience worked exactly as planned (you know plot twists etc. similarly to how movies would be quite boring if they always went exactly to the protagonists plan) , or a part of a plan since it practically automatically involves a Clarity Break for them.<br /> <br /> What the Curse then becomes is incentive for the player to avoid taking part in the game and this is bad that is not what a Curse should do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're looking at breaking points as much more likely to be Clarity losses than they probably are, and you're looking at them as punishments, not things that add to the table. <br /> <br /> If players are going to play in such as a way as to avoid all potential loss, that's going to be very hard in a game of Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:38:16-07:00","id":505034,"title":"","content":"In Vampire The Requiem, you can't really experience the fullness of the game until you accept that you will inevitably fall.<br /> <br /> Changeling the Lost doesn't need an inevitablity factor, but someone has to step off the path in order to get back on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:50:45-07:00","id":505040,"title":"","content":"Is the Curse the only, or at least primary, way to lose Clarity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:01:38-07:00","id":505049,"title":"","content":"I'd say doubtful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:11:50-07:00","id":505054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504998#post504998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're looking at breaking points as much more likely to be Clarity losses than they probably are, and you're looking at them as punishments, not things that add to the table.<br /> <br /> If players are going to play in such as a way as to avoid all potential loss, that's going to be very hard in a game of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a relative, rather than an absolute thing.<br /> <br /> Someone playing a Beast or Darkling with the new curses will take a clarity check occasionally, and quite often the players can be taking them on their own terms.<br /> <br /> A player with a Fairest is just going to be eating clarity checks constantly if they're in some way involved in any form of leadership, command or authority. The only way to not have this happen is to withdraw - it punishes the player for having agency (And no, I'm not ignoring the serious part, it's obviously up to ST fiat, but that's what makes this so much more open ended - it'll be a complete ST call rather than player or mechanical calls with the other two seemings up).<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing the carrot that goes with the stick here. The beast/darkling curses encourage different behaviour - this just encourages no behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 05-06-2015, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:12:08-07:00","id":505055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504950#post504950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance: instead of (or in addition to) saying that the Fairest suffer a Clarity Breaking Point when someone under their care gets hurt because of the Fairest's actions, say that if the Fairest gains a Condition from a Clarity Break as a result of someone they're responsible for getting hurt, then resolving that Condition earns the Fairest a point of Glamour as well as (or instead of) a Beat of experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Clarity works like Integrity... this would already be how things work; baring glamour instead of beats (though I'd rather have the beats). I think part of the whole issue with the tangent on the Curse is that as the Curse relates to Clarity, and we don't have the new Clarity rules, we don't know how they interact. A lot of people seem to be assuming the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T22:23:00-07:00","id":505057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505055#post505055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Clarity works like Integrity... this would already be how things work; baring glamour instead of beats (though I'd rather have the beats).</div> </div> </div> </div>The bit about tying a Glamour reward to this isn't a side issue; it's the heart of what I'm suggesting: the fact that everything else is the same is a <i>feature</i>, not an oversight. And if \u201cinstead of\u201d means that you'd rather have the beats than the Glamour, make it \u201cin addition to\u201d. <br /> <br /> The point is to emphasize a \u201ccompensate the player for going along with Seeming-appropriate trouble\u201d approach over a \u201cpunish the player for getting into Seeming-appropriate trouble\u201d approach. The above was intended merely as an illustration of how it might work, not as an attempted mandate of \u201cyou must do it this particular way\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think part of the whole issue with the tangent on the Curse is that as the Curse relates to Clarity, and we don't have the new Clarity rules, we don't know how they interact. A lot of people seem to be assuming the worst. </div> </div> </div>If there's something relevant about the new Clarity rules, now would be a good time to mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-06-2015, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T00:34:57-07:00","id":505117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505054#post505054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone playing a Beast or Darkling with the new curses will take a clarity check occasionally, and quite often the players can be taking them on their own terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like an odd criticism of the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> The Beast Curse is the one that's mostly out of the character's hands. It comes up hardest if they are forced into confinement.<br /> <br /> The Darkling and Fairest Curses both require an actual choice on the part of the character to come up.<br /> <br /> The Fairest Curse is written such that it only comes up if the collateral damage was the result of a decision the Fairest made. It's not written that Fairest in positions of authority have to check their Clarity every time someone bad happens involving their subordinates and organization, but rather only when things go bad as a result of, or as a side effect of, a direct call the Fairest made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505057#post505057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit about tying a Glamour reward to this isn't a side issue;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it is. Your suggestion is predicated on the assumption that there's no mechanical carrot (such as Conditions that lead to Beats) with Clarity Breaking point checks, so there needs to be additional carrots added to the system to avoid the feeling of punishment (though these are called Curses, not everything needs a carrot, some things are just bad for the character; there's no carrot for vampires that take damage from banes). What's this assumption actually based on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there's something relevant about the new Clarity rules, now would be a good time to mention it. </div> </div> </div>Probably. But that assumes they're ready for presentation to us. This is open development, and it seems largely predicated on what first drafts are done. These aren't sneak peaks of a finished work we're getting teased with. Useful feedback on what we're seeing can't include assumptions about a part of the system we haven't seen yet taken to the negative extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T00:50:42-07:00","id":505125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505117#post505117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like an odd criticism of the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> The Beast Curse is the one that's mostly out of the character's hands. It comes up hardest if they are forced into confinement.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still involves player decision outside of ST fiat and ST fiat ruins everything, ever :P . For some simple examples: Running from the police rather than co-operating with them for questioning. Refusing to pledge to a Court Monarch to allay suspicion. The curse is going to come into play as a consequence of actions taken that are likely to end up butting against their nature, rather than encouraging complete inaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Darkling and Fairest Curses both require an actual choice on the part of the character to come up.<br /> <br /> The Fairest Curse is written such that it only comes up if the collateral damage was the result of a decision the Fairest made. It's not written that Fairest in positions of authority have to check their Clarity every time someone bad happens involving their subordinates and organization, but rather only when things go bad as a result of, or as a side effect of, a direct call the Fairest made. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. So the Fairest are rewarded for not making calls. What incentive is there to make direct calls? So you don't get the blessing (which feels a bit vague as has been mentioned previously, but that's not really here nor there) but you don't run the risk of 'side effects' happening. It's WoD. When do side effects NOT happen?<br /> <br /> Edit: Haha, my Wife just read through the three seeming previews and commented: &quot;Holy crap, the Fairest Curse is heinous unless you've got an incredibly permissive ST&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 05-06-2015, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:32:18-07:00","id":505159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505125#post505125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some simple examples: Running from the police rather than co-operating with them for questioning. Refusing to pledge to a Court Monarch to allay suspicion. The curse is going to come into play as a consequence of actions taken that are likely to end up butting against their nature, rather than encouraging complete inaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... in your WOD the police are all 100% by the book and never arrest people because they can? Or a Court Monarch never decides to use the new guy as a scapegoat even though they didn't actually do anything wrong?<br /> <br /> You're going on about how the WOD somehow obligates the ST to have every call a Fairest leader makes go sideways in a fashion that forces them to make a Clarity check, but at the same time saying that a Beast that's in a position where they have to talk to the cops will never end up arrested even if they don't do anything wrong.<br /> <br /> It seems extremely inconsistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exactly. So the Fairest are rewarded for not making calls. What incentive is there to make direct calls? So you don't get the blessing (which feels a bit vague as has been mentioned previously, but that's not really here nor there) but you don't run the risk of 'side effects' happening. It's WoD. When do side effects NOT happen? </div> </div> </div>Fairest are rewarded for making calls because leaders that don't make calls don't stay leaders with all the perks of power that entails (and the Blessing). If leadership was a purely horrible thing that nobody wanted a piece of... we wouldn't fight over power so damned much.<br /> <br /> And no, the WOD does not require a side effect happened every time. Nor will every side effect will trigger the Fairest Curse either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Haha, my Wife just read through the three seeming previews and commented: &quot;Holy crap, the Fairest Curse is heinous unless you've got an incredibly permissive ST&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'm curious if you bothered pointing out the clarification made about the collateral issue to her.<br /> <br /> My wife doesn't share you wife's reading. This probably isn't a big shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:50:46-07:00","id":505164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505159#post505159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... in your WOD the police are all 100% by the book and never arrest people because they can? Or a Court Monarch never decides to use the new guy as a scapegoat even though they didn't actually do anything wrong?<br /> <br /> You're going on about how the WOD somehow obligates the ST to have every call a Fairest leader makes go sideways in a fashion that forces them to make a Clarity check, but at the same time saying that a Beast that's in a position where they have to talk to the cops will never end up arrested even if they don't do anything wrong.<br /> <br /> It seems extremely inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, no putting words in my mouth. Don't be a jerk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fairest are rewarded for making calls because leaders that don't make calls don't stay leaders with all the perks of power that entails (and the Blessing). If leadership was a purely horrible thing that nobody wanted a piece of... we wouldn't fight over power so damned much.<br /> <br /> And no, the WOD does not require a side effect happened every time. Nor will every side effect will trigger the Fairest Curse either. </div> </div> </div>No, but the game gives us incentives to play in various ways. If we didn't want mechanical carrots and sticks we'd all just join theatre guilds and act out communal stories that way. There won't always be side effects, but saying there's unlikely to be thinks you didn't expect or predict is just hubris. I play with a group of incredibly empathetic, intelligent individuals who usually manage to suss out any plot I play, but even they can't always predict what I do with 100% accuracy. Nor I them. It's not realistic. Predicating a game mechanic on something like that just feels frustrating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm curious if you bothered pointing out the clarification made about the collateral issue to her. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I got a comment of &quot;Well, I suppose if they were a master tactician who could see EVERY eventuality it'd be okay. Still seems pretty harsh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 05-06-2015, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:01:19-07:00","id":505398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=504998#post504998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're looking at breaking points as much more likely to be Clarity losses than they probably are, and you're looking at them as punishments, not things that add to the table.<br /> <br /> If players are going to play in such as a way as to avoid all potential loss, that's going to be very hard in a game of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think a big part of the problem is that we don't really know anything at all about 2e Clarity. As things stand, though, most people I play with DO look at any kind of Integrity loss as &quot;losing&quot; in the same way that taking physical damage does. Certainly, in 1e, losing Clarity was really bad with its effect on perception. Hells, going below 5 robbed you of a Kenning, which was pretty useful. <br /> <br /> As well, there's a feeling that causing people to be hurt feels bad. I certainly get that impression. Now, if it makes you giggle-evil-cackle and stop caring about people and things like that? That's another matter.<br /> <br /> There's a pretty radical shift from 1e Humanity to 2e Humanity in vampire, I'd say. So, without seeing what Clarity is like now, I think its going to be a lot of assumptions dragged in from 1e. I really suspect part of the problem is that we're not seeing the whole picture. Seemings interact heavily with Clarity, so without that, we've got more questions. Seemings also flavor your Contracts, which do have an impact on play style, so that's another part of the puzzle we aren't seeing either. <br /> <br /> I suspect a large part of the problem comes down to not having all the information on a side. You know the saying about just enough information to be dangerous...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:26:20-07:00","id":505431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505159#post505159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... in your WOD the police are all 100% by the book and never arrest people because they can? Or a Court Monarch never decides to use the new guy as a scapegoat even though they didn't actually do anything wrong?<br /> <br /> You're going on about how the WOD somehow obligates the ST to have every call a Fairest leader makes go sideways in a fashion that forces them to make a Clarity check, but at the same time saying that a Beast that's in a position where they have to talk to the cops will never end up arrested even if they don't do anything wrong.<br /> <br /> It seems extremely inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div> Putting aside accusations of people running non-corrupt police forces in the WoD (hey, depends on how people run the game), all changelings have methods of innate methods of escape. Why would a scapegoat be put in prison when most changelings have an innate ability to escape? You'd probably need to heavily pin them down with iron to the point of torture. <br /> <br /> That changes the dynamic. A lot. <br /> <br /> And no, the WOD does not require a side effect happened every time. Nor will every side effect will trigger the Fairest Curse either.[/quote] Have you ever heard of the phrase &quot;no plan ever survives contact with the enemy?&quot; Its not the WoD requiring side effects from happening. Its REALITY. That's how things work in real life, let alone a story driven game where we all thrive on drama and unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> Its inevitable simply because that's the way things are. Its unrealistic to assume that it won't happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2015, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:31:48-07:00","id":505440,"title":"","content":"One of my big problems with the assumptions comes from the apparent high level of violence that happens in peoples games. Most people don't go out of their way for a fight, so it's not like someone getting hurt under the Fairest's direction is something that happens every other game.<br /> <br /> But maybe that's just my games.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And even on the emotional or mental damage front,that's more like a &quot;Crux of story&quot; thing, not a &quot;ZOMG EVERY GAME SESSION BRINGS THE HURT LOCKER OF THE HEART!&quot;<br /> <br /> Heh. &quot;Nothing I can say, a hurt locker of the heart&quot;. I'd pay to have someone make that work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-06-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:36:21-07:00","id":505452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Beast Curse is the one that's mostly out of the character's hands. It comes up hardest if they are forced into confinement.<br /> <br /> The Darkling and Fairest Curses both require an actual choice on the part of the character to come up. </div> </div> </div>While the Beast Curse seems like it's out of the characters hands it actually isn't, completely at least, as you can always try to avoid captivity and try to escape from your captors. OFten being a prisoner is a choice it's just that sometimes that choice is worth taking the hit on your Clarity. Also if the Beast ends up captured and confined once a session then it's one hell of a weird plot the ST is running or the ST is purposefully after the Beast or it's player.<br /> <br /> Darkling Curse makes you unable to fully trust anyone and it only comes to effect should you choose to trust. There is no other way for it to come up really, it's conpletely about a player choice unless some heavy mind/emotional control powers are being employed. This Curse will not show up often unless the Player want's it to.<br /> <br /> Also with both of the above avoiding the Curse does not in any way rob you of the possibility of using your Blessing. Avoiding capture, which most PC's are doing any way no one wants to be a prisoner, does not invalidate breaking taboo nor does being distrustful rob you of opportunities to make hard choices.<br /> <br /> Fairest Curse on the other hand can apply multiple times a session, and the only way the player can affect this outcome is by playing a withdrawn character who avoids leadership roles, does not give his counsel to anyone so that no one would act on his advice etc. Unlike with the other two Seemings this also means that the Fairest are the only Seeming, so far at least, that cannot utilize it's Blessing without risking the Curse automatically as well.<br /> <br /> But yes it is true that we know next to nothing about 2nd ed Clarity and I am willing to take all my words back if loosing it only means you become more like the Fae and are stronger in those aspects of your character instead of it being punitive like loosing it was in 1st ed. That is to say if loosing Clarity leads to interesting characters that can faster evolve into the Gentry themselves then I'm cool with that, though I suspect this is still tied to Wyrd instead of Clarity loss. That is to say if it's more of a scale, a bit like with Werewolf 2n ed, about whether you are closer to Fae or Humans then it might not matter, I might even enjoy playing a character who bleeds Clarity like the current Fairest seem to, but if it is more like Integrity or Humanity where it is a slow descent into becoming an NPC that limits your pools and stacks negative effects on you then this state of the Fairest is quite unacceptable compared to the other two Seemings.<br /> <br /> So Beast Blessing and Curse both encourage the player to be proactive, doing things and making sure they stay free to do more things.<br /> <br /> Darkling Blessing encourages making hard decisions which in itself is very proactive, being distrustful of everyone is a personality trait that will likely end up as increasing PC activity as well since he has to act more to find things out for himself, being distrustful of others and all.<br /> <br /> So both Seemings encourage people to go out and do things.<br /> <br /> Fairest Blessing encourages one to take charge. Fairest Curse punishes taking charge. This creates a conflict that ends up withdrawing the character and encouraging him to not act at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:52:30-07:00","id":505634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505164#post505164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, no putting words in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain. Otherwise is seems far more that you're pissed off that I pointed at a whole in your position rather than me being a jerk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we didn't want mechanical carrots and sticks we'd all just join theatre guilds and act out communal stories that way. </div> </div> </div>Hyperbolic excluded middles aren't helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There won't always be side effects, but saying there's unlikely to be thinks you didn't expect or predict is just hubris. </div> </div> </div>Now who's putting words in someone's mouth?<br /> <br /> I never said there aren't going to be side effects. My position is that you're being inconsistent with the Curses. The Beast Curse is getting a complete pass on all of the behaviors it conceptually discourages (Beasts, who get affirmation from breaking taboos, a behavior that tends to get you arrested or worse, have the most incentive to be as upstanding citizens as possible and obey all the rules to try to avoid getting jailed) and the ease at which it can ignore player agency. The Fairest Curse is being treated in the most hyperbolic negative fashion possible.<br /> <br /> The Fairest Curse comes up when the Fairest's call has a major harm inducing snafu as an unintended consequence. You're treating it as &quot;things not going to plan.&quot; Those two are overlapping but distinct categories. Things can go not according to plans in lots and lots of ways without anyone coming to serious harm accidentally. My assumptions aren't predicated on super-precognition on the side of the Fairest or their player. It's predicated on the ST not dicking leadership PCs over by having things go sideways all the time outside of player agency induced events. If a Fairest leader makes a plan, and it's a good plan, it should work unless the PCs do something besides follow the plan; or involves an inherently unpredictable situation like combat.<br /> <br /> My issue is that the Curse isn't robbing Fairest leaders of their agency. People that assume leaders don't get to actually be effective leaders despite their character's actions and traits are what's robbing them of agency in this analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505431#post505431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Putting aside accusations of people running non-corrupt police forces in the WoD (hey, depends on how people run the game), all changelings have methods of innate methods of escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it costs considerably more for a Beast. We don't know exactly how the innate escaping bonds trick works yet. But it is three times more expensive for Beasts than everyone else. A starting-ish level Beast doesn't store all that much glamour in them, so they'd have to be very careful about trying to use this to avoid their Curse breaking point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever heard of the phrase &quot;no plan ever survives contact with the enemy?&quot; Its not the WoD requiring side effects from happening. Its REALITY. That's how things work in real life, let alone a story driven game where we all thrive on drama and unintended consequences. </div> </div> </div>I'll echo ArcaneArts on the oddity of this always coming down to a militaristic/combative view/role of leadership. There are lots of leaders that aren't commanding troops, leading police units, or whatever. Things going sideways in politics, business, and similar avenues of leadership very rarely lead to serious harm to anyone in reality. President Obama's nomination of Loretta Lynch to be Attorney General certainly counts as &quot;no plan ever survives contact with the enemy&quot; in that despite the Senate leadership wanting Eric Holder out, Lynch being a wonderful candidate, they managed to set a new record in delaying her confirmation. Who got harmed in a way that would incite the Fairest Curse if anyone involved as a leader was one?<br /> <br /> The issue, again, is not that things will always go according to plan, but that &quot;not going according to plan&quot; is not what causes a breaking point for the Fairest Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its inevitable simply because that's the way things are. Its unrealistic to assume that it won't happen. </div> </div> </div>My issue with inevitability is not the inevitability of plans going awry, but the claims of that equating to constant Fairest Curse breaking point level of things going awry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505452#post505452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Beast Curse seems like it's out of the characters hands it actually isn't, completely at least, as you can always try to avoid captivity and try to escape from your captors.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fairly easy to make capture impossible or not worth it. And escape is pointless because the Beast Curse comes in once you're caught. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if the Beast ends up captured and confined once a session then it's one hell of a weird plot the ST is running or the ST is purposefully after the Beast or it's player. </div> </div> </div>The Beast Curse's breaking point is limited to once a Story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Darkling Curse makes you unable to fully trust anyone and it only comes to effect should you choose to trust. There is no other way for it to come up really, it's conpletely about a player choice unless some heavy mind/emotional control powers are being employed. This Curse will not show up often unless the Player want's it to. </div> </div> </div>Yep. Almost to the point of it being a bit pointless to be there. If the Darkling Curse is good from a player agency perspective, than there's two issues. Either avoiding getting hit with the Curse is what players want, at which point there is no reason for Darklings to even have one since it is so easy to avoid, and the Curses in general should be equally minor (the Beast and Fairest ones are not). Or getting hit with the Curse is something players do want, at which point the fact that the Fairest Curse is a bit less in their control isn't such a bad thing because they want it to happen and it seems most people are assuming that's pretty easy to just let it ride and it will come up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also with both of the above avoiding the Curse does not in any way rob you of the possibility of using your Blessing. Avoiding capture, which most PC's are doing any way no one wants to be a prisoner, does not invalidate breaking taboo nor does being distrustful rob you of opportunities to make hard choices. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the Beast Blessing and Curse are at odds with each other; just in the opposite direction. Indulging in your Blessing increases the odds of your Curse being a problem. Running around be a taboo breaker is a great way to end up in jail overnight or worse. Avoiding your Blessing is a very simple way to help avoid your Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fairest Curse on the other hand can apply multiple times a session, and the only way the player can affect this outcome is by playing a withdrawn character who avoids leadership roles, does not give his counsel to anyone so that no one would act on his advice etc. </div> </div> </div>I have trouble imagining a session where a Fairest is making multiple leadership calls that would qualify for the Curse even in theory. That seems to be a game moving at much faster pace - and much higher octane - than the default the books go to. Or really long sessions (but that's something more of a fundamental ST system issue with narrative time structures).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fairest Blessing encourages one to take charge. Fairest Curse punishes taking charge. This creates a conflict that ends up withdrawing the character and encouraging him to not act at all. </div> </div> </div>The Fairest Curse punishes making mistakes. Yes, mistakes are inevitable. But that standard isn't being applied to the Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:07:38-07:00","id":505647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505634#post505634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have trouble imagining a session where a Fairest is making multiple leadership calls that would qualify for the Curse even in theory. That seems to be a game moving at much faster pace - and much higher octane - than the default the books go to. Or really long sessions (but that's something more of a fundamental ST system issue with narrative time structures).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to ask, why? All it would take would be a motley or court leader who gives more than one order in a session.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:44:52-07:00","id":505713,"title":"","content":"Hm... I wonder if the Curse applies to the Fairest if he himself is the only one who gets seriously hurt by his own decision. In that case, it occurs to me that some Fairest could try to profit from the Blessing and avoid the Curse by frequently centering their decisions around putting themselves in harm's way and taking on dangerous tasks personally. That's a proactive method of responding that feels appropriate to the archetype. I could kinda see it even without that qualifier, to a degree, but it might help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:47:04-07:00","id":505717,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind it doesn't have to be physical harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:51:08-07:00","id":505720,"title":"","content":"As far as my comment goes, it still merits question-just how often does social, mental, or emotional harm occur to your characters in game play? Cause for me that's a matter of climax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:07:14-07:00","id":505806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's fairly easy to make capture impossible or not worth it. </div> </div> </div>But such circumstances are quite rare in RPG's at least in my experience barring either massive blunders or ST's plot points that require it to happen. Generally though most players will try to avoid captivity whether or not they have a Curse pertaining to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Beast Curse's breaking point is limited to once a Story. </div> </div> </div>Nice catch I somehow missed that. But such a limitation seems lacking in the Fairest Curse which ironically is a lot more likely to happen often than being captured is. Even the Fairest Curse becomes quite meaningless to me, and most of my issues are about it are resolved, if it's once a story as well.<br /> <br /> At the pace we play once a story tends to be mean a rather impactless thing anyway since our Aberrant Chronicle has ran for over 10 years of real time and it could be divided into around 3 stories. Naturally the game has had some hiatuses as well, hence the story divides, but still anything applicable only once per story is likely to be quite meaningless on our table. Similarly our long running Exalted game, that lasted 2-3 years I think, could have been about 3 Stories if I'm being generous.<br /> <br /> Definitely a thing where YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have trouble imagining a session where a Fairest is making multiple leadership calls that would qualify for the Curse even in theory. That seems to be a game moving at much faster pace - and much higher octane - than the default the books go to. </div> </div> </div>And I have trouble seeing a session where it wouldn't. This is even more true of high octane action scenes but it is a problem in normal scenes and situations as well, see my real life example in a previous post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as my comment goes, it still merits question-just how often does social, mental, or emotional harm occur to your characters in game play? </div> </div> </div>Do note that it isn't limited to harm that happens to your characters quite on the contraire it is about what happens to anyone who might befall upon some harm because of your decision or counsel. Such things can and do happen fairly often in RL let alone in an RPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fairest Curse punishes making mistakes. Yes, mistakes are inevitable. But that standard isn't being applied to the Beasts. </div> </div> </div>If only that were true. Fairest Curse does not take into account acceptable collateral damage caused by a plan, MachineIV even said he liked that (the fact that it doesn't matter if the plan succeeds if someone got hurt you are struck by it) about the Curse. So it is not about making mistakes but for example in a combat situation it's about pure luck since that is the only way you are, even with a perfect plan, going to avoid any and all harm befalling your side. Similar can be said of plans in a non-combat situation where the harm is likelier to manifest as hurt feelings, which count for the Curse. So if it was about mistakes, that it struck only when your plan failed (which would be appropriate when looking at many villains, and some heroes, reactions to their plans failing), instead of being tied to any harm befalling anyone due to your leadership I would be much less critical of it.<br /> <br /> Again for the Beast part. I have been in countless games in over two decades of playing and I still can probably count the number of times I have been captured using my fingers. Times when plans have caused harm to someone, regardless of whether they fail or succeed, innumerable. The two cannot be compared really. But like said there is another major difference between the Curses, unless it is a mistake is the difference of frequency. Like you pointed out the Beast Curse clearly says it only applies once per story while the Darklings and the Fairest Curse is clearly said to apply anytime they trust someone or harm someone through their leadership. This makes the Beast Curse least likely to cause trouble during the game while the Darkling has easiest time avoiding his, even if it can strike more often than once a Story, while the Fairest is stuck bleeding Clarity all the time, unless they withdraw from decision making and such.<br /> <br /> But the ultimate point is this. If the Blessing is supposed to be something that enforces your self image by repeating the task that helped you win your freedom the Curse should be about rattling that self-image. Beast is about freedom hence it is rattled by captivity, Darkling is about betrayal thus it is rattled by trust, Fairest is about leadership and so it is rattled by... leadership? That just makes no sense at all. It would make sense if it was rattled by poor leadership, well more sense than it does now, but as pointed out it doesn't care whether the plan succeeds or fails only about harm befalling someone. It would be more sensible perhaps if it was rattled by anarchy, they risk their Clarity if they cause dissidence and chaos by rising against appointed leadership but even in this case usurpation of power should be possible without triggering the Curse if the actual structures of power remained in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T14:59:08-07:00","id":506120,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> A bit on the Curse and clarification it needs:<br /> <br /> Does the Fairest Curse come into play if the Fairest is being actively subverted?<br /> <br /> If a Fairest orders a subordinate to go negotiate a peace deal with a motley that's causing problems, and the subordinate ignores that order and just executes them all while they're expecting a peace deal, does the Fairest get hit with their Curse?<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Fairest's plans and directives are solid, but people get hurt not because of the plans, but because someone opts to completely disobey them, what happens?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:19:30-07:00","id":506250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505806#post505806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If only that were true. Fairest Curse does not take into account acceptable collateral damage caused by a plan, MachineIV even said he liked that (the fact that it doesn't matter if the plan succeeds if someone got hurt you are struck by it) about the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I THINK in the final version, the Curse is going to allow for casualties that are &quot;part of the plan&quot;. So, you can play chess. <br /> <br /> I think there's something nifty and sobering about starting off with the realisation that Steve isn't going to make it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T18:14:43-07:00","id":506285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506250#post506250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I THINK in the final version, the Curse is going to allow for casualties that are &quot;part of the plan&quot;. So, you can play chess.<br /> <br /> I think there's something nifty and sobering about starting off with the realisation that Steve isn't going to make it back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, I think it works out better that way. Carries a certain poignancy.<br /> <br /> On a less serious note, I'm now thinking of Zapp Brannigan as a Fairest. Which... Considering the Blessing is about taking charge despite not knowing what he's doing, works out even better than I thought.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, just wanted to ask again about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505713#post505713\">my post</a> last page: is the Fairest's Curse meant to trigger if the Fairest himself is the only one who gets seriously hurt from his decision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T21:25:36-07:00","id":506385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506285#post506285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a more serious note, just wanted to ask again about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505713#post505713\">my post</a> last page: is the Fairest's Curse meant to trigger if the Fairest himself is the only one who gets seriously hurt from his decision?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I wouldn't count them for their own Curse's purposes. But truth be told, I'd favor tackling that case-for-case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:28:02-07:00","id":506408,"title":"","content":"I think... what I'd rather see than the Leadership thing that is being pushed, is if it was about Perfection. Either the illusion of it, or creating it in the world around them. The person whom seems noble, and 'better' would come across as being Fairest, but the steps they have to take to make sure everything is Perfect is where the darkness starts to creep in. Those up-all-night perfectionists, trying to show their value, trying to enforce their will, putting all of themselves into making that project they want to complete perfect! But, their drive to do so shows how fallible they really are. When someone puts all of themselves into something, sure, it can be pretty. But that scraggled look of three days without sleep, hairs scattered all about as they try to stitch something together that no one else had the ability to do so (or, so the character believes) kinda feels like it's more in line with what Fairest are supposed to be in this edition, but somewhat different from the first edition, an interesting middle ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:33:00-07:00","id":506410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=505440#post505440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my big problems with the assumptions comes from the apparent high level of violence that happens in peoples games. Most people don't go out of their way for a fight, so it's not like someone getting hurt under the Fairest's direction is something that happens every other game.<br /> <br /> But maybe that's just my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran a game (mixed supernaturals) weekly for about a year and half, maybe two years. In all that time, the players were responsible for about 8-10 deaths (not counting ghosts/spirits). At least half of the NPCs they killed were killed in self defense. Almost all of the rest were very intentional, with one being an actual execution that was debated within the party. A handful of bystanders and allies suffered some sort of significant harm due to blowback/collateral damage, one did die, but it wasn't something that happened every time they tried to execute a plan. The rest of the deaths in the campaign were all due to the independent actions of the various villains, and even they didn't rack up crazy body counts. If I had to guess, I'd say that the Fairest curse would have only come up about half a dozen times, maybe a few more if you wanted to be really liberal about what constitutes seriously hurt. That game was focused on mystery and investigation, though. Conversely, I played in a vamp game recently where we were responsible for at least twice as many deaths in just a few months worth of weekly games. In that game, the curse would have come up every 2-3 sessions. So, it varies quite a bit. This might be something to tweak with house rules based on group play style. If you run a game where combat is used sparingly and/or the players' plans causing serious harm is rare, maybe keep it as is. For most of the games I run, I think it would work fine as written. If combats and collateral damage are a regular feature of your games, maybe be generous with bonuses to the breaking point roll, or limit the curse to once a session, or give them a way to avoid it, like burning all of their temporary glamour to re-roll for the breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:38:59-07:00","id":506414,"title":"","content":"My only issue with this Seeming, currently, is that it does seem like a misnomer, as someone else said earlier. Now, the Kiths do seem to indicate that Fairest make for attractive examples, so maybe it's just an omission from this draft. As the Seeming is written right now, it seems like they are looked up to, and possibly glow-y, but not necessarily beautiful. I'm fine with that, but for the sake of semantics, maybe the Seeming name should be changed to &quot;Shining&quot; or something. Personally, I hope the aspect of Fae beauty is just made explicit in a later draft, thereby justifying the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:08:30-07:00","id":506423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506414#post506414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only issue with this Seeming, currently, is that it does seem like a misnomer, as someone else said earlier. Now, the Kiths do seem to indicate that Fairest make for attractive examples, so maybe it's just an omission from this draft. As the Seeming is written right now, it seems like they are looked up to, and possibly glow-y, but not necessarily beautiful. I'm fine with that, but for the sake of semantics, maybe the Seeming name should be changed to &quot;Shining&quot; or something. Personally, I hope the aspect of Fae beauty is just made explicit in a later draft, thereby justifying the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the use of &quot;fair&quot; is that of a courteous and respectful address. Such as in Twain's Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court, &quot;Even so, fair my lord.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or perhaps referring to nonviolence. Or perhaps referring to something of considerable value, particularly in a faux modest sense. Or, referring to the most complete example. Or, just and without cheating. <br /> <br /> Or, the most likely, something that is good. Ala Macbeth. &quot;Fair is foul, and foul is fair.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:19:39-07:00","id":506427,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the &quot;Glamour-charge Social Attributes&quot; power may survive in a Fairest-specific Contract Clause?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:42:45-07:00","id":506437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506423#post506423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the use of &quot;fair&quot; is that of a courteous and respectful address. Such as in Twain's Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court, &quot;Even so, fair my lord.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or perhaps referring to nonviolence. Or perhaps referring to something of considerable value, particularly in a faux modest sense. Or, referring to the most complete example. Or, just and without cheating.<br /> <br /> Or, the most likely, something that is good. Ala Macbeth. &quot;Fair is foul, and foul is fair.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. It seems like a pretty overt reference to Snow White, in which it is specifically about beauty. Besides, the write up doesn't really call out any of those other meanings of the word either. They're described as leaders, not as courteous or just or honest or nonviolent or possessing a false modesty or even good (you said they sounded like excellent villains). None of the meanings seem to really fit to me. Either way, I like the Seeming. So, does that mean that it's an intentional omission and the Fairest are not all beautiful in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:55:18-07:00","id":506439,"title":"","content":"You know... if I get to play Lily, Sabre, Sword (the Dark Eras 17th Century France setting) with 2nd Edition rules.... La Maupin can't really be a Fairest (as she is in my 1st Edition write-up)... she'd have to be a Beast I suppose. I have no idea what animal features I'd give her, maybe cat features? I guess with the right grace/beauty associated Kith &amp; Vainglory Contracts it will still work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:56:08-07:00","id":506440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506437#post506437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does that mean that it's an intentional omission and the Fairest are not all beautiful in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the casually-mentioned examples of a Muse in 1e is a rather transparent King In Yellow sendup. 1e also notes as early as the corebook both the universal beauty of Arcadia and the diversity of ways that beauty manifests \u2014 the aforementioned Macbeth quote's first half is pretty much the textual effect of poisoned ensorcellment, and I hardly think it a coincidence that Winter Masques opts to expand the seeming's characterization along the note of &quot;a stunning majority of the Fairest possessed some notable talent that many believe to be the reason for their abduction.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T00:23:45-07:00","id":506446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506440#post506440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the casually-mentioned examples of a Muse in 1e is a rather transparent King In Yellow sendup. 1e also notes as early as the corebook both the universal beauty of Arcadia and the diversity of ways that beauty manifests \u2014 the aforementioned Macbeth quote's first half is pretty much the textual effect of poisoned ensorcellment, and I hardly think it a coincidence that Winter Masques opts to expand the seeming's characterization along the note of &quot;a stunning majority of the Fairest possessed some notable talent that many believe to be the reason for their abduction.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Their beauty could be horrifying, certainly, but it was still beauty. Or that beauty might be in the form of some talent like dance (although I don't recall getting the impression from Winter Masques that the talent was supposed to be INSTEAD of physical beauty, so much as a cause for abduction, but it's been awhile). Either way, beauty was still part of the 1e Seeming. It seems to be conspicuously absent from the 2e version. I apologize if I'm missing your meaning. BTW: Love your avatar, Satchel.<br /> <br /> I think their appearing genuine and trustworthy is the best justification possible for the name at present, even if it feels like a bit of a stretch. It's just not what the term Fairest in a fairy tale context evokes for most readers, I think. Doesn't matter that much, anyway. A rose by any other name and all that. I still like the Seeming.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T00:38:19-07:00","id":506449,"title":"","content":"Er. I also neglected to mention:<br /> <br /> Fair, at its root, is in reference to &quot;Fair Folk.&quot; The &quot;Fairest&quot; are &quot;The Most Fair Folk of the Lost&quot;. They're the most fae. That's why they have such a captivating, enthralling power on those around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T00:40:37-07:00","id":506450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506449#post506449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. I also neglected to mention:<br /> <br /> Fair, at its root, is in reference to &quot;Fair Folk.&quot; The &quot;Fairest&quot; are &quot;The Most Fair Folk of the Lost&quot;. They're the most fae. That's why they have such a captivating, enthralling power on those around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I'm sorry. (no I'm not)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T02:50:46-07:00","id":506582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506449#post506449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. I also neglected to mention:<br /> <br /> Fair, at its root, is in reference to &quot;Fair Folk.&quot; The &quot;Fairest&quot; are &quot;The Most Fair Folk of the Lost&quot;. They're the most fae. That's why they have such a captivating, enthralling power on those around them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely did not come away from reading the draft with that impression. If anything, it made me feel like they were the least like the Keepers.<br /> <br /> They're all about others. The Gentry are all about themselves.<br /> They sacrifice. The Gentry demand sacrifices.<br /> People naturally look up to them. The Fair Folk traditionally use trickery, fear, temptation, or magic to get what they want.<br /> They appear genuine and fit in wherever they are. The Keepers are otherworldly and alien, often even showing through their disguises.<br /> The Fairest takes it hard when their decisions hurt others. The True Fae are callous and cruel and treat people as pawns.<br /> The example concept mentions real love. The Fair Folk aren't well acquainted with real love.<br /> <br /> To me they read as the most human, not the most Fae: like the mortal protagonist in the Fairy Tail instead of the supernatural creature. Even the way they deal with clarity is more human; anyone's sense of self would be reinforced by taking charge and pulling through in a pinch, and normal people would certainly be shaken if their actions lead to someone being inadvertently hurt. They're like the anti-Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T04:39:39-07:00","id":506611,"title":"","content":"And in 1ed they were <b>totally</b> like a True Fae. One more bone of dissonance between idea of Fairest... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T05:01:46-07:00","id":506616,"title":"","content":"That may have had more to do with how an Actor needed to conform to a seeming and for creatures with clarity 0 Fairest had no downsides, so that's the one they'd usually pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:01:48-07:00","id":506685,"title":"","content":"That's just it though. The Fairest are the closest to the True Fae, but they are at their core human (in part, at least). Their role comes with a figment of the authority of the Gentry, but ironically they (most) defined that part for themselves by making a decision that is opposite to everything the True Fae are.<br /> <br /> The boon the Fairest receive from acting on the authority of the crown placed upon their heads is greater than the inherent risk that comes with the burden. The act of ruling, of using that enthralling presence to lead others is always a thing of self-assurance; when things may go wrong, and the weight of leadership lashes back at the changeling, nothing guarantees it will make that crown stumble from their brow and their grip on themselves slip. And even if it does, does it matter? You're just back where you started. You can account for myriad possibilities all you want, seek to gain that clarity with no losses, but you don't need to worry if you find yourself shaken by it. If in the end your mind is on the same footing, you still <i>lead</i>. You still acted upon who your Seeming makes you, and possibly succeed in every other front. Your guidance will still be looked up to.<br /> <br /> This interplay between the Blessing and the Curse encourages the Fairest to <i>act like the True Fae</i>, despite their capacity for human morality and selflessness. You don't need to <i>really </i>care for collateral damage, for unexpected consequences, for those you did not plan on getting hurt. You command, and you will not lose yourself from it. And this mentality pushes the Fairest, especially those who genuinely do care for others and believe they can do better and <i>have</i> to lead them, to detach themselves from the risks that come with taking all that responsibility on your shoulders. For some, it might even be putting the cart before the horse - you isolate your heart from accounting for those you are trying to protect, from those you are doing this for, so you may better lead them; and reaffirm yourself.<br /> <br /> It actually works quite well when you think like that, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-07-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:27:43-07:00","id":506842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506449#post506449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. I also neglected to mention:<br /> <br /> Fair, at its root, is in reference to &quot;Fair Folk.&quot; The &quot;Fairest&quot; are &quot;The Most Fair Folk of the Lost&quot;. They're the most fae. That's why they have such a captivating, enthralling power on those around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read every single Changeling sourcebook. Is it an established fact that all Gentry have &quot;a captivating, enthralling power on those around them&quot;? If not, maybe it should become one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:35:09-07:00","id":506860,"title":"","content":"It is. Even when they're hiding among the humans and fae, there's something magnetic to them. It's why you can still lose Clarity around them even if you don't know what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:37:07-07:00","id":506879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506611#post506611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in 1ed they were <b>totally</b> like a True Fae. One more bone of dissonance between idea of Fairest... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is either a poor reading of the Fairest or the Strangers.<br /> <br /> They had the most semblance to each other, they absolutely <i>were not</i> mirror images of one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T11:51:49-07:00","id":507058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506685#post506685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it though. The Fairest are the closest to the True Fae, but they are at their core human (in part, at least). Their role comes with a figment of the authority of the Gentry, but ironically they (most) defined that part for themselves by making a decision that is opposite to everything the True Fae are.<br /> <br /> The boon the Fairest receive from acting on the authority of the crown placed upon their heads is greater than the inherent risk that comes with the burden. The act of ruling, of using that enthralling presence to lead others is always a thing of self-assurance; when things may go wrong, and the weight of leadership lashes back at the changeling, nothing guarantees it will make that crown stumble from their brow and their grip on themselves slip. And even if it does, does it matter? You're just back where you started. You can account for myriad possibilities all you want, seek to gain that clarity with no losses, but you don't need to worry if you find yourself shaken by it. If in the end your mind is on the same footing, you still <i>lead</i>. You still acted upon who your Seeming makes you, and possibly succeed in every other front. Your guidance will still be looked up to.<br /> <br /> This interplay between the Blessing and the Curse encourages the Fairest to <i>act like the True Fae</i>, despite their capacity for human morality and selflessness. You don't need to <i>really </i>care for collateral damage, for unexpected consequences, for those you did not plan on getting hurt. You command, and you will not lose yourself from it. And this mentality pushes the Fairest, especially those who genuinely do care for others and believe they can do better and <i>have</i> to lead them, to detach themselves from the risks that come with taking all that responsibility on your shoulders. For some, it might even be putting the cart before the horse - you isolate your heart from accounting for those you are trying to protect, from those you are doing this for, so you may better lead them; and reaffirm yourself.<br /> <br /> It actually works quite well when you think like that, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sold!<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for using &quot;myriad&quot; correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:06:35-07:00","id":507104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=506860#post506860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. Even when they're hiding among the humans and fae, there's something magnetic to them. It's why you can still lose Clarity around them even if you don't know what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just skimmed the core book and Autumn nightmares and couldn't find the text to support this. Trying to find the relevant passages, could you point me in the right direction? They're referred to as terrifying and/or awe-inspiring pretty regularly, but I couldn't find anything about them being magnetic or people wanting to follow them.<br /> <br /> To the contrary, under The Mein in Autumn Nightmares (p. 68), it reads: &quot;When encountering a Fae whose Mask is dropped in favor of it's Mein, a mortal sees it and reacts accordingly. Most run. Some attack. Others collapse into gibbering piles.&quot;<br /> <br /> And under An Imperfect Mask in Autumn Nightmares (p. 71), it reads: &quot;In drawing attention to themselves, the Fae earn the unease of those humans around them. Social rolls made in a True Fae's favor while wearing the mortal Mask are made at at -1 die penalty, and they do not gain the 10 again benefit from such a roll. Other story-based consequences may result, as well. Some humans may flee, become belligerent or even attack. Of Course, the Fae will find other ways to get what he wants from foolish humans...&quot;<br /> <br /> These passages (and some other similar ones) seem to indicate that rather than being magnetic or enthralling, they are unsettling, terrifying, and repellent. The response isn't &quot;this guy seems trustworthy and competent, I'll follow his lead&quot;. Instead the response is more &quot;holy #$%&amp;, kill it with fire&quot;! It seems like they'd have to use Contracts, Blessings, or good old fashioned tricks to get what they want from mortals.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the books don't say what you said, just that they also say this. Wouldn't be the first time a World of Darkness game line contradicted itself (sometimes even in the same book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:59:15-07:00","id":507170,"title":"","content":"The key point there is &quot;reacts accordingly&quot;. Not all Fae look scary. Some are enticing. One of them in one book as Striking Looks 6, despite that not being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:09:54-07:00","id":507205,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be more representative of the one with Striking Looks 6, however? Redtooth, Redtooth is a bloated disgusting thing that no one would willingly attempt to follow unless it was the only option beyond being eaten.<br /> <br /> Or are all of the True Fae beautiful in second edition? They never really seemed like leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:00:26-07:00","id":507253,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's necessarily &quot;they look like leaders&quot; or &quot;they are so charismatic people follow them&quot;. Rather, it is simply that <i>they are the lords and ladies of Arcadia</i>, and whether you want it or not you cannot deny that they are masters there. Their authority <i>is</i> by virtue of the beings they are, monsters and heroes and demons and angels of legend, evident in their presence that bears down on any who see their true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:20:02-07:00","id":507267,"title":"","content":"So, again, Lords sounds more fitting.<br /> <br /> 'Mirror, mirror on the wall, who's the fairest one of all?'<br /> <br /> 'Well, you <i>are </i>the Queen, so you of course.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:16:50-07:00","id":507335,"title":"","content":"I mean, I think Fairest fits just fine because it's &quot;most fair&quot; as in &quot;most like the fair folk&quot;, which was pointed out. Also I think it sounds better. Lords/Ladies could just be a nickname of the Seeming.<br /> <br /> But I digress, and this is simply an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-07-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:10:14-07:00","id":507552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507253#post507253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it's necessarily &quot;they look like leaders&quot; or &quot;they are so charismatic people follow them&quot;. Rather, it is simply that <i>they are the lords and ladies of Arcadia</i>, and whether you want it or not you cannot deny that they are masters there. Their authority <i>is</i> by virtue of the beings they are, monsters and heroes and demons and angels of legend, evident in their presence that bears down on any who see their true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... I feel like a comparison ought to be made with Aslan, but I'm having trouble articulating one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:38:30-07:00","id":507634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507552#post507552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... I feel like a comparison ought to be made with Aslan, but I'm having trouble articulating one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one majestic mofo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:11:43-07:00","id":507680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507170#post507170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key point there is &quot;reacts accordingly&quot;. Not all Fae look scary. Some are enticing. One of them in one book as Striking Looks 6, despite that not being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, some Fae are beautiful or charming, but, at least in Autumn Nightmares, this seems to be in spite of their otherwise terrifying nature. Notice that the social penalties aren't something that is only applied to some of the Gentry. Even the beautiful or charming ones have to deal with their otherworldly &quot;wrongness&quot; putting people off. The point I was making is that being enthralling or magnetic is far from a standard feature of the Fae, at least in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:48:14-07:00","id":507718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507253#post507253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it's necessarily &quot;they look like leaders&quot; or &quot;they are so charismatic people follow them&quot;. Rather, it is simply that <i>they are the lords and ladies of Arcadia</i>, and whether you want it or not you cannot deny that they are masters there. Their authority <i>is</i> by virtue of the beings they are, monsters and heroes and demons and angels of legend, evident in their presence that bears down on any who see their true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could buy that. Some glimmer of the Fae's might shines through them. However, their blessing seems to inspire trust and confidence, instead of fear and awe like the presence of Fae. It's less Fearsome Mein of the Fae and more Poise of the Politician. Their &quot;duty and responsibility peek through&quot; not their awe-inspiring power. Since the flavor is so different, if this power is indeed intended to be a shadow of the Fae's, it bears addressing that in the Seeming description.<br /> <br /> If the Fairest are really meant to be the closest to the True Fae, why is this not alluded to in the draft? And why, then, are their Blessing and Curse focused on others, in contradiction to Fae attitudes?<br /> <br /> If their power is meant to be a glimmer of the Gentry's might, then how was it acquired? And why does it manifest so differently than it does in the Fae?<br /> <br /> The 2e Seemings are supposed to be all about how the Changeling escaped and how that changed them forever. So, how does a decision to help others and risk yourself (one of the most un-Gentry things you could do) lead the character to become more like the Strangers? <br /> <br /> I mean, I really like this concept. Perhaps the Fairest somehow learned to imitate the Keepers' power and used that to help others escape. Or the Fairest stole a portion of their Keeper's power. Maybe a selfless act in their Keeper's realm allowed them to steal and invert some of the Keeper's power because of some ancient oath, contract, or pledge. Or maybe their self-sacrificing act just caused the Wyrd to reshape them as a sort of negative image of the Keeper's with a power that achieves similar results by an opposite means. Any of these things would be cool, but there's no indication of anything like that in the text. As of the first draft, there's nothing to support the Fairest being closest to the Fae, or their power being anything other than that - theirs, not an echo or reflection of the authority that the Keepers wield by might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:22:33-07:00","id":508146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507634#post507634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was one majestic mofo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Majestic, yeah, and also terrifyingly unsafe and untamed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:06:25-07:00","id":508354,"title":"","content":"Why do you think he's majestic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:10:00-07:00","id":508601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=507170#post507170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key point there is &quot;reacts accordingly&quot;. Not all Fae look scary. Some are enticing. One of them in one book as Striking Looks 6, despite that not being a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, judging by Autumn Nightmares, some look like children(sort of). Or... a freaking car in one example. <br /> <br /> For that matter, a sample Fae from the 1e core book was supposed to be enticing in a primal, animalistic way, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:18:01-07:00","id":509583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=508601#post508601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, judging by Autumn Nightmares, some look like children(sort of). Or... a freaking car in one example.<br /> <br /> For that matter, a sample Fae from the 1e core book was supposed to be enticing in a primal, animalistic way, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth. However, the point I had been trying to make with the quote from the book was that an enticing/commanding aura was not a feature of <i>all</i> True Fae. All of the Fae that are enticing have merits, like Striking Looks or Inspiring, and/or very high social stats to make up for their innate otherworldly weirdness. The social penalties they experience around mortals, however, <i>are</i> a feature of all True Fae. So it isn't justifiable to say that an aura that inspires trust, confidence, or deference is a particularly Fae trait anymore than, say, claws or fangs or elemental features are. We've seen at least as many Fae with no such social abilities and traits that are similar to other Seemings instead. So that power, by itself, especially as presented, doesn't justify them being &quot;closest to the Fair Folk&quot;. Maybe something else about them does. Or maybe the Fair Folk in 2e are different.<br /> <br /> I feel like instead of them being close to the True Fae, it's more of a &quot;darker the negative the brighter the picture&quot; sort of deal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T02:59:13-07:00","id":509758,"title":"","content":"Of course, that's just the Autumn Nightmares True Fae. The ones in Equinox Road are never mentioned to have that weakness at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T07:28:12-07:00","id":509842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=509758#post509758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that's just the Autumn Nightmares True Fae. The ones in Equinox Road are never mentioned to have that weakness at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They also don't have a universal power of command, either, as far as I recall (don't have my copy on me, at the moment). Just a ton of dots of Contracts. I figure they just omitted that weakness because the Equinox Road is more concerned with dealing with Fae in their own realm, where they aren't very likely to be dealing with plain old mortals very much. Or they just forgot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:00:04-07:00","id":510011,"title":"","content":"I just reread the Fairest blessing and curse. The best summation I can come up with is &quot;In time of trouble, time of woe, the dark before the dawn, we turn to... anybody else.&quot; Seriously, making any call in any but the most trivial conflict is automatically a breaking point because every call will lead to someone getting hurt in some way, physical, mental, social or economic. The end result is that the Fairest are actively encouraged to take on leadership roles, then viciously punished for doing so. No thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:43:49-07:00","id":510074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510011#post510011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread the Fairest blessing and curse. The best summation I can come up with is &quot;In time of trouble, time of woe, the dark before the dawn, we turn to... anybody else.&quot; Seriously, making any call in any but the most trivial conflict is automatically a breaking point because every call will lead to someone getting hurt in some way, physical, mental, social or economic. The end result is that the Fairest are actively encouraged to take on leadership roles, then viciously punished for doing so. No thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You do realize that's going to be rewritten to &quot;roll for Clarity when <i>a,person you actually care about </i>gets <i>accidentally</i> hurt, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:52:25-07:00","id":510079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510011#post510011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reread the Fairest blessing and curse. The best summation I can come up with is &quot;In time of trouble, time of woe, the dark before the dawn, we turn to... anybody else.&quot; Seriously, making any call in any but the most trivial conflict is automatically a breaking point because every call will lead to someone getting hurt in some way, physical, mental, social or economic. The end result is that the Fairest are actively encouraged to take on leadership roles, then viciously punished for doing so. No thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summarizing a few comments from this thread, including some from developer and writer:<br /> 1) &quot;Seriously hurt&quot; is not the same as &quot;hurt to any degree whatsoever.&quot;<br /> 2) The current thinking is to cover unintended/collateral serious hurt. If a Fairest makes a call that involves the injury of Jimmy the Intern, no harm no foul if that happens (at least where the Curse is concerned.<br /> 3) Since we don't know how Clarity operates, we can't actually say how bad this is. But we do know that it's a roll: there's a guaranteed free Clarity for stepping up, and only a chance of losing it <i>if</i> something goes awry in the manner described. The Fairest might come out ahead, with a chance of just being no worse off than at the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Wording tweaks. 05-10-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:13:51-07:00","id":510372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510079#post510079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Summarizing a few comments from this thread, including some from developer and writer:<br /> 1) &quot;Seriously hurt&quot; is not the same as &quot;hurt to any degree whatsoever.&quot;<br /> 2) The current thinking is to cover unintended/collateral serious hurt. If a Fairest makes a call that involves the injury of Jimmy the Intern, no harm no foul if that happens (at least where the Curse is concerned.<br /> 3) Since we don't know how Clarity operates, we can't actually say how bad this is. But we do know that it's a roll: there's a guaranteed free Clarity for stepping up, and only a chance of losing it <i>if</i> something goes awry in the manner described. The Fairest might come out ahead, with a chance of just being no worse off than at the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it's worth noting that every single Second Edition 'morality' analogue has offered Beats when you hit a breaking point, even if you succeed. So these things are also blessings in disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:09:28-07:00","id":510431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510372#post510372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's worth noting that every single Second Edition 'morality' analogue has offered Beats when you hit a breaking point, even if you succeed. So these things are also blessings in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. I'm not as clued-in to what other lines have been up to, but that knowledge certainly helps. I'm still interested in seeing how 2e Clarity's shaped up, but I'm sure we'll get a look soon enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:50:55-07:00","id":510565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510372#post510372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, it's worth noting that every single Second Edition 'morality' analogue has offered Beats when you hit a breaking point, even if you succeed. So these things are also blessings in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by leaping into the breach and confronting their Curse, a strong willed enough Changeling can grow as a person and a character? Sounds about right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T06:49:16-07:00","id":510584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510372#post510372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's worth noting that every single Second Edition 'morality' analogue has offered Beats when you hit a breaking point, even if you succeed. So these things are also blessings in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not precisely correct. GMC only has you gaining a Beat on a Dramatic Failure or Exceptional Success for breaking points. Vampire 2nd Edition has you gaining a Beat whenever you roll for Detachment. Werewolf 2nd Edition has no reference to gaining Beats related to breaking points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T07:48:21-07:00","id":510650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=510584#post510584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not precisely correct. GMC only has you gaining a Beat on a Dramatic Failure or Exceptional Success for breaking points. Vampire 2nd Edition has you gaining a Beat whenever you roll for Detachment. Werewolf 2nd Edition has no reference to gaining Beats related to breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah. I didn't know the Werewolf one got changed. Well. Clarity breaking points will be Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:38:20-07:00","id":514910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ceycil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501177#post501177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats a dramtic change of direction for the fairest.<br /> No longer just a pretty face right enough.<br /> Never been too keen on having a fifth of the characters loosely classed as &quot;Leaders&quot; though.<br /> Tends to result in players feeling that they Have to take charge and buy up social abilities or that most of the seasonal monarchs should be fairest in the setting.<br /> Perhaps something more along the lines of the fairest being shining paragons excelling at whatever they focus on?<br /> The fairest leader is the most convincing on public speakers who turns hearts with honeyed words.<br /> The fairest fighter is a elegent duelest who wields his blade with elegence and grace.<br /> The fairest thief is the cat burglar who steals the most heavily guarded item in the musuem and leaves a calling card too boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree very much. This is like the ventrue of old world of darkness. I'm afraid it doesn't make them interesting as much as it makes them a bit one-dimensional.<br /> I also do not enjoy the idea at all that not only are you lore-wise connected to be a leader but that your whole blessing depends on it. It limits rather than opens the door. If we compare to the former version changeling, you often found in the books that rather than excluding character concepts or ideas the core-book relished in telling you just how different and awesome you could make each and every single character you ever made. I do not feel this with the fairest at all in this draft.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>A Fairest may not be the leader, but fate makes them a leader time and time again. Whether they embrace that, or run from it.&quot;</i><br /> This is exactly how you shouldn't do it because it pushes the player (and one fifth of you freehold) into a pre-set position. And not only that, a pre-set position of being a nice and good character, because it is also mentioned in the draft:<i> &quot;</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>To the Changeling eye, he can never remove the sign of leadership, often in the form of a small crown or military decoration. Whatever she does, the Fairest duty and responsibility peek through, and so when someone is in trouble. Without consideration, it\u2019s the Fairest\u2019s feet they will throw themselves down on.&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>The Fairest struggles, every day and night, to live up to their own myth, to be the great hero that they expected to be.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This is not cool! Reading the seemings and kiths so far has been a delight, but I had to stop at the fairest and re-read them again because this is the one area where it didn't go as planned. Rather than opening the horizons to endless variations the description here makes it seem as if the fairest are the leaders, no matter if they like it or not, and the fairest are more often than not the good guys. This doesn't feel very world of darkness, to put it bluntly. The leader caste, if there must be one, should be full of selfish, cruel, distant people. That's world of darkness. Things are meant to be scary, horrible and bad.<br /> <br /> So what would I see different? First of all, a fairest should be someone who excells at what they do, not the leader of the freehold. <b>We don't have to repeat vampire</b>. Anyone can lead and anyone can fail while doing so. As said before me by Cecyl, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">trying to make themselves shining paragons at whatever they do fits their situation better to. Excell, stand out and be above others. Recover clarity when you outshine someone who you consider to be of equal skill than yourself and lose clarity when you attempted to do something important but failed in front of others who will judge you for your failure (for example).<br /> <br /> Secondly, change the description/idea for their personalities. There should definitely not be a &quot;good guy&quot; group in a world of darkness game. I am aware that I am comparing a lot to the former version of changeling here, but let's take a piece of the old fairest description.</span></span></span><br /> <i>&quot;This is the way of the Fae, and it\u2019s the way of the Fairest: they take what and whom they will take, and they will have their fun first. It is their prerogative to be loved and admired, and their right to treat that love any way they will. Sure, they\u2019ll try to rise above it, but there\u2019s always the fact that they really are the fairest of them all. They won their beauty fairly. They deserve to be beautiful.</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<br /> <br /> And here is their curse description:</span></span></span><br /> <i>&quot;Curse: The Fairest, similar to the creatures who stole them, can be callous and unfeeling, vicious and prone to toy with others, even people who love them.</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>&quot;</i><br /> We should absolutely not turn what was kind of the darkest and the cruelest of the seemings into the 'good' characters of this game. Maybe it was wording that I didn't really understand, English it not my native language, or maybe it was a design choice. In either case, it doesn't feel world of darkness at all. It feels like reading the description of a good elven race in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Sorry for long post here is a<br /> TLDR.<br /> Remove leadership and hero position.<br /> Introduce paragons and villain position.<br /> <br /> And once again I'd like to add, I have loved all the stuff I have read so far, especially the kith blessing look -really- freaking cool. I enjoy almost everything that you guys have put out so far but not this draft. It needs to be reworked/reworded!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T20:52:15-07:00","id":515740,"title":"","content":"Might also want to point out that the other main splats have an archetype who specializes in leadership roles. Vampires have Ventrue, Werewolves have Storm Lords, Don't know about Mages, but I'm going to assume the Obrimos or Mastigos, based on what I've heard about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think you're being unfair by saying the Fairest being shoe horned into being leaders. Remember that this time around, Kiths are not restricted by Seeming. You can be anything you want, but your Seeming is how you apply it. If you don't want to be a leader, you don't have to be, you can pick another Seeming and still choose the same Kith. If anything it offers more customization than the previous version.<br /> <br /> As for the Fairest being 1/5th of the population, that's a bit of a stretch. You're saying the number of Changelings is evenly spread among everybody, which is very unlikely to be the case. How can you call yourself &quot;fariest of them all&quot; if you've got 20 super models walking around the place stealing your fans? The way I imagine it, Fairest would actually be a rare Seeming and those who possess it would be among the top ranking positions of a Free Hold, rather than being in every position of government. They're not the supervisor or the lawyers, or the board of directors, they're the CEO's and company presidents. They don't work for the company, they own the company!<br /> <br /> <br /> You also are forgetting that Changelings NEED to stick together. That is the one thing they have that the True Fae don't. They share power rather than hoarding it all for themselves. The True Fae can not comprehend what it means to feel true selflessness or charity for others. If the leaders of the courts are stealing from the city's coffers and sending the Sheriff of Nottingham to extort people, they might as well put a giant, gleaming sign right in front of the Hedge saying &quot;here we are!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Changeling is a game about psychological horror. You were taken to a strange, alien world, you were forced into slavery, warped physically and mentally, and you somehow managed to escape. Now you've got Huntsmen tracking you day and night, waiting for the chance to drag you back into slavery, where a very pissed off Keeper is likely waiting to punish you. And here you have the Fairest, who the rest of the court is looking to for support and leadership. They place their lives in your hands... and then you fuck up and get them killed or worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> How is that for a horror story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-16-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:38:21-07:00","id":515838,"title":"","content":"Again, I have no bloody clue how people don't see the villains in the seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T01:44:15-07:00","id":515947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515740#post515740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might also want to point out that the other main splats have an archetype who specializes in leadership roles. Vampires have Ventrue, Werewolves have Storm Lords, Don't know about Mages, but I'm going to assume the Obrimos or Mastigos, based on what I've heard about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it isn't needed here. It wasn't needed in old changeling. Why should every splat be built in the same way? One fighter clan, one sneaky investigator clan and one leader clan? No thank you! This doesn't make it interesting, it removes how unique changeling is by making it into something it isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515740#post515740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,<b> I think you're being unfair by saying the Fairest being shoe horned into being leaders</b>. Remember that this time around, Kiths are not restricted by Seeming. You can be anything you want, but your Seeming is how you apply it. <b>If you don't want to be a leader, you don't have to be, you can pick another Seeming and still choose the same Kith.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, you can be anything you want to be, unless you want to be a fairest, because then you have to be a leader? That is not good design. It doesn't open up doors to let you create whatever you want. It excludes instead of includes. I'd also like to remind that the contracts will have unique properties depending on your seeming, so it's not like you can just 'make a character with that kith instead' without missing out on something.<br /> Brujah from Old world of darkness were more three dimensional than this! When I read the Changeling: The Lost core rule-book for the first time I could not put it down until I had covered about the first 200 pages. I was amazed at how filled with awesome ideas it was and it felt like every page I turned, I was given five new character ideas just right on the spot. Because it was open ended. Want to be an nice winter elemental queen? Awesome! Want to be an autumn fairest black-widow style serial killer? Awesome!<br /> <br /> As it stands right now, it feels like when you open the fairest section and you read it, it asks you this: Want to play a leader? No? Then get out of here! That doesn't help create awesome cool concepts and ideas. It limits you. Changeling shouldn't be about what limitations you can put on a player. It should be about just how much can we loosen the reins and see where this trip takes us!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515740#post515740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Fairest being 1/5th of the population, that's a bit of a stretch. You're saying the number of Changelings is evenly spread among everybody, which is very unlikely to be the case. How can you call yourself &quot;fariest of them all&quot; if you've got 20 super models walking around the place stealing your fans? The way I imagine it, Fairest would actually be a rare Seeming and those who possess it would be among the top ranking positions of a Free Hold, rather than being in every position of government. They're not the supervisor or the lawyers, or the board of directors, they're the CEO's and company presidents. They don't work for the company, they own the company!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how they are spread out over the board. I always got the impression that they were roughly evenly spread out. I see how you are thinking though, as it regards to them being all leaders and important people now. I still think the design is terrible though. A majority of the fairest characters I have seen have not been CEO's or presidents. A majority of them have been a mix and mash of hundreds of different ideas that could be created because they weren't set with limitations the moment they decided to play fairest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515740#post515740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also are forgetting that Changelings NEED to stick together. That is the one thing they have that the True Fae don't. They share power rather than hoarding it all for themselves. The True Fae can not comprehend what it means to feel true selflessness or charity for others. If the leaders of the courts are stealing from the city's coffers and sending the Sheriff of Nottingham to extort people, they might as well put a giant, gleaming sign right in front of the Hedge saying &quot;here we are!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>All splats need to work together. That's one of the basic truths of world of darkness. And then there's the second truth, how they don't because of inside conflicts.<br /> Because the autumn queen is a freaking psychopath who kills people's fetches without consulting them first. Because the winter court has made a deal with the true fae where the gentry stays of their back if they just hand them a few human children every now and then.<br /> <br /> If everyone co-operates straight off the bat because everyone thinks that fairest should lead and they always lead well you lose the greatest source of interesting conflict, the inter-court one. It's like telling all vampires they should be friends because not only do ventrue always lead, but they always do it 'the right way'. Creating a good aligned &quot;clan&quot; is not fitting for world of darkness. It's fitting for DnD, for Exalted and for a whole bunch of other roleplaying games, but not for world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515740#post515740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling is a game about psychological horror. You were taken to a strange, alien world, you were forced into slavery, warped physically and mentally, and you somehow managed to escape. Now you've got Huntsmen tracking you day and night, waiting for the chance to drag you back into slavery, where a very pissed off Keeper is likely waiting to punish you. And here you have the Fairest, who the rest of the court is looking to for support and leadership. They place their lives in your hands... and then you fuck up and get them killed or worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> How is that for a horror story?</div> </div> </div> </div>A boring one. Because unlike any horror story about group survival, the leader in this one is always a good guy who will do their absolute to make sure that their leadership is done in a good way. If you binge watch a whole night of horror shows, let's say Walking Dead because it is farily popular, you will notice a common theme. People fuck up and people do bad things and because they do, they end up in bad situations. Sometimes they do it becuase they geniunly want to help but more often than not, they do it because they see things differently, becuase they see themselves and their kin as more important than other people.<br /> It's not a downright 'evil' point of view, but it is a selfish one. This creates conflict and it creates drama.<br /> <br /> I don't think those stories would be half as interesting if the leader was always from a specific caste and always did their outmost to rule in a manner that was as fair and good as possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T02:18:20-07:00","id":515983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515947#post515947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it isn't needed here. It wasn't needed in old changeling. Why should every splat be built in the same way? One fighter clan, one sneaky investigator clan and one leader clan? No thank you! This doesn't make it interesting, it removes how unique changeling is by making it into something it isn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially, you can be anything you want to be, unless you want to be a fairest, because then you have to be a leader? That is not good design. It doesn't open up doors to let you create whatever you want. It excludes instead of includes. I'd also like to remind that the contracts will have unique properties depending on your seeming, so it's not like you can just 'make a character with that kith instead' without missing out on something.<br /> Brujah from Old world of darkness were more three dimensional than this! When I read the Changeling: The Lost core rule-book for the first time I could not put it down until I had covered about the first 200 pages. I was amazed at how filled with awesome ideas it was and it felt like every page I turned, I was given five new character ideas just right on the spot. Because it was open ended. Want to be an nice winter elemental queen? Awesome! Want to be an autumn fairest black-widow style serial killer? Awesome!<br /> <br /> As it stands right now, it feels like when you open the fairest section and you read it, it asks you this: Want to play a leader? No? Then get out of here! That doesn't help create awesome cool concepts and ideas. It limits you. Changeling shouldn't be about what limitations you can put on a player. It should be about just how much can we loosen the reins and see where this trip takes us!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea how they are spread out over the board. I always got the impression that they were roughly evenly spread out. I see how you are thinking though, as it regards to them being all leaders and important people now. I still think the design is terrible though. A majority of the fairest characters I have seen have not been CEO's or presidents. A majority of them have been a mix and mash of hundreds of different ideas that could be created because they weren't set with limitations the moment they decided to play fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All splats need to work together. That's one of the basic truths of world of darkness. And then there's the second truth, how they don't because of inside conflicts.<br /> Because the autumn queen is a freaking psychopath who kills people's fetches without consulting them first. Because the winter court has made a deal with the true fae where the gentry stays of their back if they just hand them a few human children every now and then.<br /> <br /> If everyone co-operates straight off the bat because everyone thinks that fairest should lead and they always lead well you lose the greatest source of interesting conflict, the inter-court one. It's like telling all vampires they should be friends because not only do ventrue always lead, but they always do it 'the right way'. Creating a good aligned &quot;clan&quot; is not fitting for world of darkness. It's fitting for DnD, for Exalted and for a whole bunch of other roleplaying games, but not for world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A boring one. Because unlike any horror story about group survival, the leader in this one is always a good guy who will do their absolute to make sure that their leadership is done in a good way. If you binge watch a whole night of horror shows, let's say Walking Dead because it is farily popular, you will notice a common theme. People fuck up and people do bad things and because they do, they end up in bad situations. Sometimes they do it becuase they geniunly want to help but more often than not, they do it because they see things differently, becuase they see themselves and their kin as more important than other people.<br /> It's not a downright 'evil' point of view, but it is a selfish one. This creates conflict and it creates drama.<br /> <br /> I don't think those stories would be half as interesting if the leader was always from a specific caste and always did their outmost to rule in a manner that was as fair and good as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this post is largely opinion, and from a very specific and intentional reading. You're ignoring very broad conceptual material by purposefully narrowing it and ignoring inferred and even explicitly stated possibilities. <br /> <br /> There are some points I think you're flat-out wrong about. But the input is helpful; it tells me some people aren't getting inferences that I, and some other readers, got. So I'll take them into account when I'm doing development notes. I'll tell the writer to make some of those points far more obvious. <br /> <br /> I get that you don't like it. I get why you don't like it. I don't need it to be beaten into the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T02:35:05-07:00","id":515986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515983#post515983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this post is largely opinion, and from a very specific and intentional reading. You're ignoring very broad conceptual material by purposefully narrowing it and ignoring inferred and even explicitly stated possibilities.<br /> <br /> There are some points I think you're flat-out wrong about. But the input is helpful; it tells me some people aren't getting inferences that I, and some other readers, got. So I'll take them into account when I'm doing development notes. I'll tell the writer to make some of those points far more obvious.<br /> <br /> I get that you don't like it. I get why you don't like it. I don't need it to be beaten into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, if I'm ignoring anything I'm not doing so intentionally. I read the draft, read it a second time and then read it a third time and this is what I got out out of it. If I just misunderstood it and fairest are meant to be a lot more nuanced than the way I understood it, then I'm the happiest of all really.<br /> Secondly, of course it is opinion. I mean, you guys are literally the developers. The facts are what you make them to be and the rest of us can just either reproduce your facts or tell you our opinions on them.<br /> <br /> Also my aim was never to beat anything into the ground. I saw flaws and I pointed them out. I'd recommend you to read my first post!<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;And once again I'd like to add, I have loved all the stuff I have read so far, especially the kith blessing look -really- freaking cool. I enjoy almost everything that you guys have put out so far but not this draft. It needs to be reworked/reworded!</span></span></span></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If the fairest are deeper than what I got out from the draft I am as happy as you get. I'd love to hear what I am wrong about though. If I misunderstood the draft then tell me what is different than from how I read it!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-reading it again it may have come out as harsher than I wanted it to be. I'd like to underline that any harshness that comes out does so because I frikkin' love Changeling just as much as you guys do. I don't dislike any writer for writing XXX or YYY. I dislike the text, not the author. Keep this in mind when reading my thoughts on the creation and don't take it personal! Thanks :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","user":"A_Newfie","date":". 05-16-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T04:50:12-07:00","id":516067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515986#post515986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, if I'm ignoring anything I'm not doing so intentionally. I read the draft, read it a second time and then read it a third time and this is what I got out out of it. If I just misunderstood it and fairest are meant to be a lot more nuanced than the way I understood it, then I'm the happiest of all really.<br /> Secondly, of course it is opinion. I mean, you guys are literally the developers. The facts are what you make them to be and the rest of us can just either reproduce your facts or tell you our opinions on them.<br /> <br /> Also my aim was never to beat anything into the ground. I saw flaws and I pointed them out. I'd recommend you to read my first post!<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;And once again I'd like to add, I have loved all the stuff I have read so far, especially the kith blessing look -really- freaking cool. I enjoy almost everything that you guys have put out so far but not this draft. It needs to be reworked/reworded!</span></span></span></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If the fairest are deeper than what I got out from the draft I am as happy as you get. I'd love to hear what I am wrong about though. If I misunderstood the draft then tell me what is different than from how I read it!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-reading it again it may have come out as harsher than I wanted it to be. I'd like to underline that any harshness that comes out does so because I frikkin' love Changeling just as much as you guys do. I don't dislike any writer for writing XXX or YYY. I dislike the text. Keep this in mind when reading my thoughts on the creation and don't take it personal! Thanks :3</div> </div> </div> </div>It's totally okay. It's not a thing of taking things personal. It's just that at this point, I don't think anything new is being said about the topic. Usually when that happens, the only thing that occurs is that tones get harsher, and time is wasted. <br /> <br /> All's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T05:23:29-07:00","id":516083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515947#post515947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it isn't needed here. It wasn't needed in old changeling. Why should every splat be built in the same way? One fighter clan, one sneaky investigator clan and one leader clan? No thank you! This doesn't make it interesting, it removes how unique changeling is by making it into something it isn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially, you can be anything you want to be, unless you want to be a fairest, because then you have to be a leader? That is not good design. It doesn't open up doors to let you create whatever you want. It excludes instead of includes. I'd also like to remind that the contracts will have unique properties depending on your seeming, so it's not like you can just 'make a character with that kith instead' without missing out on something.<br /> Brujah from Old world of darkness were more three dimensional than this! When I read the Changeling: The Lost core rule-book for the first time I could not put it down until I had covered about the first 200 pages. I was amazed at how filled with awesome ideas it was and it felt like every page I turned, I was given five new character ideas just right on the spot. Because it was open ended. Want to be an nice winter elemental queen? Awesome! Want to be an autumn fairest black-widow style serial killer? Awesome!<br /> <br /> As it stands right now, it feels like when you open the fairest section and you read it, it asks you this: Want to play a leader? No? Then get out of here! That doesn't help create awesome cool concepts and ideas. It limits you. Changeling shouldn't be about what limitations you can put on a player. It should be about just how much can we loosen the reins and see where this trip takes us!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea how they are spread out over the board. I always got the impression that they were roughly evenly spread out. I see how you are thinking though, as it regards to them being all leaders and important people now. I still think the design is terrible though. A majority of the fairest characters I have seen have not been CEO's or presidents. A majority of them have been a mix and mash of hundreds of different ideas that could be created because they weren't set with limitations the moment they decided to play fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All splats need to work together. That's one of the basic truths of world of darkness. And then there's the second truth, how they don't because of inside conflicts.<br /> Because the autumn queen is a freaking psychopath who kills people's fetches without consulting them first. Because the winter court has made a deal with the true fae where the gentry stays of their back if they just hand them a few human children every now and then.<br /> <br /> If everyone co-operates straight off the bat because everyone thinks that fairest should lead and they always lead well you lose the greatest source of interesting conflict, the inter-court one. It's like telling all vampires they should be friends because not only do ventrue always lead, but they always do it 'the right way'. Creating a good aligned &quot;clan&quot; is not fitting for world of darkness. It's fitting for DnD, for Exalted and for a whole bunch of other roleplaying games, but not for world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A boring one. Because unlike any horror story about group survival, the leader in this one is always a good guy who will do their absolute to make sure that their leadership is done in a good way. If you binge watch a whole night of horror shows, let's say Walking Dead because it is farily popular, you will notice a common theme. People fuck up and people do bad things and because they do, they end up in bad situations. Sometimes they do it becuase they geniunly want to help but more often than not, they do it because they see things differently, becuase they see themselves and their kin as more important than other people.<br /> It's not a downright 'evil' point of view, but it is a selfish one. This creates conflict and it creates drama.<br /> <br /> I don't think those stories would be half as interesting if the leader was always from a specific caste and always did their outmost to rule in a manner that was as fair and good as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not so certain that all the splats need to stick together. I could understand werewolves because they're a pack. But they made it very clear in Vampire that they are solitary creatures by nature. Sure a newly made vampire could try to help out others, but eventually all the blood sucker cares about is themselves. Humanity 4 / 5 is the balancing point. Or at least that's how this was in first edition, before the Strix were introduced and gave the vampires a common enemy to worry about.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do believe that both of us are missing over some details in regards to the possibilities. I know that when I was first introduced to WoD, I had a pretty stereotypical view of each archetype for the splats, but thanks to videos like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hJRyu_e0rqI&amp;index=1&amp;list=PLqARvpQDkw7DD5zcyBFWHPQdYvR_OYYWI\" target=\"_blank\">Gentleman Gamer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S9uorGt0ngI\" target=\"_blank\">Woodwwad</a> I realized there was a heck of a lot more possibilities beyond the simple write ups. It just takes a little imagination and some basic tweaking to find it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I understand what you're saying about the idea of a leader always striving to save everybody not being a compelling story. And it's true that a suspenseful story would have the leader struggling with who to save; their little brother or the group's doctor. However, from my point of view, the idea that everybody is placing expectations on you can be its own brand of horror, especially if those expectations are impossible to live up to and suddenly you become the scapegoat of the situation. Nobody else is at fault because they were just following your orders, and those orders were wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> When I read the part about the Fate placing them in the position of leadership, I thought about stories regarding destiny. Remember Alistaire from Dragon Age? He didn't want to be king at all, like, adamantly opposed to the idea. But just because he was the King's bastard and his only remaining son, his blood mattered more than his wishes. The people who raised him and fought alongside him made the choice for him, that he was going to be king, even though he kept protesting it. That's how I view the idea of a fairest always finding themselves the leader of a situation, even if they don't want to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> In order to escape from Arcadia, the Fairest had to assume the position of leadership. Maybe once they escaped from Arcadia, they just wanted to live a normal life again. But the rebels who followed them to freedom have other plans. The Fairest managed to keep them safe for this long, so why keep following them?<br /> <br /> &quot;This is your rebellion, after all!&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe the Fairest can not in good conscience tell the other Changelings to piss off. Maybe the other Changelings stubbornly declare &quot;We'll follow you anywhere!&quot; The case may vary, but it boils down to whether a Fairest wants to or not, they find themselves thrust into the position of leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:31:27-07:00","id":516122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516067#post516067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's totally okay. It's not a thing of taking things personal. It's just that at this point, I don't think anything new is being said about the topic. Usually when that happens, the only thing that occurs is that tones get harsher, and time is wasted.<br /> <br /> All's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that out of the way, would please explain what it was that I didn't understand/ignored when I took in the fairest seeming? I've skimmed through the eighteen pages here on the topic and re-read the draft and I still don't really see how else I could interpret them than what I posted above. As I said before, English is not my native language but I've played English roleplaying games for a looong time. I'd love to enjoy the fairest as much as the next person, but first I need to understand what I didn't get about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516083#post516083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Lots of smart stuff-</div> </div> </div> </div>The way you describe them in how unique they should be they feel more like they should be an entitlement consisting only of fairest rather than the entire fairest seeming!<br /> With the risk of repeating myself, it does sound cool for a specific scenario but not so much for an entire seeming. Other than that, I do agree with what you say, especially how interesting/educational Gentleman Gamer's videos are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:44:21-07:00","id":516133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=515838#post515838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I have no bloody clue how people don't see the villains in the seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Leadership is a &quot;heroic quality&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's hard to work around subconscious inclinations like that sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:22:59-07:00","id":516209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516122#post516122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way you describe them in how unique they should be they feel more like they should be an entitlement consisting only of fairest rather than the entire fairest seeming!<br /> With the risk of repeating myself, it does sound cool for a specific scenario but not so much for an entire seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this exact argument came up in the Darkling thread too. The idea was that while the lost loyalty angle was cool for a specific character, it was too narrow for the whole seeming and would work better as an Entitlement. I think this comes from taking a writeup that was meant to depict one example of a character of the Seeming and assuming it's meant to be representative of the entire Seeming.<br /> <br /> Take another look at their Blessing. All Fairest regain Clarity from taking charge when they don't actually have a fully-formed plan. Their sense of agency is reinforced by the knowledge that people will follow them, even if they're not actually prepared to lead. What this tells me is tha they're not actually good leaders at all, they just like the feeling of being in a leadership position, especially when they're not a good fit for it. I don't know about you, but to me that speaks volumes about their vanity.<br /> <br /> Now their curse. All Fairest experience a Breaking Point when their ill-conceived plans (unsurprisingly) go awry. I'm not sure why people asaume this means they have to be good guys. I mean, I guess they <i>could</i> be hitting that Breaking Point because they feel guilty about hurting their followers. But I read it as they're breaking because the plan failed horribly. They don't have to care about the people who got hurt, it's just that the fact that people got hurt is pretty undeniable proof that their plan was shitty, and they're not the perfect leader they think they should be. They're reminded &quot;oh yeah, I'm not a great leader. I'm just a useless waste of a life, just like I've always been, and people only look up to because they don't know any better.&quot;<br /> <br /> The background and durance are just one typical example of the type of situations that might lead one to become a Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:01:45-07:00","id":516224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516083#post516083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When I read the part about the Fate placing them in the position of leadership, I thought about stories regarding destiny. Remember Alistaire from Dragon Age? He didn't want to be king at all, like, adamantly opposed to the idea. But just because he was the King's bastard and his only remaining son, his blood mattered more than his wishes. The people who raised him and fought alongside him made the choice for him, that he was going to be king, even though he kept protesting it. That's how I view the idea of a fairest always finding themselves the leader of a situation, even if they don't want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a great example, particularly when you factor in the few directions his story can take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:02:35-07:00","id":516225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516122#post516122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With that out of the way, would please explain what it was that I didn't understand/ignored when I took in the fairest seeming? I've skimmed through the eighteen pages here on the topic and re-read the draft and I still don't really see how else I could interpret them than what I posted above. As I said before, English is not my native language but I've played English roleplaying games for a looong time. I'd love to enjoy the fairest as much as the next person, but first I need to understand what I didn't get about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of belabouring the point, I'm going to try to make sure it comes across clearer in the next draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:11:25-07:00","id":516230,"title":"","content":"It's very interesting to me that I was a big Darkling fan for 1e, but now most of my Darkling concepts seem more appropriate to Fairest, and me more interested in playing a Fairest. I really look forward to seeing the whole thing come together to see what concepts spawn from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:20:29-07:00","id":516381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516209#post516209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, this exact argument came up in the Darkling thread too. The idea was that while the lost loyalty angle was cool for a specific character, it was too narrow for the whole seeming and would work better as an Entitlement. I think this comes from taking a writeup that was meant to depict one example of a character of the Seeming and assuming it's meant to be representative of the entire Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the case, then I am very happy and I am hoping that it will be put much clearer in the final product. One has to remember that the World of Darkness is beloeved by many and if you try and remake it and walking too far away from the original content, people will critisize you for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516209#post516209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take another look at their Blessing. All Fairest regain Clarity from taking charge when they don't actually have a fully-formed plan. Their sense of agency is reinforced by the knowledge that people will follow them, even if they're not actually prepared to lead. What this tells me is tha they're not actually good leaders at all, they just like the feeling of being in a leadership position, especially when they're not a good fit for it. I don't know about you, but to me that speaks volumes about their vanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it should say that they are vain. It shouldn't be up to each and every player to inerpret whether they are vain or not, it should be outlined that the fairest are vain. Imagine it being the first time you pick up a roleplaying book and you decide to pick up world of darkness 2.0. You'd be confused beyond imagination!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516209#post516209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now their curse. All Fairest experience a Breaking Point when their ill-conceived plans (unsurprisingly) go awry. I'm not sure why people asaume this means they have to be good guys. I mean, I guess they <i>could</i> be hitting that Breaking Point because they feel guilty about hurting their followers. But I read it as they're breaking because the plan failed horribly. They don't have to care about the people who got hurt, it's just that the fact that people got hurt is pretty undeniable proof that their plan was shitty, and they're not the perfect leader they think they should be. They're reminded &quot;oh yeah, I'm not a great leader. I'm just a useless waste of a life, just like I've always been, and people only look up to because they don't know any better.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is all how you (not <b>you</b>-you, but rather any reader) interpret it, not how the text is written. It sounds a little bit too much self-pitiful for what I tend to enjoy but once again, the book should tell you what it is like, it shouldn't tell you &quot;what it may be like but go ahead and imagine it in any different interpretion you want&quot;. This isn't a religious scripture after all, it is the core rule-book for a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516209#post516209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The background and durance are just one typical example of the type of situations that might lead one to become a Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope you are right and that the final product will be clear on this point if that is the case! :3<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:55:23-07:00","id":516423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516381#post516381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is the case, then I am very happy and I am hoping that it will be put much clearer in the final product. One has to remember that the World of Darkness is beloeved by many and if you try and remake it and walking too far away from the original content, people will critisize you for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandably. Fortunately, 1st edition will still be around for those who prefer it (I know we've got a few regulars on these forums who do, and I can't fault them for it), and even better, the rules are similar enough between the editions that it's easy to mix and match your favorite parts of either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then it should say that they are vain. It shouldn't be up to each and every player to inerpret whether they are vain or not, it should be outlined that the fairest are vain. Imagine it being the first time you pick up a roleplaying book and you decide to pick up world of darkness 2.0. You'd be confused beyond imagination!<br /> <br /> But this is all how you (not <b>you</b>-you, but rather any reader) interpret it, not how the text is written. It sounds a little bit too much self-pitiful for what I tend to enjoy but once again, the book should tell you what it is like, it shouldn't tell you &quot;what it may be like but go ahead and imagine it in any different interpretion you want&quot;. This isn't a religious scripture after all, it is the core rule-book for a roleplaying game. </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just the opposite of what you were asking for earlier, though? Your complaint was that the writeup was too specific and didn't leave room for different character concepts, but then when I explained a different character concept that could fit within the writeup, you responded that if that's what it's supposed to be it should just say that and not leave it up to interpretation. Sounds self-contradictory to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really hope you are right and that the final product will be clear on this point if that is the case! :3 </div> </div> </div>I'm with you there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-16-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:49:51-07:00","id":516496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516423#post516423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandably. Fortunately, 1st edition will still be around for those who prefer it (I know we've got a few regulars on these forums who do, and I can't fault them for it), and even better, the rules are similar enough between the editions that it's easy to mix and match your favorite parts of either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to play first edition or a mix of first and second. I want a second edition to be awesome and if someone presents a draft and asks for opinions, thoughts and how to improve it, then I will give it. If I walked into a bookshop and wanted to buy a changeling game and then complained that it didn't play out as I wanted it, I'd understand the argument that there's always the first edition. But this isn't the case. Someone made a draft and showed it off, asking for critisism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't that just the opposite of what you were asking for earlier, though? Your complaint was that the writeup was too specific and didn't leave room for different character concepts, but then when I explained a different character concept that could fit within the writeup, you responded that if that's what it's supposed to be it should just say that and not leave it up to interpretation. Sounds self-contradictory to me.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I think you just misunderstood me. I want it to be open, way, way, way more open than how it is presented now. My point was that it is too narrow now, forcing players to drag concepts out of it rather than feeling washed over by the amount of cool conepts that come to mind. Reading Fairest in the older books (I am aware it had a lot more text than this draft) you were offered -loads- of different cool ideas just out of the few pages it were and you certainly didn't feel limited. Here it is lead or don't play fairest.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have grinded my point over and over and I fear it might not have any greater impact on it as a hole because the design choice for Changeling is clearly to give the different seemings more affirmed personalities. Beasts are rebel/gangrel, Fairest are leaders/ventrue and I'm expecting we will see similair roles for the upcomming other seemings. That's not something that a few posts from someone on a forum will change, but I can hope that in future drafts more doors will be opened rather than shut.<br /> Don't make us drag concepts out of your description. Overwhelm us with concepts instead. Changeling is after all the splat that offers us, by far, the most colorful palette to play with.<br /> <br /> A_Newfie who won't spam this thread anymore, I hope!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T18:35:48-07:00","id":516633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516496#post516496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to play first edition or a mix of first and second. I want a second edition to be awesome and if someone presents a draft and asks for opinions, thoughts and how to improve it, then I will give it. If I walked into a bookshop and wanted to buy a changeling game and then complained that it didn't play out as I wanted it, I'd understand the argument that there's always the first edition. But this isn't the case. Someone made a draft and showed it off, asking for critisism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you just misunderstood me. I want it to be open, way, way, way more open than how it is presented now. My point was that it is too narrow now, forcing players to drag concepts out of it rather than feeling washed over by the amount of cool conepts that come to mind. Reading Fairest in the older books (I am aware it had a lot more text than this draft) you were offered -loads- of different cool ideas just out of the few pages it were and you certainly didn't feel limited. Here it is lead or don't play fairest.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have grinded my point over and over and I fear it might not have any greater impact on it as a hole because the design choice for Changeling is clearly to give the different seemings more affirmed personalities. Beasts are rebel/gangrel, Fairest are leaders/ventrue and I'm expecting we will see similair roles for the upcomming other seemings. That's not something that a few posts from someone on a forum will change, but I can hope that in future drafts more doors will be opened rather than shut.<br /> Don't make us drag concepts out of your description. Overwhelm us with concepts instead. Changeling is after all the splat that offers us, by far, the most colorful palette to play with.<br /> <br /> A_Newfie who won't spam this thread anymore, I hope!</div> </div> </div> </div>But where's the line for you? <br /> <br /> Because when you say, &quot;I want it to be open, way, way, way more open than how it is presented now,&quot; the answer that springs to mind is, &quot;Okay, play whatever you want. Use your imagination.&quot; Now, that's clearly not ideal. <br /> <br /> I absolutely disagree that Fairest in 1e were particularly broad. I feel that many of the concepts presented were very overlapped, many of them were too focused on who they were and what they looked like, and not enough about what they're like now at the table. I also really dislike the comparison to Gangrel and Ventrue. As someone that's put in a ton of work on Vampire, I see almost no similarities in Gangrel/Ventrue to Beasts/Fairest. Like almost none, without forcing the issue. <br /> <br /> Changeling does in fact offer a lot of colourful palette. Sure. But one of the problems I saw frequently with 1e games (and I've played a lot, from dozens of chronicles with three to five players, to games with over 100 players) is that many of the character types were just used for &quot;concept posing&quot;, and ceased to deliver anything but less nuanced, more archetypal play. I saw far too many players lean too heavily on what their combination of character options made them look like, and not what that means in the world, in practice. That's not roleplaying; that's a gallery. <br /> <br /> As far as those things go, Fairest aren't leaders. They're people who their peers prop up as leaders. They're perceived as leaders. That's a million concepts. And that's inherently tied to behaviour. That's something that creates action, tension, and drama from moment one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:01:46-07:00","id":516642,"title":"","content":"Now, something I do wanna poke around on: given the somewhat fragile psychological state of changelings in general, I'm curious how the Fairest's curse isn't something that anyone else in their position wouldn't suffer as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:09:05-07:00","id":516647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516633#post516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling does in fact offer a lot of colourful palette. Sure. But one of the problems I saw frequently with 1e games (and I've played a lot, from dozens of chronicles with three to five players, to games with over 100 players) is that many of the character types were just used for &quot;concept posing&quot;, and ceased to deliver anything but less nuanced, more archetypal play. I saw far too many players lean too heavily on what their combination of character options made them look like, and not what that means in the world, in practice. That's not roleplaying; that's a gallery.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I never felt fully satisfied with any of my Changeling characters in 1e. The books inspired me to create a lot of very cool character concepts, but when it came to fleshing them out and developing them into full-fledged characters, I always struggled. I could never quite put my finger on why I had so much trouble developing a deep Changeling character, but I think this hits the nail right on the head. There were so many options for cool combinations, but it was too easy to just use &quot;I'm a dual kith something something of the whatever court&quot; and just kind of brush over who this person <i>was</i> and what they <i>did. </i>I can't tell you how glad it makes me to see this issue properly articulated, and to know that it's being specifically addressed in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T21:22:06-07:00","id":516697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516642#post516642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, something I do wanna poke around on: given the somewhat fragile psychological state of changelings in general, I'm curious how the Fairest's curse isn't something that anyone else in their position wouldn't suffer as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, we don't know how Clarity works yet. It's possible that the Seeming Banes may just make these things <i>guaranteed</i> Breaking Points instead of adding them as completely new Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T21:40:06-07:00","id":516715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516697#post516697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, we don't know how Clarity works yet. It's possible that the Seeming Banes may just make these things <i>guaranteed</i> Breaking Points instead of adding them as completely new Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember David speaking at one point about how, in 2e, building the Durance is part of building the character. Kith and Seeming play into that in obvious ways (what the character was made to be and how the character broke free), but I suspect they aren't the extent of it. My guess at this point is that the nature of and circumstances around one's Durance will define some more individualized Clarity Breaking Points, and likely more besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T21:47:11-07:00","id":516719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516697#post516697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, we don't know how Clarity works yet. It's possible that the Seeming Banes may just make these things <i>guaranteed</i> Breaking Points instead of adding them as completely new Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had this big ol' post(Well, okay, maybe I need to reconsider what that means, because it's quite smaller than what others would consider my big posts) sent out to David on the subject, so if it's literally just because I forgot to read something out as &quot;AUTO-DROP&quot;, I'm going to be so annoyed with myself.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm going to re-read it now to see if that's what's intended.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, no, It does not seem like it's automatic. If it was, that would instantly clear it up. It would also run the risk of &quot;probably too much&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-17-2015, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T22:02:53-07:00","id":516751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516719#post516719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had this big ol' post(Well, okay, maybe I need to reconsider what that means, because it's quite smaller than what others would consider my big posts) sent out to David on the subject, so if it's literally just because I forgot to read something out as &quot;AUTO-DROP&quot;, I'm going to be so annoyed with myself.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm going to re-read it now to see if that's what's intended.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, no, It does not seem like it's automatic. If it was, that would instantly clear it up. It would also run the risk of &quot;probably too much&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I meant guaranteed Breaking Point as in you're guaranteed to have it as a Breaking Point, not that you're guaranteed to lose Clarity for encountering it as a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> So, for example, if it works like Humanity where Breaking Points are tied to specific levels, maybe the Seeming Curse Breaking Points are all Breaking Points at Clarity 5 for everyone, but your Seeming makes one of them a Breaking Point at any level for you. Or, if Clarity works more like Integrity where Breaking Points are always Breaking Points no matter your level, but you choose certain Breaking Points that are specific to your character at character creation, maybe the Seeming Curse Breaking Points are all available as options to any character, but your Seeming determines one that you <i>must</i> chose. We just don't know enough about how Clarity and its Breaking Points work to safely assume that the Seeming Curses imply that those situations <i>can't </i>be Breaking Points for characters of other Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T22:04:13-07:00","id":516754,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes more sense.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Man, I am just not reading things right right now. This is what I get for eating Little Ceaser's pizza.<br /> <br /> Arcane Arts Breaking Points<br /> <br /> Clarity 1 Breaking point: Eating Little Ceaser's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T00:47:59-07:00","id":516850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516633#post516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But where's the line for you?<br /> <br /> Because when you say, &quot;I want it to be open, way, way, way more open than how it is presented now,&quot; the answer that springs to mind is, &quot;Okay, play whatever you want. Use your imagination.&quot; Now, that's clearly not ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but there has to be a point in between &quot;Do whatever you want&quot; and &quot;play the leader&quot;. Those are two ends of the extremes. When I tried to make sense out of one fifth of the freehold being leaders, I was told that one fifth wouldn't be fairest. I'd love to hear numbers on roughly how many of each seeming that are what, I have always assumed that they are sort of roughly equal in numbers. To take an example from right now, I'm playing on the Wanton Wicked roleplaying website and there are eight fairest characters active who play on the website. Out of these only two could theoretically be percieved as leaders, but even then it is stretching it a bit as one of them is a ballet dance teacher for kids and the next one owns a nightclub with mortal employees. I just don't want to see these other concepts die down because of wording and focus in the description we are given on fairest in the final product.<br /> <br /> To underline, it is absolutely fine that people <b>percieve</b> them as leaders, even if they aren't. It's not fine if a freehold only consists of 6 fairest in total and all of them are monarchs or CEOs. I want a beast autumn monarch, an elemental ice queen and a spring fairest to rule my freeholds, not four fairest!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as those things go, Fairest aren't leaders. They're people who their peers prop up as leaders. They're perceived as leaders. That's a million concepts. And that's inherently tied to behaviour. That's something that creates action, tension, and drama from moment one. </div> </div> </div>That's great! Then the draft just needs to be reworded so that it becomes more clear on that point.<br /> I feel so relieved already :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T02:36:12-07:00","id":516900,"title":"","content":"I think you're getting a bit hung up on &quot;leader&quot; having to mean &quot;rulers in Changeling society&quot; or &quot;super important person.&quot;<br /> <br /> The three example concepts in the write-up all don't go there as what is core to the concept as a Fairest. A lawyer that's working with poor families and has political pressure to run for mayor; not monarch of the Freehold or a senior partner in a prestigious firm. A guy the prowls the back alleys vigilante style.<br /> <br /> Yes. Leading a classroom as a teacher, or running a business, are forms of leadership that apply to the Fairest.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it is likely that there will be 1e concepts that make more sense with different splats in 2e. I had a Summer Wizened that makes more sense from what we know of 2e as a Fairest. That's fine. It's a new edition. A few concepts shifting around which Seeming makes the most sense isn't restricting concepts.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that with the major changes to the relationship between Kith and Seeming, and the major changes to how Courts will be presented, a lot of assumptions about them from 1e need to be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T02:41:01-07:00","id":516901,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I somehow missed Heavy Arms posting the thrust of my point, here -- good show, there -- but gonna post it, anyway.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516850#post516850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take an example from right now, I'm playing on the Wanton Wicked roleplaying website and there are eight fairest characters active who play on the website. Out of these only two could theoretically be percieved as leaders, but even then it is stretching it a bit as one of them is a ballet dance teacher for kids and the next one owns a nightclub with mortal employees. I just don't want to see these other concepts die down because of wording and focus in the description we are given on fairest in the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is definitely not a safe assumption that all characters who fit a 1e Seeming will automatically be members of the same 2e Seeming. This is regardless of how broad or narrow one finds the Fairest Seeming.<br /> <br /> Like, take the Beasts. 1e Beasts are about clawing one's way <i>out of</i> animal instinct to get free, while 2e Beasts are about throwing themselves <i>into</i> animal instinct to get their freedom. Those are completely reversed narratives. 1e Beast is just what you pick if you want an animal-like character, while 2e Beast is what you pick if you want a character who flaunts social taboos. Those two groups will have some overlap, but it is guaranteed not to be absolute. Some 1e Beasts are just going to be better fits for different 2e Seemings. Case in point, I had a lot of fun with Beast characters in 1e, but the type of character 2e Beast represents is just not something I'm interested in playing. When all the 2e Seeming particulars are teased/written, I'll either find 2e Seemings that fit the characters in question or be disappointed and go Seemingless instead.<br /> <br /> This was always going to be true for all the Seemings. It just isn't much of a narrative loss (when it is at all) because 2e Kiths are dissociated from 2e Seemings. 2e Kiths basically fulfill the default narrative role that 1e Kith and 1e Seeming used to fulfill together. Character concepts from 1e aren't less valid, they just might be differently represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T05:50:03-07:00","id":517884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=516633#post516633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As far as those things go, Fairest aren't leaders. They're people who their peers prop up as leaders. They're perceived as leaders. That's a million concepts. And that's inherently tied to behaviour. That's something that creates action, tension, and drama from moment one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the opposite direction, what if the player wants to play a Fairest as a leader? The draft seems to support it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Character Creation</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Fairest are, natural leaders, and of course rapidly and easily pick up the skills to go with that. Unless he actively avoids it, many Fairest show a knack for politics and law. Many Fairest as well, end up developing specific knowledge of the logistical, if not mystical workings of Oaths. No one is exactly sure why. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So if the character actually is a leader and not bluffing, does he still get the Blessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T08:52:40-07:00","id":518096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=517884#post517884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going from the opposite direction, what if the player wants to play a Fairest as a leader? The draft seems to support it.<br /> <br /> So if the character actually is a leader and not bluffing, does he still get the Blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can absolutely play a leader. I'll be fussing the wording, but it's just not a requirement. <br /> <br /> And yeah. I'll be working on that wording for the Blessing, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T22:13:15-07:00","id":518928,"title":"","content":"Something that i still dont get is why are Fairest thrown to leadership positions, what is it that they got that draws people to them??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T03:42:17-07:00","id":519245,"title":"","content":"&quot;Agency&quot; is the new buzzword, but how long before it becomes dated? The whole emphasis on it seems to be to counteract the view of C:tL that you play a victim, but if the Seeming gives you an unremovable form of PTSD, isn't that counterproductive? Is playing without a Seeming an option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T04:54:18-07:00","id":519429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=519245#post519245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Agency&quot; is the new buzzword, but how long before it becomes dated? The whole emphasis on it seems to be to counteract the view of C:tL that you play a victim, but if the Seeming gives you an unremovable form of PTSD, isn't that counterproductive? Is playing without a Seeming an option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing without Seeming is an option. I don't know if it's specifically mentioned in the outline, but it's been discussed numerous times. <br /> <br /> Seeming curses are NOT PTSD. They're Seeming curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:55:28-07:00","id":519580,"title":"","content":"Building a little on that, it is worth keeping in mind that as a creatures of stories and dreams now, you don't have a one-to-one equivalent exchange from human psychology to faerie characterization-it's a blurry, messy affair.<br /> <br /> Given that Integrity is basically 1E's Clarity in several ways, I assume then there's a reason that we still have Clarity instead of integrity, and by and large that's because faerie tale curses and blessings are a fact of life for you now. Actually, they are pretty much a fact of <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=501370#post501370\">This post seems all the more relevant.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-19-2015, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:02:17-07:00","id":519992,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Clarity - Is there any discussion on that as of yet? I think it would be interesting if Clarity worked similarly to Harmony in WTF2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T16:06:15-07:00","id":520082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=519992#post519992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Clarity - Is there any discussion on that as of yet? I think it would be interesting if Clarity worked similarly to Harmony in WTF2.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points?p=300013#post300013\">I clearly disagree.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T23:38:51-07:00","id":520566,"title":"","content":"I haven't read WTF2, so I'm not sure how Harmony works in the new ed, but it definitely seems like Clarity is going to fluctuate a lot more than it did in 1e, given the way these Blessings/Curses work.<br /> <br /> Personally, I felt like Clarity was something of a balancing act in 1e. From a strictly mechanical perspective, players wanted to keep Clarity high enough to retain Kenning and not suffer from penalties to perception, but didn't generally want to take it up so high that their ability to use their special powers and advantages was compromised. From a rp perspective, it was about balancing stability and power and, also, balancing excitement and wonder with calm and comfort. If your Clarity got too low, you risked losing touch with the life, the world, that you struggled so hard to get back to (and with your own sanity). If you maintained a very high Clarity, you did so at the cost of mystical tools (Dreamwalking, the Hedge, Tokens) that could not only improve your life, but could save you from being recaptured or killed should your Keeper or a Privateer or Loyalist come for you.<br /> <br /> A Changeling's fae side is an important part of who they are, so I'd love to see a Clarity system that focuses a little more on striking a balance. (To clarify, I mean I'd like a system in which striking a balance is represented by a high Clarity score, as opposed to 1e Clarity, where striking a balance might be desirable for other reasons, but was represented by a middling score in Clarity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T23:59:49-07:00","id":520599,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about what a Motley with two different Fairest in it might look like, and it made me think of the Walking Dead (the tv series not the comics). In the current seasons, you've got a handful of leaders that the group looks up to. Rick is like a Fairest who embraces his leadership role (at least in part, because he doesn't feel that anyone else can do a better job). As a result, he pretty regularly loses Clarity when things go sideways- talking to his dead wife on the phone, chewing on people's jugulars, etc. But then he pulls the group out of a tough situation and gets his psychological ducks back in a row - a Clarity gain. It's up and down. He's probably lost more than he's gained, but he's a good leader and he manages to eek out victory often enough that he's relatively stable most of the time. Meanwhile, you've got Daryl. Everybody looks up to him and follows his lead, but he absolutely does not want to be in charge. Sometimes, he ends up having to lead a small group, but mostly he keeps to himself, lets Rick do the leading and either lends him support or stays out of his way. He's a Fairest too, but he actively avoids both his Blessing and Curse. Luckily, he has another Fairest he can defer to when people need a leader, so he avoids making the plans that get people hurt. On the rare occasion when he is forced to lead, he wings it and usually succeeds. As a result he's gained Clarity, albeit slowly, over the course of the series. He's more self-assured and stable than when we met him in season 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T01:46:54-07:00","id":520983,"title":"","content":"Harmony 2e works by making the mid-point (5) the most ideal position to aim for. You can't spend XP on Harmony, and it changes have having breaking points in both directions (Flesh and Spirit). You can (somewhat similar to your Walking Dead example) accept going up and down a lot and try to stay near the middle as much as possible, or try to avoid too much breaking points in either direction to be stable in the middle. The Walking Dead isn't a bad example for WtF 2e in general with the main cast as the pack. They all struggle with needing to be hard survivors in the zombie apocalypse with forces them to make brutal choices (breaking towards Spirit in Harmony, not exactly, but not too far off), while trying to find ways to ground themselves and keep their humanity (breaking towards Flesh). Brutally killing enemy raiders juxtaposed against sitting back and having a bit tin of pudding.<br /> <br /> As for Fairest, I think there's an interesting case of a lot of the main cast of the Walking Dead to be examples of different takes on being a Fairest. A lot of them, even if they're not the overt leader that Rick is, have things that they &quot;do&quot; and everyone generally defers to them on. I think you can generally cluster them into three basic groups: the natural leaders that take the reins (Rick, Shane, Dale, Herschel, Abraham, the Governor even), the ones that rejected other people much to their mental detriment and might be on the path of balance by embracing being looked up to for their reliability (Daryl as noted, but Michonne as well, Sasha maybe, Gabriel though not really doing well with it), and the ones that fell neatly into a balance of not being leaders but still having a vital skill that puts them in charge for specific situations (Glenn, Carol, Eugene, Tyrese).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T01:59:32-07:00","id":521081,"title":"","content":"That sounds exactly like what I'd like to see for Changeling! Breaking toward Fae or Human nature is exactly what I'm hoping for.<br /> <br /> I was primarily thinking of characters that were sort of looked to in every situation, as opposed to just when their focus comes up. More so than everybody else, it seems like when Rick makes a call they aren't sure about, people kind of go &quot;what does Daryl think&quot;. Michonne and Carol had major leadership roles in the last season, but I think they fit much better as a Beast (Michonne) and a Darkling (Carol). You could definitely make the case for a lot of the characters you mentioned being Fairest, for sure. I think the Governor would totally be a fairest. Hands down. Discussing the best Seemings for the whole WD gang could really get out of control, though, so we should probably stop that. The main takeaway is this: there are a lot more concepts that fit the Fairest Seeming than some people give it credit for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:09:27-07:00","id":521730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=521081#post521081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds exactly like what I'd like to see for Changeling! Breaking toward Fae or Human nature is exactly what I'm hoping for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already kind of ranted about this once, but I'll be arsed if I can find the post, so in summary: the Harmony design does not fit Clarity at all. It works as a balancing scale for Werewolves by virtue of what they inherently are - both spirit and flesh, both man and wolf, able to live in either world but denied the chance of existing simultaneously in both. Clarity is not that. Clarity is your grip on the real world, it is your lifeline as a human after having Arcadia carved into you. Changelings don't want to &quot;balance&quot; their fae and human sides. Faerie is a land of illusion that draws the Lost ever closer to its fantastic narrative and ever further from their independent identity. It is beautiful - as beautiful as madness, and madness separates you from your fellow people and pushes you to see dreams and reality as equal.<br /> <br /> At least based on what it represented in 1e, which does not seem to have changed that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-20-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:39:21-07:00","id":521792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=521081#post521081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds exactly like what I'd like to see for Changeling! Breaking toward Fae or Human nature is exactly what I'm hoping for..</div> </div> </div> </div>My house rule topic should interest you then - come, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points\">see and talk here</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:49:56-07:00","id":521803,"title":"","content":"And as mentioned before, see why it's a <i>terrible idea for Clarity</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:58:00-07:00","id":521885,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Arcane here. Just because in 1e there were some disadvantages to having high Clarity does not mean balance is the goal for the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T08:06:36-07:00","id":521896,"title":"","content":"Eh. Not doing that. I appreciate the hack's existence. But Clarity's about having more clarity, not achieving a balance between two things. <br /> <br /> It's not PTSD. It's not a place between fae and human. I'll try to chatter on it soon, or at least post a working draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:26:26-07:00","id":521953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=521730#post521730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Changelings don't want to &quot;balance&quot; their fae and human sides.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=521885#post521885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm with Arcane here. Just because in 1e there were some disadvantages to having high Clarity does not mean balance is the goal for the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really blame people for thinking 1e Clarity is a balancing act when that's what it explicitly states in the main book. Some quotes from the corebook (emphasis mine, obviously):<br /> <br /> &quot;In order to thrive as Changelings, each individual <b>must maintain somewhat of a balance between his human side and his fae self. To ignore is human side is devastating to a Changeling's Clarity</b>. He begins to lose any sense of what is real and what is merely the discontented grumblings and terrified shrieks of his wounded soul. Delusions, hallucinations, depression, compulsions, phobias and psychosomatic ailments all wait down that road, greedily anticipating the arrival of a Changeling who eschews the mortal world too greatly. Considering the dangers that await those who have immersed themselves solely in fae matters, the logical reaction would seem to be to err in the other direction. <b>The other extreme, however, is, if anything, more dangerous</b>. While low-Clarity Changelings are in danger of losing their sanity, those who eschew the fae world entirely put themselves in danger of withdrawal-like symptoms as their fae side slowly starves.&quot; -CtL corebook p. 26<br /> <br /> &quot;Their time in Faerie swept away the certainty of the real world, and upon returning they must learn to <b>balance the human and fae realities</b>, hopefully without losing themselves in the process. This balance, called Clarity, is one of the most important factors in a Changeling's life. Too much Clarity, and he is in danger of losing touch with his fae self. Too little, and he risks insanity and finds himself uncertain of the reality of the world around him.&quot; - CtL corebook p. 28<br /> <br /> &quot;The concept of Morality as it applies to mortals is replaced by the concept of Clarity, respresenting the character's ability to distinguish the solidity of the mortal world from Faerie and to <b>reconcile the two disparate halves of his nature</b>.&quot; - CtL corebook p. 75<br /> <br /> &quot;Upon returning to Earth, most changelings find themselves <b>walking a fine line between two worlds</b>.&quot; - CtL corebook p. 91<br /> <br /> &quot;Clarity tracks this <b>delicate balance between the mundane world and the maddening realms of Glamour </b>.&quot; -CtL corebook p. 91 again.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acts that trigger a breaking point may be morally reprehensible or not. The true measure is whether or not these acts might awaken psychic trauams that distort the changeling's perspective, or push the Changeling too far down the path of <b>ignoring one of her two distinct selves</b>.&quot; - CtL corebook p. 91 one more time.<br /> <br /> The problem was that the descriptive text frequently talked about Clarity as being able to distinguish between the two aspects of one's life clearly, without ignoring or focusing on either one more than the other, but the breaking points given for Clarity loss skewed heavily towards ignoring ones fae side to maintain higher clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:56:07-07:00","id":521967,"title":"","content":"The problem with assuming that Clarity ought to work like 2e Harmony because a higher rating means you're closer to a mundane human mindset is that <i>they all work like that.</i> Harmony gets a pass on that because the otherworld it trucks with is nigh-omnipresent, regularly attempts to meddle with aspects of normal reality orthogonal to the characters, and not actively threatening to consume werewolves' minds from every corner of their perspective. The nearest point of similarity I'd say is actually <i>viable</i> is the fact that you can theoretically be rehabilitated from 2eHarmony 0 and there are rules for a similar activity in 1eClarity along with the precedent of Charlatans gaining Clarity.<br /> <br /> You'll notice that those withdrawal-like symptoms are manifest in the rules and hacks for <i>Glamour</i>, not Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:11:28-07:00","id":521985,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that within 2E's paradigm, there are only two critters who have this shifting/non-standard Integrity stat setup, those being Werewolves and Beasts*.<br /> <br /> Both of those <i>literally were never human to begin with</i>.<br /> <br /> Everything else? It has a human root, even Prometheans**. That human frame of references helps provide the framing of the Integrity stats.<br /> <br /> This is important, because while changelings are now and forever faeries, they have a human mindset-and Clarity is the fight to keep the Wyrd from warping their minds so they can find security in the clarity of a human perspective.<br /> <br /> This is a fucking fight to see things as they are. Clarity is not a fucking balancing act between your Fae life and your Human Life, it's a internal brawl to see things as they are. Yes, involvement with the Fae means you'll likely fall into low clarity, but that's the price you pay.<br /> <br /> FOr fuck's sake, YOU ARE LOSING YOUR MIND AND YOUR STORY AS A CHANGELING. The 'middle road' you all propose lies in staying as far from the fucking edge of insanity as possible, keeping the Wyrd under fucking heel and going where you will.<br /> <br /> I need to stop. I'm sick of this argument. Harmony-based Clarity is <i>fucking stupid</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: THough, as I also said in that thread, if you wanted to restructure the game around a new Integrity stat that functions like Harmony, that would be cool-I'd be for that. Just Don't push that idea off to Clarity, because Clarity doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, calmer now,I can come in and do those two notes I missed.<br /> <br /> *No word on Sin-Eaters yet, but in that case you have two personalities literally arguing over what to do and how to live life after death-Harmony works there,and we also haven't seen it yet.<br /> <br /> **It's just that in their case, the entire bar is flipped around,so the framework is being aspired to, not just remembered.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the outburst, it's just-gah, I'm stressed out, but more importantly, I really don't like Clarity-as-Harmony, and I feel like Errol, Satchel, and I pretty soundly explained why it doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-20-2015, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:12:57-07:00","id":521987,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the tendency towards low glamour is a consequence of high Clarity, so they're connected.<br /> The book vacillates between talking about Changelings needing to find a balance between high and low Clarity, and describing Clarity itself as that balance. It's inconsistent. The point is, it does talk about balancing the two aspects, fae and human, quite a bit in relation to Clarity. It's presented as the default for balance to be most characters' goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:20:24-07:00","id":521995,"title":"","content":"Again, I don't know the 2e Harmony system, I'd just like a Clarity system that focuses on balancing the dual natures, as opposed to the 1e system where the writing emphasized striking a balance (see the above quotes) and high Clarity represented a mostly undesirable unbalance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:26:27-07:00","id":522002,"title":"","content":"But hey, as far as 2e is concerned, I'm going to reserve judgement until I see what they have in mind.<br /> <br /> Just don't try to tell me that balance wasn't a goal in 1e when nearly every entry for Clarity in the core talks about the need to achieve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:44:06-07:00","id":522013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522002#post522002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But hey, as far as 2e is concerned, I'm going to reserve judgement until I see what they have in mind.<br /> <br /> Just don't try to tell me that balance wasn't a goal in 1e when nearly every entry for Clarity in the core talks about the need to achieve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I have had to say multiple times in the 2e-speculation threads for Werewolf and Promethean is that the 1e corebook is generally a terrible deciding metric for what 2e is or ought to be like as a refinement of the 1e version of the game.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite gamelines is Geist, a game that has directly contradictory text <i>within the only book it doesn't share with another line.</i><br /> <br /> I'm still halfway through the third supplement of Changeling 1e and haven't encountered anything that picks up and runs with the &quot;balance&quot; talk from the core.<br /> <br /> Like, at all. Editing and development miss things or change direction from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:01:09-07:00","id":522029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=521985#post521985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that within 2E's paradigm, there are only two critters who have this shifting/non-standard Integrity stat setup, those being Werewolves and Beasts*.<br /> <br /> Both of those <i>literally were never human to begin with</i>.<br /> <br /> Everything else? It has a human root, even Prometheans**. That human frame of references helps provide the framing of the Integrity stats.<br /> <br /> This is important, because while changelings are now and forever faeries, they have a human mindset-and Clarity is the fight to keep the Wyrd from warping their minds so they can find security in the clarity of a human perspective.<br /> <br /> This is a fucking fight to see things as they are. Clarity is not a fucking balancing act between your Fae life and your Human Life, it's a internal brawl to see things as they are. Yes, involvement with the Fae means you'll likely fall into low clarity, but that's the price you pay.<br /> <br /> FOr fuck's sake, YOU ARE LOSING YOUR MIND AND YOUR STORY AS A CHANGELING. The 'middle road' you all propose lies in staying as far from the fucking edge of insanity as possible, keeping the Wyrd under fucking heel and going where you will.<br /> <br /> I need to stop. I'm sick of this argument. Harmony-based Clarity is <i>fucking stupid</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: THough, as I also said in that thread, if you wanted to restructure the game around a new Integrity stat that functions like Harmony, that would be cool-I'd be for that. Just Don't push that idea off to Clarity, because Clarity doesn't work like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it expressly states that it <b>is</b> balancing act. <br /> <br /> &quot;...they must learn to balance the human and fae realities, hopefully without losing themselves in the process. This balance, called Clarity...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not about keeping the Wyrd under heel; it's about making peace between the two sides of the Changeling's self.<br /> <br /> &quot;... the concept of Clarity, representing the character's ability to distinguish the solidity of the mortal world from Faerie and to <b>reconcile the two disparate halves of his nature</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> And breaking points shouldn't just be about pushing back against the Wyrd; they're also about keeping in touch with it.<br /> <br /> &quot;... [breaking points] push the Changeling too far down the path of ignoring one of her two distinct selves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it's about seeing things the way they really are, but that includes the fae side that the &quot;human perspective&quot; can't see. High Clarity should mean realizing that objective, human reality is not the only reality that exists, or matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:09:17-07:00","id":522042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522029#post522029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it expressly states that it <b>is</b> balancing act.<br /> <br /> &quot;...they must learn to balance the human and fae realities, hopefully without losing themselves in the process. This balance, called Clarity...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not about keeping the Wyrd under heel; it's about making peace between the two sides of the Changeling's self.<br /> <br /> &quot;... the concept of Clarity, representing the character's ability to distinguish the solidity of the mortal world from Faerie and to <b>reconcile the two disparate halves of his nature</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> And breaking points shouldn't just be about pushing back against the Wyrd; they're also about keeping in touch with it.<br /> <br /> &quot;... [breaking points] push the Changeling too far down the path of ignoring one of her two distinct selves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, it's about seeing things the way they really are, but that includes the fae side that the &quot;human perspective&quot; can't see. High Clarity should mean realizing that objective, human reality is not the only reality that exists, or matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>THere's a difference in conversation here, not the least of which seems to be a limit of research. I don't know how many books you own, or have read-I own all of them and have read them many times over.<br /> <br /> I don't want to go into it right now-and can't go into it right now, because I have school work to do all damn day-but for now I want to remind everyone that this is a <i>psychological horror</i> game. If this were a video game, <i>Clarity would be your health bar</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:15:44-07:00","id":522062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522042#post522042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to go into it right now-and can't go into it right now, because I have school work to do all damn day-but for now I want to remind everyone that this is a <i>psychological horror</i> game. If this were a video game, <i>Clarity would be your health bar</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the Lost Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:18:44-07:00","id":522078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522013#post522013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things I have had to say multiple times in the 2e-speculation threads for Werewolf and Promethean is that the 1e corebook is generally a terrible deciding metric for what 2e is or ought to be like as a refinement of the 1e version of the game.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite gamelines is Geist, a game that has directly contradictory text <i>within the only book it doesn't share with another line.</i><br /> <br /> I'm still halfway through the third supplement of Changeling 1e and haven't encountered anything that picks up and runs with the &amp;quot;balance&amp;quot; talk from the core.<br /> <br /> Like, at all. Editing and development miss things or change direction from time to time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point about 1e vs 2e. Like I said, I'm going to reserve judgement about the new Clarity until I see it.<br /> <br /> Geist was a mess. I think I have more house rules for it than there are official rules. Still love the concept, though.<br /> <br /> I don't personally remember the supplements contradicting the balance aspect, but it's been years since I read them in full. Either way, It's not fair to totally discount the core book just because future supplements might take a slightly different approach. Remember that many players may never read anything else and might run rich and lengthy campaigns using just the core. If it changed direction over time that's fine, but it's not grounds to dismiss the original approach as invalid or to tell a player that liked the presentation in the core that their version of Clarity is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:40:37-07:00","id":522143,"title":"","content":"Actually, why the fuck are we even continuing this? Dave already said that's not what's being done, So why keep going on about it. We're done, moving on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:45:14-07:00","id":522145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522042#post522042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THere's a difference in conversation here, not the least of which seems to be a limit of research. I don't know how many books you own, or have read-I own all of them and have read them many times over.<br /> <br /> I don't want to go into it right now-and can't go into it right now, because I have school work to do all damn day-but for now I want to remind everyone that this is a <i>psychological horror</i> game. If this were a video game, <i>Clarity would be your health bar</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have all the books, it's just been awhile since I read the supplements cover to cover. I'm reading through Rites of Spring now, and it presents Clarity in a very different light than the core does. The RoS version of Clarity seems like what you're referencing. In my mind, both are valid approaches, given the &quot;toolbox approach&quot; of the new WoD. Personally, I prefer the &quot;balancing your dual nature&quot; approach from the core over the &quot;overcoming psychological trauma&quot; version presented in RoS. You're obviously very passionate about the RoS version, and that's cool, but I don't think it's fair to tell those who prefer what's written in the core that they're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:40:28-07:00","id":522325,"title":"","content":"Wow, I love changeling, but I don't like this take on Fairest at all. I apologize the writer of the second edition if I am too blunt in the following-- I hope that you can read it with some professional distance despite my strong feelings on the subject.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with WoD is that it tends to repeat the stereotypes of those original vampire clans too closely. Don't get me wrong, I like the Vampire system and set up, but I just don't think every other part of WoD needs to mimic that system too closely. That's one of the wonderful things about Changeling is that with the Courts, Seemings and Kiths, the characters just doesn't fit into that classic Vampire mode of Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, etc. With the addition of leadership as an attribute, what we are left with is Fairest= Ventrue, and that just bores me to death. <br /> <br /> The wonderful thing about Changeling the Lost was that it drew very knowledgeably from world-wide fairy tales and myths. While some fairest are leaders-- has anyone read the Mary Poppins novels? She's endlessly vain and powerful-- and clearly harvesting glamour from those kids. Not all fairest are leaders: in Snow White we get two Fairest, Snow and the Queen. Perhaps the evil Queen is a leader, but she did marry into the position. Snow definitely not leading the dwarves, since they will keep her if she agrees to:<span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;take care of our house, cook, make the beds, wash, sew, and knit, and if you will keep everything neat and clean.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> I'm surprised when reading other comments that any Changeling campaign would discount Fairest. They are after all, the most pretty, desirable people by definition, and they get bonuses to persuade to boot. Mortals leap up to open doors and buy them drinks (or cars, jewelry, etc.). Changelings are not immune to their charms-- how better to cement your court status than having a Fairest on your arm? How better to move up the ranks in your court than being (or being with) someone who can seduce heartlessly? To be Fairest is to be more free of the memories of durance than any other Changeling (or at least among the freest)-- as a result, they are more like the Fae than anyone. Every Fairest is a diamond designed to cut anyone who tries to hold onto him or her. In my campaigns, most groups love to have a Fairest (despite the prima donna attitude) because he or she is so great at gathering information, getting favors from strangers in emergencies, getting along with people when in a new place, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:51:21-07:00","id":522338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522325#post522325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all fairest are leaders: in Snow White we get two Fairest, Snow and the Queen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snow is, IMO, kithless under this new paradigm, she has no agency and is a prize to be won. Yeah, she's &quot;the fairest (prettiest)&quot;, but that doesn't mean she's <i>a</i> Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:36:11-07:00","id":522559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522325#post522325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I love changeling, but I don't like this take on Fairest at all. I apologize the writer of the second edition if I am too blunt in the following-- I hope that you can read it with some professional distance despite my strong feelings on the subject.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with WoD is that it tends to repeat the stereotypes of those original vampire clans too closely. Don't get me wrong, I like the Vampire system and set up, but I just don't think every other part of WoD needs to mimic that system too closely. That's one of the wonderful things about Changeling is that with the Courts, Seemings and Kiths, the characters just doesn't fit into that classic Vampire mode of Ventrue, Toreador, Brujah, etc. With the addition of leadership as an attribute, what we are left with is Fairest= Ventrue, and that just bores me to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sigh*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but this is an incredibly shallow reading of both the Ventrue and this draft of Fairest. I can understand not enjoying the focus on leadership (although, as has been discussed in this thread at great length, they're more about having leadership thrust upon them because people can't help but look up to them due to their Fae likeness, rather than actually being inclined to lead, let alone being good at it). But comparing them to Ventrue is putting way more emphasis on what is a very small part of both splats than it deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:39:10-07:00","id":522562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522559#post522559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sigh*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but this is an incredibly shallow reading of both the Ventrue and this draft of Fairest. I can understand not enjoying the focus on leadership (although, as has been discussed in this thread at great length, they're more about having leadership thrust upon them because people can't help but look up to them due to their Fae likeness, rather than actually being inclined to lead, let alone being good at it). But comparing them to Ventrue is putting way more emphasis on what is a very small part of both splats than it deserves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, more please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:58:45-07:00","id":522571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522325#post522325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the addition of leadership as an attribute, what we are left with is Fairest= Ventrue, and that just bores me to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>My knowledge of Changeling is weak compared to others here, but if you're referring to the Requiem Ventrue I would have thought they were more about power and exercising it for its own sake than leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":".  Missing word 05-21-2015, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:36:49-07:00","id":522597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522559#post522559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sigh*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but this is an incredibly shallow reading of both the Ventrue and this draft of Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it what you wish, but it still not an impression that just a single person has gotten.<br /> Of the players who I normally play pen and paper with (who are not present on this forum) they all more or less share the same agreement regarding the status of fairest. And evidently some people on this forum who read the draft feel the same.<br /> Still, I'll bite my tongue and wait for the next draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","user":"A_Newfie","date":". 05-20-2015, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:16:53-07:00","id":522680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522597#post522597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Call it what you wish, but it still not an impression that just a single person has gotten.<br /> Of the players who I normally play pen and paper with (who are not present on this forum) they all more or less share the same agreement regarding the status of fairest. And evidently some people on this forum who read the draft feel the same.<br /> Still, I'll bite my tongue and wait for the next draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. This is not a new issue, people have always compared splats of other lines to the Vampire Clans. And they're not <i>wrong</i>, exactly. If you ignore the context of the gamelines and distil every splat down to the most basic possible archetype, then yeah, pretty much every line has a &quot;fighter&quot; splat, a &quot;leader&quot; splat, a &quot;sneaky&quot; splat, etc. That's why I said it was a shallow reading, not an inaccurate one. The problem is, simplifying the splats to that degree does a huge disservice to the game, because it throws out a great deal of depth and nuance in favor of presenting the splats in terms of simple, easy to understand archetypes. Not to mention there just aren't a whole lot of fundamental character archetypes when you get down to it, so if you're looking at it from that perspective <i>of course</i> you're going to find a lot in common across various sources. You could also say the Fairest in 1e were just Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-20-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:25:47-07:00","id":522709,"title":"","content":"If the Second Editions coming out have taught me anything, it's that a large part of the fanbase tends towards shallow readings.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem, per se- from what I've seen, it encourages the writers and devs to push for greater clarity in their writing and presentation, which makes the games more accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T18:39:21-07:00","id":522748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522709#post522709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Second Editions coming out have taught me anything, it's that a large part of the fanbase tends towards shallow readings.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem, per se- from what I've seen, it encourages the writers and devs to push for greater clarity in their writing and presentation, which makes the games more accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I have no problem with shallow readings <i>per se</i>, I just think it's a little odd to look for the archetype in each splat and then complain that the splats are all too archetypal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T00:42:32-07:00","id":523001,"title":"","content":"Uh, when are the other Seemings getting released? I remember seeing that they were expected to come out during the next week, but I think we're beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:30:56-07:00","id":523126,"title":"","content":"David's having to deal with life things. It's brutal. Mundane, but brutal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:27:54-07:00","id":523152,"title":"","content":"Do you work/have you worked for Oynx Path? I'm only asking as you've commented on a lot of things here, you have an Icon in the Comment section on the website (and not the Forums), and you've been a bit passionate about everything so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:45:59-07:00","id":523167,"title":"","content":"Shit, they're onto me. ABANDON FORUMS!<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I have not worked for Onyx Path yet, though I'm confident that I will some day. I am currently a passionate fan of at least eight years, particularly about Changeling*, and I keep my ear on the ground in a lot of places and as a result sometimes hear snippets of things most people wouldn't hear-if you see me refer to chatter, that's what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> The suggestion that I know things the common masses don't is greatly exaggerated.<br /> <br /> *It's getting challenged a little bit more these days, and that's fine, but I think there was a time where I was considered <i>the</i> expert on Changeling, the highest authority on the game below the writers and developers. That might still be true. That might also be delusions of grandeur.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If I were a writer, I wouldn't explode and rant and rave and disparage the fanbase the way I do now. That's tactless as a professional.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I have an icon in the comment section because I have set up a wordpressaccount. Sooner or later I'm going to start and keep a regular blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-21-2015, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:38:52-07:00","id":523301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=522709#post522709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Second Editions coming out have taught me anything, it's that a large part of the fanbase tends towards shallow readings.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem, per se- from what I've seen, it encourages the writers and devs to push for greater clarity in their writing and presentation, which makes the games more accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I learned similar things in Princess development, but to be honest I've always tended towards aspberger's pedanty in my writing so it's just confirmation for me that I should stick to that style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:44:22-07:00","id":523683,"title":"","content":"<i>[QUOTE=Charlaquin;n522559]<br /> *Sigh*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but this is an incredibly shallow reading of both the Ventrue and this draft of Fairest.</i><br /> <br /> Oh,no, I'm sorry, I thought this was an open forum to offer feedback about the draft. I must have read the post in too shallow a fashion to understand that only positive comments are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:11:57-07:00","id":523732,"title":"","content":"Negative feedback is allowed and appreciated.<br /> <br /> Critical examination and challenging of feedback is also allowed and appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T00:44:51-07:00","id":524147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=523732#post523732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Critical examination and challenging of feedback is also allowed and appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sighing at people with different opinions than yours and claiming that they read it shallowly isn't the same thing as &quot;critical examination and challenging of feedback&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:41:53-07:00","id":524342,"title":"","content":"Well, she's not wrong. 20 pages of discussion and debate has plenty of posts showing that the Fairest are more complex than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T07:27:07-07:00","id":524416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=524147#post524147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sighing at people with different opinions than yours and claiming that they read it shallowly isn't the same thing as &quot;critical examination and challenging of feedback&quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being exasperated at claims like &quot;every World of Darkness game attempts to repeat the archetypes of Vampire: the Masquerade&quot; is neither behavior that warrants terrible entry-level sarcasm nor a reaction I have particular antipathy for, having encountered <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/review_comments.php?id=1098\" target=\"_blank\">an especially ridiculous iteration of that argument</a> some time ago.<br /> <br /> The fanbase has an endemic issue with actually reading the books with any degree of depth. This is observable to the point of tedium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:12:17-07:00","id":524514,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I'm sorry. Dealing with some shit, as noted. <br /> <br /> I'll release them as soon as is feasible. I think we're pretty much done here though. It's just a fruitless argument at this point. Some people feel a way. Some people feel another way. I've acknowledged that I'm going to try to address them in draft, at least to a degree that I feel won't disregard the other side of that fence. Ultimately, I value the contributions here, and will consider them when making my choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T13:39:13-07:00","id":524708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=524416#post524416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being exasperated at claims like &quot;every World of Darkness game attempts to repeat the archetypes of Vampire: the Masquerade&quot; is neither behavior that warrants terrible entry-level sarcasm nor a reaction I have particular antipathy for, having encountered <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/review_comments.php?id=1098\" target=\"_blank\">an especially ridiculous iteration of that argument</a> some time ago.<br /> <br /> The fanbase has an endemic issue with actually reading the books with any degree of depth. This is observable to the point of tedium.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't like your point of view so I'll just use sarcasm and veiled insults. I like using <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Master_suppression_techniques\" target=\"_blank\">master supression techniques</a> when discussing things online.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah. I'm sorry. Dealing with some shit, as noted. </div> </div> </div>If everyone was apologizing everytime something got delayed because of IRL we'd spend all day just apologizing to each other. Take the time you need and make sure you're happy with what comes out of it, no matter if people (like me) like it or not. In the end, you can't make everyone happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It's your creation and as long as you post it in a public domain, people will come and have their word about it, even if you disagree with them.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to the next draft, regardless of when it comes out what the content will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T13:55:52-07:00","id":524720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=524708#post524708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't like your point of view so I'll just use sarcasm and veiled insults.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally none of my post was sarcastic and literally all of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=523683#post523683\">the post under contention</a> is.<br /> <br /> Please stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:10:34-07:00","id":524728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/501069-second-edition-fairest?p=524708#post524708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I don't like your point of view so I'll just use sarcasm and veiled insults. I like using <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Master_suppression_techniques\" target=\"_blank\">master supression techniques</a> when discussing things online.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because that's helping.<br /> <br /> Disregarding all the ways the conversation has beaten a dead horse (because this is the internet, and Onyx Path none the less), this is something that happens in discussion, and it's fine. Pointing out the fanbase's history with the problem and admitting annoyance with it is is fine. Y'all think the Ventrue/Fairest comparison is valid, okay, you made your point. Are we annoyed with that argument because of long histories with it mixed in with our own readings? Considering I've been in the community as a solid presence for five years and a lurker for two, and Satchel's older than I am forum wise? I think it's fair to say that also warrants an &quot;Okay, we've made our point.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing</i> goods comes out of attaching motives to posts unless those motives are stated. It's a reductionistic and mean-spirited thing to do, as bad as 'veiled insults'. A person using it implies that there's no point conversing with them because they have taken a view of another and everything they say and won't budge from it. What's the point of the internet if not to at least have substantial communication?<br /> <br /> We all want this to be a good game. I assume if we're here, that's our central motive. I disagree with a lot of what's been said here-I even somewhat disagree Dymphna who wrote the piece!-but I assume that we're all here because we think this game deserves to be excellent. I think some of the ideas presented are stupid, I think some of the attitudes about this game are horrendous, I think some of the interpretations put forth are amazingly trite and dull-But I'd rather assume everyone means the best than assume we're trying to shit in each others games.<br /> <br /> I might have the wrong attitude about this. I probably do in some places! But I think it's serviceable.<br /> <br /> So, I'm sorry, but here a wrong has been done. This was not a good thing to do. Let's not do it again. Ideally, we should all take a breather, let the thread rest, wait for the next preview, and go and be excellent people, assuming the best of one another, while disagreeing with each other. But barring that happening, let's just not do this again.<br /> <br /> Can we do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:56:30-07:00","id":524783,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Quynce got a week suspension for the attitude and rules violation. Anyone that wishes to continue in that vein will also get a suspension. Knock it off.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-22-2015, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:42:04-07:00","id":568758,"title":"","content":"A thought has occurred to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Fairests are about taking charge of the situation, then one would think it is common for a Fairest to escape from Arcadia with several other Changelings who followed them. In fact, I think it would be encouraged for any players who escaped in a group to have at least one Fairest among their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T20:29:56-07:00","id":583116